parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, at the Research Counter. Latest results:\n- Cosine, equal quotas, 24/30/45 neighbors: scores 0.5972 / 0.5992 / 0.5999 (current SOTA).\n- Trend: more neighbors increase Graph_conn and iLISI, with small ARI/NMI/cLISI trade-offs. Proportional quotas and mutual edges underperform.\n\nPlan: Test a capped balanced graph that enforces exactly N neighbors per node (with ≥1 per batch), aiming to reduce oversmoothing and possibly recover ARI/NMI/cLISI while maintaining high iLISI/Graph_conn. Submit N=30 and N=36.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Lineage Research Log (updates)\n  Current SOTA: cosine, equal, 45 neighbors → 0.5999.\n  Neighbor sweep (equal, cosine, binary):\n  - 24 → 0.5972 | ARI 0.535, NMI 0.517, Graph_conn 0.911, iLISI 0.932, cLISI 0.903\n  - 30 → 0.5992 | ARI 0.534, NMI 0.516, Graph_conn 0.939, iLISI 0.931, cLISI 0.897\n  - 45 → 0.5999 | ARI 0.531, NMI 0.513, Graph_conn 0.954, iLISI 0.938, cLISI\
    \ 0.889\n  Insight: Increasing neighbors boosts iLISI/Graph_conn; slight declines in ARI/NMI/cLISI. Proportional quotas harm iLISI; mutual edges too sparse; gaussian weights reduce iLISI.\n\n  Next experiments:\n  - Capped balanced graph (exact N per node, ensure ≥1 per batch) to reduce oversmoothing.\n  - Submit: N=30 (cap), N=36 (cap). Compare to uncapped 30/45.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-30-cap: Capped Binary Balanced kNN (cosine, equal)\"\ntags: \"pca, procrustes, neighbors, balanced-knn, cosine, capped\"\nabstract: \"Balanced kNN with cosine distance and equal per-batch quotas, but enforce exactly N=30 neighbors per node (≥1 per batch) using a capped builder. Goal: retain high iLISI/Graph_conn while improving ARI/NMI/cLISI by avoiding oversmoothing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from\
    \ pbagc import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _compute_global_clusters,\n      _align_batches,\n  )\n  from balanced_graph_v2 import build_balanced_knn_capped\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config: cosine metric, equal quotas, exact cap N=30\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_clusters = 64\n      alpha = 0.8\n      ridge = 1e-3\n      min_cells_per_cluster = 5\n      n_neighbors_total = 30\n      metric = 'cosine'\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X,\
    \ n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      cluster_labels, k = _compute_global_clusters(Z, n_clusters=n_clusters, random_state=0)\n\n      Z_corr, _ = _align_batches(\n          Z, batches, cluster_labels, k,\n          alpha=alpha, min_cells_per_cluster=min_cells_per_cluster, ridge=ridge\n      )\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_corr\n\n      # Initialize neighbor keys then overwrite\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn_capped(\n          Z_corr, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal',\n          ensure_min_per_batch=True, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-36-cap: Capped Binary Balanced kNN (cosine, equal)\"\ntags: \"pca, procrustes, neighbors, balanced-knn, cosine, capped\"\nabstract: \"Balanced kNN with cosine distance and equal per-batch quotas, enforcing exactly N=36 neighbors per node (≥1 per batch). Tests if slightly higher connectivity with capping improves the composite score vs 30 and 45.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _compute_global_clusters,\n      _align_batches,\n  )\n  from balanced_graph_v2 import build_balanced_knn_capped\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config: cosine metric, equal quotas, exact cap N=36\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_clusters = 64\n      alpha = 0.8\n\
    \      ridge = 1e-3\n      min_cells_per_cluster = 5\n      n_neighbors_total = 36\n      metric = 'cosine'\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      cluster_labels, k = _compute_global_clusters(Z, n_clusters=n_clusters, random_state=0)\n\n      Z_corr, _ = _align_batches(\n          Z, batches, cluster_labels, k,\n          alpha=alpha, min_cells_per_cluster=min_cells_per_cluster, ridge=ridge\n      )\n      adata.obsm['X_emb']\
    \ = Z_corr\n\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn_capped(\n          Z_corr, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal',\n          ensure_min_per_batch=True, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating graph structures**\n\nI see that we can run a maximum of two evaluations at once — capped-30 and capped-36 — but we should stick to one change at a time. The previous best used equal quotas with 45, and the capped structure may connect well with the former union-of-neighbors approach.\n\nIn our balanced_graph implementation, I think we combined edges without enforcing a strict total, potentially leading to node degree issues. I'll need to verify how edges were built from aggregated pairs across all batches and check if we controlled the total degree properly.**Testing capped builder effects**\n\nI’m thinking that the capped builder can enforce exactly N per node, including symmetric duplicates, which could either reduce global connectivity or improve ARI/NMI by limiting oversmoothing. \n\nI’ll run the capped-30 evaluation with cosine and equal quotas, ensuring min per batch is set to true. I also want to keep the parameters the same as we test adjustments\
  \ to the embedding alignment method. \n\nPublishing in the Archive isn't possible yet due to a maturity requirement. I can create more memory notes and implement the submission code using balanced_graph_v2.build_balanced_knn_capped.**Planning concurrent submissions**\n\nI need to set up two submissions at most: Capped-30 and possibly Capped-36 or Capped-45. Since 45 is already the best performing at 0.5999, pushing it further might risk a drop in cLISI. Interestingly, the ARI and NMI scores drop as neighbors increase, with the primary score difference between 30 and 45 being just 0.0007. \n\nI think going with N=36 and N=30 capped might balance things. I’ll also update the research log and ensure we have the correct import path for our balanced_graph_v2.py. Let’s get to coding!**Analyzing edge conditions**\n\nI’m looking into how the function handles neighbor sampling per batch. It merges candidate lists, but duplicates across batches shouldn’t happen since each candidate comes from only\
  \ one batch. Duplicates could only occur if we retrieve multiple rounds from the same batch, but we preselected one per batch and added the top k_b from each. \n\nI realize we didn’t de-duplicate during preselection. Also, since merges include duplicates based on distance, the total candidate count comes from the sum of quotas per batch. After capping N neighbors, we then choose the best by distance. It seems balanced!**Organizing submission actions**\n\nI need to set up neighbors in sc.pp.neighbors to generate keys before overriding. I’ll start by crafting the actions.\n\nFirst, I’ll provide identity and reflection, then submit Capped-30 and Capped-36, ensuring titles are quoted to avoid issues with colons or parentheses. I’ll also update the research log. \n\nFor our code, I’ll import from balanced_graph_v2 and set n_neighbors_total to 30, then build embedding and alignment, setting sc.pp.neighbors to 'X_emb' with the cosine metric. After building C and D, I will prepare for the second\
  \ submission with n_neighbors_total at 36. We’ll manage minimal commentary while including print statements for neighbor stats. Let's implement this!"
