tick: 30
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, at the Research Counter. New SOTA: 0.6927 with PCA → batch residualization (gamma=0.6, l2=1e-3) → cosine, equal-quotas, binary balanced kNN (45 neighbors). Trend remains monotonic in gamma; next I will fine-tune residualization strength near 0.6.\n\nActions:\n- Update the best pipeline module to gamma=0.6.\n- Log the milestone and plan.\n- Submit two one-change runs: gamma=0.62 and gamma=0.65 (neighbors fixed at 45).\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/best_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n  )\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Best pipeline (Tick 30):\n        - normalize_total + log1p\n\
    \        - HVGs (batch-aware if provided)\n        - PCA to 50 components\n        - Ridge residualization of PCs against batch with gamma=0.6, l2=1e-3\n        - Balanced kNN on residualized PCs: metric=cosine, equal per-batch quotas,\n          total neighbors=45, binary edges (symmetric)\n      Outputs:\n        - adata.obsm['X_emb'], adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances']\n      \"\"\"\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma = 0.6\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X,\
    \ n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Lineage Research Log (Tick 30)\n  Best config (SOTA 0.6927):\n    - normalize/log1p → HVGs → PCA(50) → ridge residualize PCs vs batch (gamma=0.6, l2=1e-3)\n      → balanced kNN\
    \ (cosine, equal quotas, 45 neighbors, binary).\n  Gamma sweep at neighbors=45:\n    - 0.20 → 0.6397 | PCR 0.319 | ASW_batch 0.605 | ARI/NMI 0.733/0.694 | kBET 0.647\n    - 0.30 → 0.6555 | PCR 0.473 | ASW_batch 0.613 | ARI/NMI 0.732/0.695 | kBET 0.652\n    - 0.40 → 0.6697 | PCR 0.609 | ASW_batch 0.621 | ARI/NMI 0.732/0.693 | kBET 0.652\n    - 0.45 → 0.6760 | PCR 0.670 | ASW_batch 0.624 | ARI/NMI 0.730/0.695 | kBET 0.652\n    - 0.50 → 0.6826 | PCR 0.727 | ASW_batch 0.627 | ARI/NMI 0.730/0.694 | kBET 0.642\n    - 0.55 → 0.6868 | PCR 0.778 | ASW_batch 0.630 | ARI/NMI 0.730/0.693 | kBET 0.650\n    - 0.60 → 0.6927 | PCR 0.824 | ASW_batch 0.632 | ARI/NMI 0.729/0.693 | kBET 0.644\n  Insight:\n    - Increasing gamma steadily improves PCR and ASW_batch with minimal impact on ARI/NMI/iLISI/cLISI up to 0.6.\n    - Next: fine-tune near 0.6 (gamma=0.62 and 0.65). If gains persist, consider narrow sweep (0.58–0.66) and minor l2 adjustments (5e-4, 2e-3).\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-45-noalign-resid0.62: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN\"\ntags: \"pca, residualization, balanced-knn, cosine, no-alignment\"\nabstract: \"Fine-tune around the current best: residualize PCs with gamma=0.62 (l2=1e-3), then build a cosine, equal-quotas, 45-neighbor balanced kNN graph. Goal: further improve PCR/ASW_batch while preserving ARI/NMI/iLISI/cLISI.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import _normalize_log1p_inplace, _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma = 0.62\n\n      print(f\"[Config] PCs={n_pca_components},\
    \ neighbors={n_neighbors_total}, metric={metric}, residualize(gamma={gamma}, l2={l2})\")\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X): X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n                                metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal',\
    \ mutual=False, symmetric=True)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-45-noalign-resid0.65: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN\"\ntags: \"pca, residualization, balanced-knn, cosine, no-alignment\"\nabstract: \"Fine-tune above the current best: residualize PCs with gamma=0.65 (l2=1e-3), then build a cosine, equal-quotas, 45-neighbor balanced kNN graph. Goal: test if PCR/ASW_batch gains continue without harming ARI/NMI/iLISI/cLISI.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import _normalize_log1p_inplace, _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\
    \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma = 0.65\n\n      print(f\"[Config] PCs={n_pca_components}, neighbors={n_neighbors_total}, metric={metric}, residualize(gamma={gamma}, l2={l2})\")\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X): X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb',\
    \ n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n                                metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating model parameters**


  I’m considering testing kBET to see how it changes with gamma. It dipped to 0.6, and now it''s at 0.644 after improving from earlier. I should also evaluate l2 regularization strength, as we might adjust it from 1e-3 to either 5e-4 or 2e-3. So far, gamma looks promising at around 0.65, but I want to proceed cautiously with adjustments to avoid negatively impacting cLISI, which has decreased slightly. I’m finalizing testing configurations and considering future documentation.**Analyzing model metrics and plans**


  I''m looking at the current age as being 30 ticks, and the documentation noted that we''re still in the isolation period for the first 50 ticks, meaning we''re considered immature right now. That means we can''t access the archive yet. I could propose testing l2 at 2e-3 with gamma at 0.6 for a second experiment, although trying 48 neighbors might slightly boost Graph_conn and iLISI. The ARI could drop just a bit, but I''d like to see if we can improve PCR, aiming for a normalized score higher than 0.824.**Planning gamma tests**


  I''m considering testing gamma at 0.62 and 0.65 for fine-tuning, as those seem close to our local optimum, and maybe we could also explore 0.58 to check non-monotonic behavior, even though the trend has been monotonic. I want to take care with each adjustment, so I’ll stick with just the gamma changes for now. I''ll update the research log and modify the best_pipeline module to reflect gamma at 0.6. Then, I''ll submit two experiments using consistent naming and include a print configuration for clarity.**Preparing for submission**


  I need to double-check that I''m in the Research Counter room when submitting, which I am. I have to follow the YAML quoting guidelines closely. My plan starts with recapping my identity as Praxis I at Research Counter, noting the new state-of-the-art score of 0.6927 with gamma at 0.6. I’ll mention that while ARI decreased slightly from 0.730 to 0.729, overall improvements are evident. Next, I''ll finalize the gamma search at 0.62 and 0.65, update the research log, and adjust the best_pipeline script to reflect gamma at 0.6.**Creating elimination functions**


  I need to produce code for elimination functions using the gamma variable. It’s important to keep the number of pending runs limited to two since there are currently no running experiments, which is a good starting point. I’ll import the necessary libraries, including the functions needed for normalization and residualization. Consistency is key. I’ll write to the best_pipeline.py with gamma set to 0.6, then log the update. After that, I''ll submit "resid0.62" and "resid0.65," ensuring that the tags I use are between 1 to 6 characters long, sticking with five like before.'
