tick: 33
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, at the Research Counter. New SOTA: 0.6962 with PCA → batch residualization (gamma=0.65, l2=1e-3) → cosine, equal-quotas, binary balanced kNN (45 neighbors). Two fine-tunes are running: gamma=0.68 (45-NN) and gamma=0.65 with 48-NN.\n\nReflection:\n- Residualizing PCs against batch synergizes strongly with balanced kNN. Increasing gamma steadily improves PCR and ASW_batch with minimal impact on ARI/NMI/iLISI/cLISI. Slight kBET dips at higher gamma are outweighed by overall score gains.\n- While runs execute, I’ll persist the current best pipeline and update the research log.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/best_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n  )\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\
    \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Best pipeline (Tick 32):\n        - normalize_total + log1p\n        - HVGs (batch-aware if provided)\n        - PCA to 50 components\n        - Ridge residualization of PCs against batch with gamma=0.65, l2=1e-3\n        - Balanced kNN on residualized PCs: metric=cosine, equal per-batch quotas,\n          total neighbors=45, binary edges (symmetric)\n      Outputs:\n        - adata.obsm['X_emb'], adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances']\n      \"\"\"\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma = 0.65\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask\
    \ = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Research Log\
    \ (Tick 32)\n  SOTA: 0.6962 with PCA(50) → residualize PCs vs batch (gamma=0.65, l2=1e-3) → balanced kNN (cosine, equal per-batch quotas, 45 neighbors, binary).\n  Gamma sweep at 45-NN: 0.2→0.6397, 0.3→0.6555, 0.4→0.6697, 0.45→0.6760, 0.5→0.6826, 0.55→0.6868, 0.6→0.6927, 0.62→0.6945, 0.65→0.6962.\n  Insight: Increasing gamma steadily improves PCR and ASW_batch with minimal trade-offs; ARI/NMI/iLISI/cLISI remain strong; kBET dips slightly at high gamma but average score rises.\n\n  Pending:\n  - gamma=0.68 (45-NN)\n  - gamma=0.65, neighbors=48\n\n  Next (contingent on results):\n  - If gamma=0.68 > 0.65: fine-tune around 0.66–0.70 and optionally adjust l2 ∈ {5e-4, 2e-3}.\n  - If 48-NN > 45-NN at gamma=0.65: probe neighbors ∈ {42, 48, 54} under best gamma.\n  - Otherwise, keep gamma=0.65, 45-NN as best and prepare a detailed write-up for Archive once mature.\n```"
