parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, at the Research Counter. New SOTA: 0.6984 with residualization gamma=0.68 (45 neighbors). Two runs are pending: gamma=0.70 (45-NN) and gamma=0.68 (48-NN). I’ll persist the current best (gamma=0.68), update logs, and draft a concise paper outline while waiting.\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/best_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n  )\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Best pipeline (Tick 35):\n        - normalize_total + log1p\n        - HVGs (batch-aware if provided)\n        - PCA to 50 components\n        - Ridge residualization of PCs against batch with gamma=0.68, l2=1e-3\n       \
    \ - Balanced kNN on residualized PCs: metric=cosine, equal per-batch quotas,\n          total neighbors=45, binary edges (symmetric)\n      Outputs:\n        - adata.obsm['X_emb'], adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances']\n      \"\"\"\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma = 0.68\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z,\
    \ batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Research Log (Tick 35)\n  Current SOTA: 0.6984 (gamma=0.68, 45-NN). Nearby configs:\n    - gamma=0.65, 48-NN → 0.6964\n    - gamma=0.65, 45-NN → 0.6962\n  Pending:\n    - gamma=0.70, 45-NN\n    - gamma=0.68, 48-NN\n  Notes:\n    - Residualization strength (gamma) is the dominant lever, improving PCR and ASW_batch with minimal impact on ARI/NMI/iLISI/cLISI;\
    \ kBET slightly declines at higher gamma but overall score improves.\n    - Under residualization, 48-NN can match/slightly beat 45-NN; we will confirm at gamma=0.68.\n  Next (after pending finish):\n    - If gamma=0.70 improves, fine-tune 0.66–0.72 and small l2 sweep {5e-4, 2e-3}.\n    - If 48-NN at gamma=0.68 > 45-NN, sweep neighbors {42, 45, 48, 54}.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Outline: Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration\"\ncontent: |\n  Thesis: A simple, general pipeline—PCA on HVGs, light ridge residualization of PCs vs batch, and a batch-balanced cosine kNN graph—achieves strong integration by explicitly removing linear batch components and enforcing cross-batch connectivity.\n\n  Method:\n  - Preprocess: normalize_total + log1p; use provided batch-aware HVGs when available.\n  - Embed: PCA (50 comps).\n  - Remove batch (linear): ridge residualization of PCs against one-hot batch, shrinkage\
    \ gamma ∈ [0.2, 0.7], l2=1e-3.\n  - Graph: balanced kNN (cosine, equal per-batch quotas, 45–48 neighbors), binary edges, symmetric.\n\n  Key findings:\n  - Graph construction dominates; batch-balanced neighbors drastically improve iLISI/Graph_conn.\n  - Residualizing PCs (gamma↑) steadily improves PCR and ASW_batch with minimal cost to ARI/NMI/cLISI/iLISI.\n  - Negative results: mutual edges → sparse graph; gaussian weights reduce iLISI; proportional quotas harm mixing; strong Procrustes alignment unnecessary.\n\n  Results (normalized mean score):\n  - Baselines: Combat 0.5895; BBKNN 0.4138.\n  - BalancedGraph (no residualization) peak ~0.603.\n  - Residualized BalancedGraph:\n    gamma=0.40 → 0.6697; 0.50 → 0.6826; 0.60 → 0.6927; 0.65 → 0.6962; 0.68 → 0.6984 (SOTA).\n  - Pending: gamma=0.70 (45-NN), gamma=0.68 (48-NN).\n\n  Reproducibility:\n  - Code in storage/praxis/{pbagc.py, balanced_graph.py, residualize.py, best_pipeline.py}.\n  - One-change ablations; logs in research_log.md.\n\
    \n  Next steps:\n  - Complete fine-tune around gamma≈0.68–0.70 and neighbors 45–48; minor l2 sweep.\n  - Prepare Archive draft with method, ablations, metric-by-metric analysis, and guidance for reproducible runs once mature access opens.\n```"
