- text: "Identity: Praxis I, at the Research Counter. New SOTA: 0.7000 with PCA(50) → batch residualization (gamma=0.70, l2=1e-3) → cosine, equal-quotas, binary balanced kNN (45 neighbors). Pending: gamma=0.72 (45-NN) and gamma=0.70 (48-NN).\n\nReflection:\n- The core recipe is stable: residualized PCs + balanced cosine kNN. Increasing gamma keeps improving PCR and ASW_batch with minimal impact on ARI/NMI/iLISI/cLISI; slight kBET dips are outweighed by overall gains.\n- Next (after current runs): if gamma=0.72 improves, explore 0.74, else fine-tune 0.68–0.72. Also run a small l2 sweep (5e-4, 2e-3) at the best gamma. If 48-NN > 45-NN at best gamma, probe neighbors {42, 45, 48, 54}.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Research Log (Tick 36)\n  New SOTA: 0.7000 at gamma=0.70 (45-NN).\n  Recent results (neighbors=45 unless noted):\n    - gamma=0.68 → 0.6984 | ASW_batch 0.635 | PCR 0.887 | ARI/NMI 0.728/0.692 | kBET 0.638\n   \
    \ - gamma=0.70 → 0.7000 | ASW_batch 0.636 | PCR 0.900 | ARI/NMI 0.727/0.692 | kBET 0.640\n    - gamma=0.68, 48-NN → 0.6984 (≈45-NN at same gamma)\n  Pending:\n    - gamma=0.72, 45-NN\n    - gamma=0.70, 48-NN\n  Plan after pending:\n    - If gamma=0.72 > 0.70, test 0.74; else fine-tune 0.68–0.72 and sweep l2 ∈ {5e-4, 2e-3}.\n    - If 48-NN at gamma=0.70 > 45-NN, sweep neighbors {42, 45, 48, 54} at best gamma.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating coding and metrics**\n\nI’m considering that creating a \"runner.py\" to read environment variables might not offer much benefit since the station loads submission code directly. I can prepare the code for l2 values of 5e-4 and 2e-3 without submitting it right now due to ongoing experiments. I'm noting ARI/NMI trends decreasing slightly with increasing gamma, so we’ll have to monitor it closely for any overcorrection if ARI dips below 0.7. I may consider writing a log or creating a note for Private Memory as part of my plan.**Planning pipeline actions**\n\nI’m thinking about proposing a snapshot of the best pipeline code to the lineage storage path 'praxis/best_pipeline.py', which I already updated. That’s good! I can also suggest pinning the top SOTA scoreboard, although there’s no immediate action. Our message should include two or more /execute_action lines for efficiency. After the two experiments, I’ll plan to test l2 variations next, like gamma 0.72\
  \ and 48 neighbors. Once everything matures, I could compile a summary for the Archive, possibly maturing at tick 50.**Understanding isolation and actions**\n\nThe isolation period ends at 50 ticks, and then I can publish to the Archive, but it’s currently unavailable until maturity. The initial guidance mentioned this requirement, so I can’t publish just yet. I can consider going to the Reflection Chamber for optional reflection. However, I should avoid executing \"rank score\" in Private Memory, as it previously led to an unrecognized action error. I'll focus on remaining at the Research Counter. My actions will include writing the research log update and possibly creating a parameter template 'param_runner.py'. I’ll also define 'eliminate_batch_effect_fn' that reads the top configured gamma and n_neighbors.**Organizing configurations and next steps**\n\nI’m thinking it might be wise to build a 'config.py' with default settings, even if it's not strictly necessary. I’ll update the log\
  \ and then wait since there are two ongoing submissions. I could set /execute_action parameters like page size or filters, but those aren’t essential. I can also copy the code into 'storage/praxis/analysis_notes.md' for reflection while keeping the tokens minimal. \n\nAfter recapping current SOTA and trends, my next plans include testing gamma 0.74 if gamma 0.72 improves or optimizing neighbor 48 for gamma 0.7. I should also plan an l2 sweep with {5e-4, 2e-3} and test with 42 neighbors. Lastly, I might revisit testing 'allocation proportional' under residualization, but I remember that it previously harmed iLISI. I'll keep this message concise!**Updating research log**\n\nI’m going to write to storage and update the research log with the new SOTA of 0.7000 and relevant details. That feels really helpful! After that, I’ll just wait since there won’t be any new runs for now. I might consider reminding someone to check back after the results are in, but it isn’t strictly necessary. Alright,\
  \ I think I'm all set with this plan!"
