tick: 38
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, at the Research Counter. New SOTA: 0.7005 at gamma=0.72 (45 neighbors). Neighbor 48 at gamma=0.70 ≈ 45; core gains come from increasing residualization gamma. Next: push gamma further and test mild ridge change.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/best_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n  )\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Best pipeline (Tick 38):\n        - normalize_total + log1p\n        - HVGs (batch-aware if provided)\n        - PCA to 50 components\n        - Ridge residualization of PCs against batch with gamma=0.72, l2=1e-3\n        - Balanced kNN on residualized PCs: metric=cosine,\
    \ equal per-batch quotas,\n          total neighbors=45, binary edges (symmetric)\n      Outputs:\n        - adata.obsm['X_emb'], adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances']\n      \"\"\"\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma = 0.72\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma,\
    \ center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Research Log (Tick 38)\n  Best results (neighbors=45 unless noted):\n    - gamma=0.68 → 0.6984 | ASW_batch 0.635 | PCR 0.887 | ARI/NMI 0.728/0.692 | kBET 0.638\n    - gamma=0.70 → 0.7000 | ASW_batch 0.636 | PCR 0.900 | ARI/NMI 0.727/0.692 | kBET 0.640\n    - gamma=0.72 → 0.7005 (SOTA) | ASW_batch 0.636 | PCR 0.913 | ARI/NMI 0.724/0.692 | kBET 0.636\n    - gamma=0.70, 48-NN\
    \ → 0.7000 (≈45-NN)\n  Insight: Increasing gamma steadily improves PCR and ASW_batch with minimal impact on ARI/NMI/iLISI/cLISI; small kBET dips are outweighed by overall gains. Neighbor 48 can match 45 but isn’t consistently better.\n  Next ablations:\n    - gamma=0.74 at 45-NN (extend monotonic gamma).\n    - gamma=0.72 at 45-NN with l2=2e-3 (mild ridge tweak).\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-45-noalign-resid0.74: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN\"\ntags: \"pca, residualization, balanced-knn, cosine, no-alignment\"\nabstract: \"Increase residualization to gamma=0.74 (l2=1e-3) on PCA, then build a cosine, equal-quotas, 45-neighbor balanced kNN graph. Goal: continue PCR/ASW_batch gains while preserving ARI/NMI/iLISI/cLISI.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import _normalize_log1p_inplace,\
    \ _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma = 0.74\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X): X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb',\
    \ n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-45-noalign-resid0.72-l2_0.002: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN\"\ntags: \"pca, residualization, ridge, balanced-knn, cosine, no-alignment\"\nabstract: \"Hold gamma=0.72 (near-best) and increase ridge to l2=2e-3 in the batch residualization step to test stability and potential ASW_batch/PCR/kBET trade-offs, keeping the 45-neighbor balanced cosine kNN graph.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import\
    \ anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import _normalize_log1p_inplace, _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 2e-3\n      gamma = 0.72\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X): X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma,\
    \ center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating proposed models**\n\nI’m looking at possible model runs, wanting to include actions and performance reflection. I’m considering two setups: gamma=0.74 with 45-NN and gamma=0.72 with 48-NN. \n\nI might also explore an l2 sweep with gamma=0.72 at two values, but I'm limited to two slots. The trend shows increasing gamma could bring improvement, and I think gamma=0.74 might be a good choice along with a l2 adjustment. I'll also update the research log to reflect these insights.**Updating best pipeline and actions**\n\nI need to set the best pipeline to gamma=0.72, since it appears to be the best now. It was previously updated to gamma=0.70, but I’ll change it to 0.72. I'll make sure to write this change into the storage file for best_pipeline.\n\nThen, I’ll update the research log to summarize the new findings and plans. I’ll submit run configurations for both gamma=0.74 with 45NN and gamma=0.72 with l2 set at 0.002. Using this level should help balance the regularization\
  \ without underfitting. Let's get this done!**Ensuring proper YAML formatting**\n\nI need to make sure the title \"PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN\" is correctly quoted in YAML, especially with the colon. I've seen it done before, so I know it’s allowed. \n\nReflecting on my analysis: scores improved with increasing gamma, but using 48 neighbors didn’t show further benefits at gamma=0.68 or 0.70. At 0.70, 48 was equivalent to 45, indicating that neighbor count isn’t highly sensitive. \n\nFor actions, I’ll write the best_pipeline with gamma=0.72, update the research log, and submit the runs with appropriate l2 settings. I need to be mindful of concurrency limits and ensure proper formatting when I write the code."
