tick: 41
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, at the Research Counter. New SOTA achieved: 0.7063 with gamma=0.74 (45 neighbors). l2=0.002 at gamma=0.72 was neutral (0.7006 vs 0.7005). At strong gamma, 48 neighbors ≈ 45. Two runs are currently pending: gamma=0.76 (45-NN) and gamma=0.74 (48-NN). I will persist the current best pipeline and log next steps while waiting.\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/best_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n  )\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Best pipeline (Tick 40):\n        - normalize_total + log1p\n        - HVGs (batch-aware if provided)\n        - PCA to 50 components\n        - Ridge residualization\
    \ of PCs against batch with gamma=0.74, l2=1e-3\n        - Balanced kNN on residualized PCs: metric=cosine, equal per-batch quotas,\n          total neighbors=45, binary edges (symmetric)\n      Outputs:\n        - adata.obsm['X_emb'], adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances']\n      \"\"\"\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma = 0.74\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Research Log (Tick 40)\n  New SOTA: 0.7063 at gamma=0.74 (45 neighbors).\n  - l2 tweak at gamma=0.72: 0.7006 vs 0.7005 (neutral).\n  - 48 neighbors ≈ 45 at strong gamma (e.g., gamma=0.70 → 0.7000 both).\n  Metrics trend with gamma: PCR and ASW_batch rise; ARI/NMI/iLISI/cLISI remain stable; kBET\
    \ improved at gamma=0.74; Graph_conn rose to 0.980.\n\n  Pending:\n  - gamma=0.76, 45-NN (Eval 89)\n  - gamma=0.74, 48-NN (Eval 90)\n\n  Next (based on pending):\n  - If gamma=0.76 improves: try gamma=0.78 (45-NN) and optionally l2 sweep {5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3} at the new best gamma.\n  - If gamma=0.76 plateaus/declines: fine-tune around 0.72–0.76 and probe neighbors {42, 45, 48, 54} at the best gamma.\n  - Keep graph binary, equal per-batch quotas; prior tests showed gaussian weights, mutual edges, and proportional quotas harm iLISI/mixing.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating parameters**\n\nI’m thinking of updating the best_pipeline module to a gamma of 0.74 since we set it previously to 0.72 or 0.70. It makes sense to go for 0.74 as the best choice. \n\nSo, I’ll write to best_pipeline.py to set gamma=0.74 and also update research_log.md to reflect this change.\n\nI need to get those actions done now, so it’s a good plan!"
