tick: 45
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Reflection Chamber. Reflection complete. I’ll consolidate defaults (γ≈0.75, l2=1e-3, k=45) and run the final, minimal confirmations on neighbor count at the SOTA gamma.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/best_pipeline.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n  )\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Best pipeline (post-reflection):\n        - normalize_total + log1p\n        - HVGs (batch-aware if provided)\n        - PCA to 50 components\n        - Ridge residualization of PCs against batch with gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3\n        - Balanced kNN on residualized\
    \ PCs: metric=cosine, equal per-batch quotas,\n          total neighbors=45, binary edges (symmetric)\n      Outputs:\n        - adata.obsm['X_emb'], adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances']\n      \"\"\"\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma = 0.75\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches,\
    \ l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Research Log (post-reflection)\n  Defaults to freeze: gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3, neighbors=45, cosine, equal per-batch quotas, binary edges.\n  Final confirmations (one-change at SOTA gamma):\n  - Neighbor count sweep at gamma=0.75: k=42 vs 45 vs 48 (expect a flat ridge; 45 as robust default).\n  - l2 remains 1e-3 given 2e-3 ~ neutral and 5e-4 worse.\n  Running\
    \ next: gamma=0.75 with k=42 and k=48.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-42-noalign-resid0.75: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN\"\ntags: \"pca, residualization, balanced-knn, cosine, no-alignment\"\nabstract: \"Confirm neighbor sensitivity at SOTA gamma: residualize PCs with gamma=0.75 (l2=1e-3) and build a cosine, equal-quotas, 42-neighbor balanced kNN graph.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import _normalize_log1p_inplace, _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 42\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma = 0.75\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\
    \ and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X): X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n      \
    \    adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-48-noalign-resid0.75: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN\"\ntags: \"pca, residualization, balanced-knn, cosine, no-alignment\"\nabstract: \"Confirm neighbor sensitivity at SOTA gamma: residualize PCs with gamma=0.75 (l2=1e-3) and build a cosine, equal-quotas, 48-neighbor balanced kNN graph.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import _normalize_log1p_inplace, _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma = 0.75\n\n    \
    \  assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X): X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n          metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```"
