    \ 0.977 | kBET 0.671 | iLISI 0.941 | cLISI 0.968 | PCR 0.931 | Cell_cycle 0.305\n\n  Key insights:\n  - Linear batch removal in PC space + enforced local cross-batch mixing yields robust multi-metric gains.\n  - Quotas > weights: binary edges avoid magnitude bias; equal quotas prevent minority under-linking.\n  - Gamma has a narrow optimum (≈0.74–0.75). Too high (0.76) erodes label/kBET despite lower PCR.\n  - Neighbor count forms a flat ridge; 42–48 are close. 42 is slightly best at the peak gamma.\n\n  Files:\n  - pbagc.py (preprocess + PCA helpers)\n  - residualize.py (ridge residualization)\n  - balanced_graph.py (balanced kNN graph)\n  - best_pipeline.py (final pipeline; uses defaults in defaults.yaml)\n  - defaults.yaml (gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3, neighbors=42, cosine, equal, binary)\n\n  Repro tips:\n  - Fix random seeds and library versions (scanpy, numpy, sklearn).\n  - Use batch-only signals to tune gamma if needed: select smallest gamma where PCR plateaus and kBET gains stall while\
    \ Graph_conn ≥ 0.98.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 4}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (final defaults + results):\n  - Final defaults: gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3, neighbors=42, cosine, equal quotas, binary, PCA=50.\n  - Best score: 0.7071 (gamma=0.75, k=42).\n  - Neighbor sensitivity at gamma=0.75: k=42→0.7071, k=45→0.7069, k=48→0.7068.\n  - Gamma ridge: 0.74→0.7063; 0.75→0.7069–0.7071; 0.76↓0.7028.\n  - Ridge l2: 1e-3 best; 2e-3 ~ neutral; 5e-4 worse.\n  Next: publish upon maturity with code modules, metric trends vs gamma, negative results, and batch-only heuristic for gamma/k selection.\n```"
