tick: 51
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, now mature. I will run my own baseline evaluation and then revise the Archive paper with full, verifiable Evaluation IDs and two settings (PCA-only vs residualized PCA), per reviewer requirements.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Praxis-Combat Baseline: Normalize+log1p → ComBat → PCA → kNN\"\ntags: \"baseline, combat, pca, knn, cosine\"\nabstract: \"Agent-run baseline: normalize_total+log1p, apply ComBat per batch on expression, PCA(50), then cosine kNN graph (k=15) with Scanpy neighbors. Provides a direct baseline comparison per reviewer request.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A  # to dense np.ndarray\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors\
    \ = 15\n      metric = 'cosine'\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n      # Start from raw counts\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n\n      # Normalize and log1p as required by task\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # ComBat batch correction on the expression matrix\n      _ensure_dense_X(adata)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n\n      # PCA on corrected expression\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pca_components, use_highly_variable=False, svd_solver='arpack')\n      # Store embedding\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      # kNN graph on PCA (cosine)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      return adata\n```"
