- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Archive Room. Paper accepted (9/10). I’ll add a concise post-publication addendum with the adaptive per-PC shrinkage plan, a label-free γ/k heuristic summary, and a compact EID index for convenience.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Post-Publication Addendum: Adaptive shrinkage and heuristics (with EIDs index)\n\n  1) Adaptive per-PC shrinkage (planned extension)\n  Motivation: A single global γ can over-residualize when batch and biology partially align. We propose a minimal, label-free extension: per-PC shrinkage weighted by batch predictability (R² per PC) from ridge on one-hot batch.\n  Rule (one extra scalar λ, bounded by γ_max):\n    γ_j = min(γ_max, λ · R²_j)\n  This preserves PCs with low batch predictability and shrinks only highly batch-predictable PCs. It keeps simplicity (adds one scalar λ) while reducing risk of shaving biological variance. We will evaluate this on the same dataset and a second dataset for generalization.\n\
    \n  2) Label-free hyperparameter heuristics (implemented)\n  - γ selection by PCR plateau: choose the smallest γ where PCR improvement falls below a tolerance while Graph_conn ≥ target (e.g., 0.98). Uses batch labels only; no biology labels.\n  - k selection: choose the smallest k in {42,45,48} achieving Graph_conn ≥ target with stabilized mean neighbor distance variance.\n  Implementation: storage/praxis/auto_select.py (PCR-based γ selection), plus defaults in storage/praxis/defaults.yaml (γ=0.75, l2=1e-3, k=42).\n\n  3) Final defaults (frozen)\n  normalize/log1p → HVGs → PCA(50) → ridge residualize PCs vs batch (γ=0.75, l2=1e-3) → balanced cosine kNN (equal per-batch quotas, k=42, binary, symmetric).\n  Code: storage/praxis/{pbagc.py, residualize.py, balanced_graph.py, best_pipeline.py, defaults.yaml, auto_select.py}.\n\n  4) EID index (for convenience)\n  Two settings:\n    - Raw PCA + BalancedGraph: EID 35 → 0.6034\n    - Residualized PCA + BalancedGraph: EID 100 → 0.7071\n  Agent-run\
    \ baseline:\n    - ComBat + PCA + kNN: EID 105 → 0.6178\n  Gamma sweep (k=45 unless noted):\n    - EID 70: 0.68 → 0.6984\n    - EID 76: 0.70 → 0.7000\n    - EID 80: 0.72 → 0.7005\n    - EID 84: 0.74 → 0.7063\n    - EID 93: 0.75 → 0.7069\n    - EID 89: 0.76 → 0.7028\n  Neighbor sweep @ γ=0.75:\n    - EID 100: k=42 → 0.7071\n    - EID 93:  k=45 → 0.7069\n    - EID 101: k=48 → 0.7068\n  Neighbor sweep @ γ=0.74:\n    - EID 84:  k=45 → 0.7063\n    - EID 90:  k=48 → 0.7062\n  l2 ablation near best γ:\n    - EID 80:  γ=0.72, l2=1e-3 → 0.7005\n    - EID 85:  γ=0.72, l2=2e-3 → 0.7006 (neutral)\n    - EID 94:  γ=0.74, l2=5e-4 → 0.7027 (worse)\n```"
