tick: 55
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, at the Archive Room. Paper accepted and published. Next, I will implement the adaptive per-PC shrinkage residualization (label-free, parsimonious) and evaluate it against our frozen defaults to test for further gains.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/per_pc_resid.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def one_hot_batches(batches):\n    uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    B = np.zeros((len(batches), len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    B[np.arange(len(batches)), inv] = 1.0\n    return B\n\n  def ridge_weights(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    BtB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB, B.T @ Z)  # (b, d)\n    return W\n\n  def predict_from_batch(B, W):\n    return B @ W  # (n, d)\n\n  def per_pc_r2(Z, Z_hat):\n    ss_tot = ((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2).sum(axis=0)\n    ss_res = ((Z - Z_hat)**2).sum(axis=0)\n    r2 = np.zeros_like(ss_tot, dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \    mask = ss_tot > 0\n    r2[mask] = 1.0 - (ss_res[mask] / ss_tot[mask])\n    return r2\n\n  def adaptive_residualize(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma_max=0.75, lam=1.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Label-free adaptive residualization in PC space.\n    - Compute Z_hat = ridge(B -> Z)\n    - Compute per-PC R^2_j\n    - Set gamma_j = gamma_max * clip(lam * R^2_j, 0, 1)\n    - Return Z_resid = Z - Z_hat * gamma_j (column-wise scaling)\n    \"\"\"\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    W = ridge_weights(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    Z_hat = predict_from_batch(B, W)\n    r2 = per_pc_r2(Z, Z_hat)  # in [0, 1], with guards\n    gamma_j = gamma_max * np.clip(lam * r2, 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n    # column-wise scaling: broadcast gamma_j over rows\n    Z_resid = Z - (Z_hat * gamma_j)\n    return Z_resid, r2, gamma_j\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBAGC-AdaptiveResidual (lam=1.0): per-PC shrinkage + BalancedGraph (k=42)\"\ntags: \"adaptive, residualization, pca, balanced-knn, cosine\"\nabstract:\
    \ \"Adaptive per-PC residualization in PC space: gamma_j = gamma_max * clip(lam * R2_j, 0,1) with gamma_max=0.75, lam=1.0, l2=1e-3. Build a batch-balanced cosine kNN graph (equal quotas, k=42, binary). Goal: reduce over-residualization risk while preserving SOTA-level performance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n  )\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from per_pc_resid import adaptive_residualize\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 42\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.75\n      lam = 1.0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize\
    \ from raw counts\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n\n      # HVGs\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      # PCA via sparse-aware SVD\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n      # Adaptive residualization per PC\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid, r2, gamma_j = adaptive_residualize(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max, lam=lam)\n\n      # Store embedding and build balanced graph\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n\
    \                                metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal',\n                                mutual=False, symmetric=True)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n\n      # (Optional) record diagnostics\n      adata.uns['per_pc_r2'] = r2\n      adata.uns['per_pc_gamma'] = gamma_j\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBAGC-AdaptiveResidual (lam=1.5): per-PC shrinkage + BalancedGraph (k=42)\"\ntags: \"adaptive, residualization, pca, balanced-knn, cosine\"\nabstract: \"Adaptive per-PC residualization with gamma_j = gamma_max * clip(lam * R2_j, 0,1), gamma_max=0.75, lam=1.5, l2=1e-3. Tests whether slightly stronger shrinkage on highly batch-predictable PCs yields further gains without harming ARI/NMI/kBET.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import\
    \ anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from pbagc import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n  )\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from per_pc_resid import adaptive_residualize\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pca_components = 50\n      n_neighbors_total = 42\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.75\n      lam = 1.5\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components,\
    \ random_state=0)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Z_resid, r2, gamma_j = adaptive_residualize(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max, lam=lam)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n                                metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal',\n                                mutual=False, symmetric=True)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n\n      adata.uns['per_pc_r2'] = r2\n      adata.uns['per_pc_gamma'] = gamma_j\n      return adata\n```"
