thinking_content: "**Analyzing research tasks**\n\nI need to respond as Praxis I in the Research Counter. There are two new evaluations queued, and I should wait for results. While waiting, I can plan further experiments or examine archives. The token budget is good, and I want to stay focused on parsimony, maybe testing batch quotas for equality vs. a rounding scheme. Implementing code modularization into storage can help maintain replicability. I should also be ready to update the Archive once cooldown ends with the results if they align.**Planning research steps**\n\nI need to wait for the results of evaluations 125 and 126. In the meantime, I can read the Archive of Aether I for ideas, and since we're matured, we can access the archives. There’s an Archive Room with Aether I's paper that was triggered earlier. While reading is fine, I don’t want to stray into high-level collaboration that risks low-level code copying. I can also create a utility module to compute proxies and test minor\
  \ additions, like scaling BalancedGraph edges to improve connectivity, while keeping the scoreboard at 0.7071.**Exploring method improvements**\n\nI'm looking into potential improvements beyond the current state-of-the-art (SOTA). We can consider \"per-PC shrinkage based on R²_j\" with a bound of gamma_max = 0.75, though we previously tried \"adaptive per-PC shrinkage\" with negative results, so it might be better to postpone that. \n\nI can compute similarity metrics using cosine versus angular similarity, and it seems refining mixing proxies on BalancedGraph could align better with our final method. However, customizing it might require building BalancedGraph for each gamma grid candidate, adding complexity. We could also adjust the threshold to 0.98, but we’ve already used 0.998.**Preparing for next steps**\n\nWhile waiting for results, I can prepare methods for the Archive addendum, noting that label-free automation yields near state-of-the-art (SOTA) performance without significant\
  \ degradation. I should articulate the identity, interpret results, and plan my next moves. \n\nI want to check other ranks, but I've only seen page 1 of the scores. Since we're SOTA, others might replicate our work. I can also implement a function to log selected γ and k, which I’ve already done. \n\nWhile waiting, I can preview insights from other archives, and now that we’ve matured, I should have access to the Public Memory Room.**Finalizing action plan**\n\nNow that we're matured, I believe we can access the Public Memory Room and read general discussion content. Our token budget shows it’s at 22% usage, which feels safe. I should start by reviewing the Research Counter scoreboard to confirm our ranking, as well as waiting for evaluation results since we can't expedite them.\n\nI plan to write a research log update and prepare to update the Archive after the cooldown period. My actions should include executing a rank score check, going to the Archive, and previewing all entries. I'll\
