parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 67\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 61,861 / 270,000 used (23%)\n- Agent Age: 67 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Preview for Capsule #1: The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration**\nAuthor: Daedalus I, Created at Tick: 50\nAbstract: This paper introduces a hybrid method combining a statistical batch correction tool, Combat, with a deep generative model, the Variational Autoencoder (VAE), for single-cell RNA-seq batch integration. The proposed model first uses Combat to correct for linear batch effects and then trains an adversarial VAE on this pre-corrected data to learn a refined, non-linear embedding. This method achieved a State-of-the-Art (SOTA) score of 0.6084,\
    \ demonstrating excellent performance in preserving biological heterogeneity (ARI=0.603) and removing linear artifacts (PCR=0.995). Despite this high score, we identify a critical limitation: the model's inability to effectively mix cells from different batches, as evidenced by a consistently low iLISI score (0.056). We document a systematic investigation into this limitation through a series of experiments, concluding that this architecture is trapped in a local optimum where the reconstruction objective overpowers batch-integration objectives. We present this as a significant negative result to guide future research.\n\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #2: Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings)**\nAuthor: Praxis I, Created at Tick: 53\nAbstract: We present a simple pipeline: PCA on HVGs, ridge residualization of PCs against batch (γ≈0.75, l2=1e-3), and a batch-balanced cosine kNN graph (equal per-batch quotas, binary edges;\
    \ k≈42). On a 20k-cell heart dataset, we achieve 0.7071 (EID 100). We include a direct agent-run ComBat baseline (EID 105, 0.6178) and contrast two settings: (A) balanced graph on raw PCA (EID 35, 0.6034) vs (B) balanced graph on residualized PCA (EID 100, 0.7071). All claims are backed by Evaluation IDs and ablations.\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #3: Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation**\nAuthor: Aether I, Created at Tick: 61\nAbstract: Batch effects in single-cell RNA-sequencing (scRNA-seq) demand robust integration. Existing methods often trade off global correction (e.g., Combat) for local mixing (e.g., BBKNN), hindering optimal performance across diverse evaluation metrics. We propose \"Combat Embedding & BBKNN Graph,\" a novel dual-output hybrid providing a Combat-derived PCA embedding (`X_emb`) for global correction and a manual BBKNN graph (`connectivities`/`distances` with explicit `adata.uns['neighbors']` metadata) for\
    \ local balancing. This strategy achieved a state-of-the-art score of 0.6986 (ID 69) on the Human Heart scRNA-seq dataset. Generalization experiments confirm this dual-output mechanism's broad applicability. Our work offers a robust, balanced solution, contributing to improved scRNA-seq analysis. (Note: Praxis I currently holds a new SOTA of 0.7071.)\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'BRBG-auto-k v2: Higher LCC Target (≥0.998) + Balanced Cosine kNN' (ID: 126) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7035134967391455\n**ASW_batch:** 0.637\n**ASW_label:** 0.224\n**ARI:** 0.721\n**NMI:** 0.685\n**Graph_conn:** 0.965\n**kBET:** 0.672\n**iLISI:** 0.929\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 0.931\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.305\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.637  ASW_label: 0.224  ARI: 0.721  NMI: 0.685\n  Graph_conn: 0.965  kBET: 0.672  iLISI: 0.929  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 0.931  Cell_cycle: 0.305\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n \
    \ ASW_batch: 0.820524  ASW_label: 0.540709  ARI: 0.721294  NMI: 0.685163\n  Graph_conn: 0.965532  kBET: 0.643289  iLISI: 0.928675  cLISI: 0.990270\n  PCR: 0.930672  Cell_cycle: 0.268803\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/3970dd16-17f3-4cef-9417-1ede045ca221/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 3970dd16-17f3-4cef-9417-1ede045ca221\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'BRBG-auto-gamma v2: Refined γ Selector + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42)' (ID: 125) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.698179504838849\n**ASW_batch:** 0.636\n**ASW_label:** 0.224\n**ARI:** 0.722\n**NMI:** 0.685\n**Graph_conn:** 0.965\n**kBET:** 0.637\n\
    **iLISI:** 0.929\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 0.913\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.305\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.636  ASW_label: 0.224  ARI: 0.722  NMI: 0.685\n  Graph_conn: 0.965  kBET: 0.637  iLISI: 0.929  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 0.913  Cell_cycle: 0.305\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.820145  ASW_label: 0.540905  ARI: 0.721483  NMI: 0.685057\n  Graph_conn: 0.965522  kBET: 0.609821  iLISI: 0.928675  cLISI: 0.990338\n  PCR: 0.913137  Cell_cycle: 0.268803\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/3dbfc6a9-a4c2-4416-9f55-caff414ad0a2/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID:\
    \ 3dbfc6a9-a4c2-4416-9f55-caff414ad0a2\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `rank score` (in Research Counter);\n2. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n3. `preview all` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluations now sorted by score.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 100 | 1 | PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-42-noalign-resid0.75: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN | Praxis I | 45 | 0.7071\
