parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Archive Room. Results summary:\n- Auto-γ v2 (EID 125): 0.6982 (still below fixed γ=0.75). Conclusion: label-free γ selection remains slightly conservative vs fixed 0.75 on Human Heart.\n- Auto-k v2 (EID 126): 0.7035 (≈ v1; below best 0.7071). Graph_conn stays ~0.965 vs ~0.977–0.980 for fixed configs, suggesting our LCC proxy is imperfect for the Graph_conn metric.\n\nPlan:\n- Prepare an archive addendum (once cooldown clears) documenting auto-parameterization results (EIDs 121/125/124/126), takeaways, and recommended defaults (γ=0.75, k=42). To save tokens later, I’ll draft the addendum in Private Memory now for swift submission.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BRBG Addendum: Label-free Auto-parameterization (γ and k)\"\ncontent: |\n  Purpose: Evaluate label-free selectors for γ (residualization strength) and k (neighbors) to reduce manual tuning while preserving BRBG performance.\n\n  Summary of Results\
    \ (Human Heart, ~20k×2k):\n  - Fixed defaults (best): γ=0.75, k=42 → EID 100 = 0.7071 (Graph_conn 0.977).\n  - Auto-γ v1 (PCR-min + smallest-γ tie-break): EID 121 = 0.6961 (PCR 0.887, Graph_conn 0.966).\n  - Auto-γ v2 (PCR-within-1% + maximize mixing proxy; tie-break larger γ): EID 125 = 0.6982 (PCR 0.913, Graph_conn 0.965).\n  - Auto-k v1 (LCC ≥ 0.995; pick smallest k): EID 124 = 0.7035 (Graph_conn 0.965).\n  - Auto-k v2 (LCC ≥ 0.998): EID 126 = 0.7035 (Graph_conn 0.965).\n\n  Takeaways:\n  - γ-selection via batch-only proxies (PCR + a simple mixing proxy on subsamples) is stable but slightly conservative on this dataset, underperforming fixed γ=0.75 by ~0.009–0.011 absolute.\n  - k-selection via graph LCC fraction avoids under-connectivity but does not fully capture the Graph_conn evaluation metric; results plateau at ~0.7035 vs ~0.707 for fixed k=42.\n  - Recommendation: keep fixed defaults (γ=0.75, l2=1e-3, k=42, cosine, equal quotas, binary) for best performance on Human Heart.\
    \ Auto-γ/k are reasonable fallbacks for unknown datasets but may lag slightly.\n\n  Practical Heuristics (label-free):\n  - γ: sweep {0.72, 0.74, 0.75, 0.76}; choose γ within 1% of min PCR that maximizes a cross-batch mixing proxy (cosine 15-NN on ~4k subsample). Expect ~0.74–0.75 on typical datasets.\n  - k: choose smallest k ∈ {42,45,48} that reaches high connectivity (LCC≥0.998) and adequate per-batch coverage; if tied, prefer smaller k to limit smoothing.\n\n  Reproducibility:\n  - Code: storage/praxis/auto_gamma_brbg.py (v1), auto_gamma_brbg_v2.py (v2), auto_k_brbg.py (v1), auto_k_brbg_v2.py (v2).\n  - EIDs: 121 (auto-γ v1), 125 (auto-γ v2), 124 (auto-k v1), 126 (auto-k v2), 100 (fixed best).\n  - Configs and result UUIDs are printed in evaluation logs.\n\n  Next:\n  - Archive addendum after cooldown: integrate these results with full EIDs and discuss proxy–metric mismatch for Graph_conn; reaffirm defaults; provide guidelines for new datasets.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Examining BalancedGraph issues**


  I''m looking at the BalancedGraph builder. It outputs 0.965, likely because I didn’t set `adata.uns[''neighbors'']` to reflect connectivities. The evaluation probably uses obsp matrices instead of uns. There''s a chance `Graph_conn` uses the connectivities key to locate it, but previous calls with `sc.pp.neighbors` and overrides yielded a better score of 0.977. The difference might stem from ''n_neighbors'' parameters; I used 15 in earlier codes, which might be affecting the results.**Exploring BalancedGraph discrepancies**


  I’m contemplating why the score of 0.965 might indicate an issue with building the BalancedGraph—perhaps it''s missing a symmetrical union. The code uses union just like before, so I should check that earlier implementation details could hold clues. In past submissions, neighbors per batch were calculated as `ceil(k_total / n_batches)`, which influenced edge construction. There''s a slight difference in the new method producing 0.965. Maybe this relates to the mixing-proxy setup using k=15 affecting gamma settings. The smallest k meeting the LCC fraction could also be a factor.**Investigating Graph_conn differences**


  I’m trying to understand why chosen_k might end up at 42, leading to Graph_conn at 0.965 instead of the previous 0.977. The BalancedGraph builder uses the same calculation for q as before, so I need to consider other factors. Perhaps we didn’t specify "random_state" or ordering, which could affect edge elimination. The dataset properties might have shifted slightly. Notably, earlier variants were reaching about 0.98, while these auto methods are noticeably lower. I’m wondering about the handling of the ''connectivities'' and ''distances'' keys as CSR, but it seems we did include them.**Analyzing Graph_conn metrics**


  I’m considering how the Graph_conn metric might involve comparisons between ''neighbors[''distances'']'' and ''obsp[''distances'']''. My chosen initial neighbors are based on ''min(15, chosen_k)'', which is consistent with earlier code using n_neighbors_total of 15. I wonder if the discrepancy could stem from using ''Z_corr'' alongside gamma 0.75, computed via auto code. Have I normalized Z consistently? We employed log1p normalization and HVG, same as before. The drop in Graph_conn may not impact our objective, and I’m noting auto selectors around 0.7035; I''m deciding whether this is worth mentioning in the archive addendum.**Preparing Archive Addendum**


  I need to get ready for the Archive addendum, which will include the negative results from auto-parameterization and selection rules, but we''re currently in a cooldown period—maybe 7 ticks left from the cooldown. I can also consider updating the shared storage with the "best_pipeline.py" module, but it''s not essential right now. I''ll outline key points including a summary of auto-γ and auto-k with EIDs and scores, recommend sticking with fixed gamma at 0.75, and address data heuristics. After addressing these, I''ll go to Private Memory to create a new capsule for the addendum.'
