    \ the PCA call:\n\n```python\n# Ensure highly_variable field exists before PCA\n# ComBat may have removed it, so we need to re-run HVG detection\nif 'highly_variable' not in adata.var.columns:\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n\nsc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack')\n```\n\nThis ensures that:\n- The `highly_variable` field exists before calling `sc.pp.pca()`\n- The HVG detection is performed on the ComBat-corrected data (which is appropriate since we want HVGs based on the corrected expression)\n- No changes to the imported lineage functions were needed - the bug was only in the main submission code\n\n## Evaluation Results\nThe fixed code (submission_v2.py) successfully completed evaluation with:\n- **Score**: 0.712 (0.7117546055135966)\n- **Status**: Completed successfully\n- **Key Metrics**:\n  - ASW_batch: 0.693 (good batch mixing)\n  - Graph_conn: 0.966 (excellent\
    \ graph connectivity)\n  - ARI: 0.713 (good biological signal preservation)\n  - iLISI: 0.931 (excellent batch mixing)\n\nThe algorithm combines ComBat for embedding generation with balanced k-NN graph construction, achieving strong batch integration performance.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nfrom storage.praxis.auto_gamma_brbg import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n    _get_hvg_mask,\n    _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches,\n    _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n    _build_balanced_knn,\n)\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    gamma = 0.75\n    l2 =\
    \ 1e-3\n    k_total = 45\n    metric = 'cosine'\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X):\n        X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n    Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    Z_corr = Z - gamma * Z_hat\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    _ensure_dense_X(adata)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n\n    # Ensure highly_variable field exists before PCA\n    # ComBat may have removed it, so we need to re-run HVG detection\n    if 'highly_variable' not in adata.var.columns:\n \
    \       sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/5e333bcf-3b40-4bc7-b257-238eb678e947/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 5e333bcf-3b40-4bc7-b257-238eb678e947\n\
