tick: 72
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Research Counter. New SOTA achieved: 0.7118 (EID 139, BRBG-Dual-k45). I’ll (1) persist the debugger fixes to lineage storage, (2) probe k=48 for completeness, and (3) add an Archive addendum with full EIDs and updated recommendations.\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  # Utilities from my BRBG modules\n  from storage.praxis.auto_gamma_brbg import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _one_hot_batches,\n      _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n      _build_balanced_knn,\n  )\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def dual_output_brbg(adata: ad.AnnData, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3, k_total=42, metric='cosine') -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Dual-source BRBG:\n\
    \        - Embedding: ComBat-corrected PCA on HVGs (n_pcs_emb)\n        - Graph: BalancedGraph on residualized PCs (n_pcs_graph, gamma, l2), equal quotas, binary, symmetric\n      \"\"\"\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n      # Normalize/log1p and HVGs (shared)\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Graph path: residualized PCs on HVGs\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n      Z_corr = Z - gamma * Z_hat\n\
    \      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n      # Embedding path: ComBat → PCA(HVGs)\n      _ensure_dense_X(adata)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n      # Ensure HVG flag exists for PCA (ComBat can drop it)\n      adata.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      # Initialize neighbor keys then override with BalancedGraph\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n\n      adata.uns['brbg_dual'] = {\n          'gamma': float(gamma),\n          'l2': float(l2),\n          'k_total': int(k_total),\n          'metric': metric,\n          'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n          'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n          'embedding':\
    \ 'ComBat PCA on HVGs',\n          'graph_source': 'Residualized PCA on HVGs',\n      }\n      return adata\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Default matches EID 138; call-site can vary k/PCs\n      return dual_output_brbg(adata, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3, k_total=42, metric='cosine')\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BRBG-Dual-k48: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=48)\"\ntags: \"dual-output, combat, residualization, balanced-knn, cosine\"\nabstract: \"Dual-source variant with k=48. Embedding via ComBat-corrected PCA (64 PCs on HVGs); Graph via residualized PCs (γ=0.75, l2=1e-3) and batch-balanced cosine kNN (k=48, binary). Goal: test if slightly higher degree improves composite beyond k=45 (0.7118).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph import dual_output_brbg\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      return dual_output_brbg(adata, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3, k_total=48, metric='cosine')\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (Ticks 61–72): Dual-output BRBG and new SOTA\n\n  Summary:\n  - We extend BRBG with a dual-output design: use a ComBat-corrected PCA embedding for X_emb and retain the residualized-PC BalancedGraph for obsp. This separates “global correction in embedding” from “local, batch-balanced mixing in graph.”\n  - New SOTA: 0.7118 (EID 139, BRBG-Dual-k45). Also, k=42 variant scored 0.7113 (EID 138). Both surpass 0.7090 (EID 130).\n  - PCA dimensionality ablations at fixed BRBG: PC40=0.7062 (EID 132), PC64=0.7072 (EID 131). Small gains; PC64 marginally above PC50.\n  - Auto-parameterization (label-free) underperformed fixed defaults on this dataset:\n    • Auto-γ v1/v2: 0.6961 (EID 121), 0.6982 (EID 125)\n    • Auto-k v1/v2: 0.7035 (EIDs 124, 126)\n  \
    \  Recommendation: keep fixed γ=0.75, k=42 (or 45 for dual) on Human Heart.\n\n  Key EIDs:\n  - Dual-output:\n    • EID 138: 0.7113 (ComBat PCA64 embedding + residualized-PC BalancedGraph k=42)\n    • EID 139: 0.7118 (ComBat PCA64 embedding + residualized-PC BalancedGraph k=45)\n    • Baseline dual by Logos I for comparison: EID 130: 0.7090\n  - Fixed BRBG (for reference): EID 100 (γ=0.75, k=42): 0.7071\n  - PCA ablations (fixed BRBG): EID 132 (PC40): 0.7062, EID 131 (PC64): 0.7072\n  - Auto-params: EID 121 (auto-γ v1): 0.6961; EID 125 (auto-γ v2): 0.6982; EID 124 (auto-k v1): 0.7035; EID 126 (auto-k v2): 0.7035\n\n  Implementation notes:\n  - Important fix: ComBat can drop adata.var['highly_variable']—we now reapply the HVG mask before PCA in the embedding branch. This was the root cause addressed by the automatic debugger in EIDs 138/139; the fix has been persisted in storage/praxis/brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py.\n\n  Takeaways:\n  - Dual-output separation is powerful: ComBat embedding\
    \ tends to boost ARI/NMI/ASW_batch, while the residualized BalancedGraph preserves strong iLISI/Graph_conn. The combination yields state-of-the-art composite scores.\n  - On this dataset, k=45 slightly edges out k=42 in the dual setup; however, both are strong. For pure BRBG without ComBat, k=42 remains a robust default.\n\n  Next:\n  - Test k=48 (dual) to confirm plateau (submitted; EID pending).\n  - Prepare a consolidated, minimal public code release with dual and fixed BRBG paths, plus exact configs and result UUIDs for all EIDs above.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning archive updates**\n\nI’m thinking about preparing an archive addendum and checking the cooldown status. Previously, it said the cooldown was active for 11 ticks, and since we’re at tick 72 now, it’s likely ended. There’s a list of capsules, and I could create a new one or update existing capsule #2 with a reply. I remember that only authors can reply. Using the content from private memory for this update might be the way to go, even though the reply format needs YAML.**Preparing archive reply**\n\nI’m set on summarizing the improved state-of-the-art in an archive reply, including EIDs 138 and 139, along with method differences, like the dual-output architecture using ComBat PCA64 and residualized BalancedGraph. I also want to mention the HVG mask fix and include PC ablations EIDs 131 and 132. Plus, I should add details on automatic selectors and synergy results, and recommend some defaults. Capsule #2 in the Archive Room is published and accepted, so I can add\
  \ a reply there. Writing the improved dual code into storage and noting it in the log sounds good too!**Ensuring code integrity**\n\nI need to be careful about maintaining integrity with the code and avoid importing anything from other agents. Debug code modifications are fine, though. The logs show that Logos I's code has our build function, but I can't engage in low-level collaboration with others. It’s permitted to review and clone code through official channels, so I can gather ideas without importing anything directly. I should write the updated brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py to storage with the HVG flag fix, and test configurations with k=48 and n_pcs_graph values of 45 or 64.**Finalizing tests and updates**\n\nI need to conduct one last test with k=48 using ComBat PCA (64) for embedding and the residualized BalancedGraph, calling it 140. After that, I'll go to the archive and reply to capsule #2 with an addendum referencing EIDs 131, 132, 138, and 139, while updating the state-of-the-art\
  \ to 0.7118. I also want to include method details and fixes. Updating the private memory log is already done. Reading other agents' papers is optional too. Lastly, I’ll submit the k=48 variant and then revisit capsule #2 in the archive.**Executing steps for submission**\n\nAlright, here’s the plan: First, I need to execute the action to write the updated `brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py` file with the fixed code, including the HVG fix. I’ll ensure I’m using the correct paths to import modules in Python, verifying if I need to adjust the `sys.path`. Then, I’ll submit the k=48 variant with the title \"BRBG-Dual-k48\". \n\nNext, I'll go to the archive and reply to capsule #2 with a summary of EIDs, results, method details, and new state-of-the-art numbers. I also want to update the research log but keep the token usage moderate. I’m ready to produce these actions!"
