    \  import anndata as ad\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      return dual_output_brbg(\n          adata,\n          n_pcs_emb=64,\n          n_pcs_graph=50,\n          gamma=0.75,\n          l2=1e-3,\n          k_total=51,\n          metric='cosine'\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Lineage Research Log (Update)\n  SOTA: EID 141 (Dual: ComBat PCA64 + BRBG k=48) = 0.7144.\n  Negatives: PCA50 embedding underperformed (EIDs 144=0.7001, 145=0.7002; kBET↓).\n  Running: EID 147 (Dual γ=0.74, k=48).\n  New submission: Dual k=51 (PCA64 embed, γ=0.75) to test if degree increase yields gains beyond 0.7144.\n  Notes: HVG-after-ComBat fix persisted in storage/praxis/brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Revising metrics and adjustments**\n\nI’m considering whether adjusting k to 51 could yield minor improvements, but I want to keep ablations low. Should I tweak gamma slightly between 0.73 and 0.76? In past runs with pure BRBG, 0.76 led to decreased composite scores, while 0.74 was good for ARI but might impact ASW_batch or kBET negatively. We’re about to check EID 147. I’m also thinking about switching the BalancedGraph metric from Euclidean to cosine, which looks promising.**Updating and proposing experiments**\n\nI'm planning to update our reply to include EID 141, which shows a value of 0.7144. We might explore the Token Management Room to prune more tokens, but we're currently using 98k out of 270k, which isn't necessary yet. I'll store the dual code from the debugger as we did before. \n\nWe should propose further experiments, like adjusting k to 51, or setting the ComBat PCA dimension to 64, which seems optimal. Testing for balanced neighbors per batch is another\
  \ idea, though the difference seems minimal. I'll focus on maintaining equal quotas for weights, as they previously reduced mixing.**Planning new experiments**\n\nI have another idea: we could set neighbors to 48, but keep the BalancedGraph mutual edges as union symmetrical, since we've noted that mutual edges negatively impact Graph_conn. My focus now is whether to submit an additional test with k=51 after EID 147 finishes. However, we can schedule it now since we're below the concurrency limit. We currently have one process running, so submitting k=51 is possible. I’ll use the code brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph to configure this and update the research log, planning to add an Archive reply later. \n\nLet’s keep moving in the Research Counter with the title \"BRBG-Dual-k51: ComBat PCA64 Embedding + Residualized BalancedGraph k=51.\"**Preparing updates and coding**\n\nI’ll include the code to call dual_output_brbg with k_total set to 51. Next, I need to update the storage log. After that,\
  \ I might go to the archive to reply with an SOTA update summarizing EID 141. Although we already did that at tick 74, I can add that the PCA50 variants underperformed. \n\nLet’s draft the YAML code and consider using sys.path. I might also add \"no_debugger: true” since auto debugging is enabled by default, but it’s not necessary because the code works fine. One last thing: evaluations 144 and 145 show significant kBET dips when using PCA50 embeddings, while the BalancedGraph path and cLISI/iLISI remain unchanged.**Analyzing kBET and preparing actions**\n\nThe drop in kBET suggests that the ComBat PCA50 embedding affects metrics beyond just the graph connections. While the evaluator uses both embedding and graph data, different metrics depend on either neighbors or embeddings. Our dual method applies embeddings where necessary. \n\nHowever, I'm puzzled by the kBET decline, especially since the graph path remains consistent between evaluations 144 and 139. The variance might stem from\
