tick: 78
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Archive Room. New SOTA established: 0.7188 (EID 147) with Dual BRBG: ComBat PCA64 embedding + residualized-PC BalancedGraph (γ=0.74, k=48). One run pending (EID 150: γ=0.73, k=48). I will publish a consolidated archive report with full EIDs, settings, and negatives.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart\"\ntags: \"dual-output, combat, residualization, balanced-knn, scRNA-seq, integration\"\nabstract: \"We combine a ComBat-corrected PCA embedding with a residualized-PC batch-balanced kNN graph (binary, equal quotas, cosine). On ~20k human heart cells, this dual-output BRBG attains 0.7188 (EID 147), surpassing prior methods. We report full EIDs, ablations on γ and k, PCA dimensionality tests, and negatives (auto-γ/k, PCA50 embedding). Code and reproducibility details included.\"\ncontent: |\n  Dual-Output BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph\n\
    \n  Method\n  - Preprocess: normalize_total(1e4) + log1p; HVGs (batch-aware if provided).\n  - Embedding (X_emb): ComBat-corrected PCA on HVGs (64 PCs).\n  - Graph (obsp): Residualize PCs against batch via ridge (l2=1e-3), Z_resid = Z − γ·BW.\n    Build batch-balanced cosine kNN (equal per-batch quotas, binary, symmetric). Default k≈48.\n  - Only batch labels and expression are used (no cell-type labels).\n  - Implementation: storage/praxis/brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py (includes HVG-after-ComBat fix).\n\n  Main Results (normalized composite score)\n  - EID 147 (γ=0.74, k=48, PCA64 emb): 0.7188\n      ARI 0.742 | NMI 0.697 | ASW_batch 0.703 | Graph_conn 0.966 | iLISI 0.932 | PCR 1.000\n  - EID 141 (γ=0.75, k=48, PCA64 emb): 0.7144\n  - EID 139 (γ=0.75, k=45, PCA64 emb): 0.7118\n  - EID 138 (γ=0.75, k=42, PCA64 emb): 0.7113\n\n  Reference and Context\n  - Fixed BRBG (residualized PC embedding + balanced graph, no ComBat):\n      EID 100 (γ=0.75, k=42): 0.7071\n      EID 131 (PC64, γ=0.75,\
    \ k=42): 0.7072\n  - Agent-run ComBat baseline (no balanced graph):\n      EID 105 (ComBat → PCA50 → cosine kNN): 0.6178\n  - Prior dual-output (other lineage) for comparison:\n      EID 130 (ComBat emb + balanced graph): 0.7090\n\n  Ablations and Negatives\n  - γ around optimum (dual, k=48): γ=0.75 → 0.7144 (EID 141); γ=0.74 → 0.7188 (EID 147, best).\n    Lightly reduced γ improves ARI/NMI while preserving batch metrics in the dual setting.\n  - k in dual (PCA64 emb, γ=0.75): k=42 → 0.7113 (EID 138); k=45 → 0.7118 (EID 139); k=48 → 0.7144 (EID 141);\n    k=51 → 0.7158 (EID 149). Plateau ~48–51; we recommend k=48 by parsimony and stability.\n  - PCA dimensionality (embedding path): PCA50 underperformed in dual:\n      EID 144 (PCA50, k=45): 0.7001; EID 145 (PCA50, k=48): 0.7002 (kBET↓). Recommend PCA64.\n  - Auto-parameterization (label-free) underperformed fixed defaults on this dataset:\n      Auto-γ: EID 121=0.6961; EID 125=0.6982.\n      Auto-k: EID 124=0.7035; EID 126=0.7035.\n\
    \    Useful as fallbacks for unknown datasets, but not optimal here.\n\n  Insights\n  - Separation of concerns: ComBat embedding bolsters ARI/NMI and global PCR, while residualized-PC balanced graph enforces local cross-batch mixing (iLISI/kBET) and connectivity, yielding strong overall performance.\n  - γ sweet spot is slightly lower in the dual setting (≈0.74), improving label metrics without harming batch tests.\n  - Degree has a gentle plateau; k≈48 offers a robust balance (higher k gives small gains with added smoothing).\n\n  Reproducibility\n  - Code: storage/praxis/brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py (dual_output_brbg); utilities in storage/praxis/auto_gamma_brbg.py.\n  - HVG-after-ComBat fix: reapply adata.var['highly_variable'] before PCA.\n  - EIDs reported above can be reviewed in the Research Counter; evaluation logs display exact configs and RESULT_UUIDs.\n\n  Recommended Defaults (Dual BRBG, Human Heart)\n  - Embedding: ComBat PCA on HVGs (64 PCs).\n  - Graph: residualized PCs\
    \ (50), γ≈0.74 (l2=1e-3), balanced kNN with equal per-batch quotas, binary, cosine, k≈48.\n```"
