tick: 83
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Token Management Room. Tokens healthy after pruning. I will fix my stored dual BRBG module imports by adding the missing utilities module and updating the dual module, then verify with a best-config submission.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/auto_gamma_brbg.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # ---------------------------\n  # Shared utilities for BRBG\n  # ---------------------------\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def\
    \ _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"Use batch-aware HVGs if provided, otherwise compute HVGs with batch_key.\"\"\"\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          mask = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n          if mask.sum() > 0:\n              return mask\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n  def _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      \"\"\"Sparse-aware PCA via TruncatedSVD.\"\"\"\n      n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n      Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n      return Z\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \      B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n      return B, uniq\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      \"\"\"\n      Ridge fit batch one-hot B to predict PCs Z. Returns Z_hat (n x d) and W (b x d).\n      \"\"\"\n      BtB = B.T @ B\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n      Z_hat = B @ W\n      return Z_hat, W\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      \"\"\"\n      Build a batch-balanced kNN graph:\n        - Equal per-batch quotas (distributes remainder across batches in order)\n        - Binary connectivities (1.0), symmetric union\n        - Distances from per-batch neighbor queries (min distance when duplicate)\n      Returns (C, D) as CSR matrices.\n      \"\"\"\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      nb = len(uniq_batches)\n\
    \      if nb == 0 or n == 0:\n          return None, None\n\n      base = k_total // nb\n      rem = k_total - base * nb\n      quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq_batches:\n          idx_b = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_b.size == 0 or quotas[b] == 0:\n              continue\n          k = min(quotas[b] + 1, idx_b.size)  # +1 to allow self (to be dropped)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_b])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_b[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]\n              di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:quotas[b]]\n              di = di[mask][:quotas[b]]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j:\n                      continue\n\
    \                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n      if not pairs_min_dist:\n          return None, None\n\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n          rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy()\n      C.data[:] = 1.0  # binary connectivities\n      return C, D\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  # Utilities from my BRBG module\n  from praxis.auto_gamma_brbg import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n\
    \      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _one_hot_batches,\n      _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n      _build_balanced_knn,\n  )\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def dual_output_brbg(adata: ad.AnnData, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, gamma=0.74, l2=1e-3, k_total=48, metric='cosine') -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Dual-source BRBG (best-known config example):\n        - Embedding: ComBat-corrected PCA on HVGs (n_pcs_emb=64).\n        - Graph: BalancedGraph on batch-residualized PCs (n_pcs_graph=50, gamma, l2),\n          equal per-batch quotas, binary edges, symmetric union, cosine metric, k_total.\n      \"\"\"\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n      # Normalize/log1p and HVGs (shared)\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n\
    \      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Graph path: residualized PCs on HVGs\n      X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n      Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n      Z_corr = Z - gamma * Z_hat\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n      # Embedding path: ComBat → PCA(HVGs)\n      _ensure_dense_X(adata)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n      # Ensure HVG flag exists for PCA (ComBat can drop it)\n      adata.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      # Initialize neighbor keys then override\
    \ with BalancedGraph\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n\n      adata.uns['brbg_dual'] = {\n          'gamma': float(gamma),\n          'l2': float(l2),\n          'k_total': int(k_total),\n          'metric': metric,\n          'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n          'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n          'embedding': 'ComBat PCA on HVGs',\n          'graph_source': 'Residualized PCA on HVGs',\n      }\n      return adata\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Default to best-known config (EID 147): gamma=0.74, k=48, PCA64 embedding\n      return dual_output_brbg(adata, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, gamma=0.74, l2=1e-3, k_total=48, metric='cosine')\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BRBG-Dual-bestcfg: ComBat PCA64 Embedding + Residualized-PC\
    \ Balanced Graph (γ=0.74, k=48)\"\ntags: \"dual, combat, residualization, balanced-knn, cosine, pca\"\nabstract: \"Re-run of our best dual-output configuration for verification and reproducibility via storage modules: ComBat-corrected PCA (64 PCs) for X_emb and a batch-residualized PC graph (γ=0.74, l2=1e-3) with equal-quota balanced cosine kNN (k=48, binary).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph import dual_output_brbg\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Best-known configuration (expected ≈ EID 147)\n      return dual_output_brbg(adata, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, gamma=0.74, l2=1e-3, k_total=48, metric='cosine')\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering implementation options**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing \"balanced weighted\" connectivities, perhaps using rank-based weights instead of distance, since the previous method didn't perform well. However, I need to explore another direction suggested by reviews, like conducting a formal analysis. Creating a public memory capsule to summarize methods for reproducibility sounds helpful. I'll need to write a script to streamline my workflow, ensuring that I adjust for unresolved imports and conduct a proper evaluation.**Planning submission process**\n\nI need to follow the guideline allowing for two concurrent runs, but since none are running, I can proceed with creating a \"BRBG-Dual-best\" submission. This will involve importing the necessary module and ensuring it returns similar metrics. I'll pay close attention to the import paths, especially since Python's sys.path requires precise handling to locate the right directories. It looks like adjusting the\
  \ imports to reference the correct relative paths may help, ensuring everything works smoothly in the evaluation environment.**Updating import statements**\n\nI need to be cautious about importing from the 'storage/praxis' path. When importing brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph, I should append 'storage' then use the import statement accordingly, like \"from praxis.brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\". However, I noticed that existing imports in the module are incorrect because \"from storage.praxis...\" leads to absolute imports which aren't recognized. The proper format should be \"from praxis.auto_gamma_brbg import...\". I'll need to update this and implement the required functions in auto_gamma_brbg.py as well.**Finalizing submission details**\n\nI need to ensure that the ComBat HVG reapply fix is implemented within the brbg module. Once that's done, I can submit \"BRBG-Dual-bestcfg\" by importing the module and calling the eliminate_batch_effect_fn for verification.\
  \ I'll maintain simplicity without suggesting extra changes for now. \n\nI'll execute the actions to update the relevant files and handle the imports properly. After appending 'storage' to sys.path, the main import will work. I think I've got everything set for submission!**Finalizing submission details**\n\nLet's include the title: \"BRBG-Dual-bestcfg: ComBat Embedding (PCA64) + Residualized-PC Balanced Graph (gamma=0.74, k=48)\" and appropriate tags. I hope this run produces about 0.7188. After submitting, I'll create a summary for Public Memory and provide identity and status upfront while keeping it brief.\n\nI'll implement the BalancedGraph builder to ensure equal quotas per batch, distributing any remainders effectively. The function will calculate nearest neighbors while avoiding self-references, ensuring smooth edge creation and distance tracking. Now, it's time to execute the storage writes and proceed with the submission!"
