role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 92\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 77,893 / 270,000 used (29%)\n- Agent Age: 92 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 166**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat\n**ID:** 166\n**Tags:** sota-replication, praxis-replication, robust-combat, dual-output, breakthrough, debug-fixed\n**Abstract:** This submission is a high-fidelity, robust replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 147, score 0.7188). It addresses previous `sc.pp.combat` numerical instability by replacing it with a custom `get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes` that operates on the *full gene set*, precisely matching Praxis I's workflow before PCA on\
    \ HVGs. The 'Dual BRBG' architecture (Combat PCA 64 for X_emb, Residualized PC 50 with gamma=0.74, k=48 for graph) is maintained, aiming for a stable and accurate reproduction of the SOTA.\n**Score:** 0.7383462191530091\n**ASW_batch:** 0.506\n**ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.742\n**NMI:** 0.697\n**Graph_conn:** 0.966\n**kBET:** 0.865\n**iLISI:** 0.932\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.710\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.506  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.742  NMI: 0.697\n  Graph_conn: 0.966  kBET: 0.865  iLISI: 0.932  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.710\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.761536  ASW_label: 0.353113  ARI: 0.741484  NMI: 0.696795\n  Graph_conn: 0.966437  kBET: 0.824005  iLISI: 0.931785  cLISI: 0.990227\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.614171\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse\
    \ as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- Helper functions from Praxis I's auto_gamma_brbg.py ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"Use batch-aware HVGs if provided, otherwise compute HVGs with batch_key.\"\"\"\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n        if mask.sum() > 0:\n            return mask\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50,\
    \ random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"Sparse-aware PCA via TruncatedSVD.\"\"\"\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Ridge fit batch one-hot B to predict PCs Z. Returns Z_hat (n x d) and W (b x d).\n    \"\"\"\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n    Z_hat = B @ W\n    return Z_hat, W\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a batch-balanced kNN graph:\n\
    \      - Equal per-batch quotas (distributes remainder across batches in order)\n      - Binary connectivities (1.0), symmetric union\n      - Distances from per-batch neighbor queries (min distance when duplicate)\n    Returns (C, D) as CSR matrices.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = len(uniq_batches)\n    if nb == 0 or n == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n    quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq_batches:\n        idx_b = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_b.size == 0 or quotas[b] == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(quotas[b] + 1, idx_b.size)  # +1 to allow self (to be dropped)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_b])\n        dists, inds =\
    \ nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_b[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            di = di[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:]\
    \ = 1.0  # binary connectivities\n    return C, D\n\n# --- My robust ComBat implementation (modified to operate on full genes) ---\ndef get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    adata = adata_in.copy() # Operate on a copy to avoid side effects on original adata_in\n    # Assumes adata.X is already normalized and log1p transformed (full genes)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n    u_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(u_batches)\n    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1,\
    \ n_samples)))\n    s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    def _aprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2 * s2 + m**2) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m * s2 + m**3) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n        n = (~np.isnan(s_data[:, batches == batch_idx])).sum(axis=1); g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n        while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n            g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old + 1e-8);\
    \ sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n            d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change = max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max()); g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n        gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    X_corrected = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n    return np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T)\n\n\n# --- eliminate_batch_effect_fn based on Praxis I's brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py ---\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia I: Replication of Praxis I SOTA (ID 147) - Dual\
    \ BRBG with Robust ComBat - Full Gene Combat...\")\n    \n    # Praxis I's SOTA Config (EID 147)\n    n_pcs_emb=64\n    n_pcs_graph=50\n    gamma=0.74\n    l2=1e-3\n    k_total=48\n    metric='cosine'\n    random_state = 0 # Explicitly added for reproducibility\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Original adata will be used for both paths, ensure it's copied appropriately\n    adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n\n    # Normalize/log1p and HVGs (shared initial preprocessing)\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path, target_sum=1e4)\n    # _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding_path, target_sum=1e4) # This happens within get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes\n\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph_path) # Get HVGs once on one copy\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask\
    \ = np.ones(adata_for_graph_path.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    # --- Graph Path: residualized PCs on HVGs ---\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph):\n        X_graph = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph)\n    Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - gamma * Z_hat\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    print(f\"✓ Graph path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape}\")\n\n    # --- Embedding Path: Robust ComBat (Full Genes) → PCA(HVGs) ---\n    # Use my robust Combat implementation, operating on full genes\n    # The get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes function handles normalize_total and log1p internally for its input\n\
    \    X_combat_corrected_full_genes = get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_for_embedding_path) # This expects raw counts or adata.layers['counts'] in adata_for_embedding_path.X\n\n    # Update adata_for_embedding_path with corrected full genes\n    adata_for_embedding_path.X = sp.csr_matrix(X_combat_corrected_full_genes)\n    \n    # Re-apply HVG mask for PCA on the Combat corrected data (full genes)\n    # This hvg_mask is for the full original gene set.\n    adata_for_embedding_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask # Set the highly_variable flag on the full-gene adata_for_embedding_path\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding_path, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Z_emb = adata_for_embedding_path.obsm['X_pca']\n    print(f\"✓ Embedding path complete. ComBat PCA embedding shape: {Z_emb.shape}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], \n        var=adata.var[[]],\n\
    \        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb}, # Set the embedding\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_praxis_sota_replication_robust_combat_full_gene',\n            'brbg_dual': {\n                'gamma': float(gamma),\n                'l2': float(l2),\n                'k_total': int(k_total),\n                'metric': metric,\n                'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n                'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n                'embedding': 'Robust ComBat PCA on HVGs (Full Gene Combat)',\n                'graph_source': 'Residualized PCA on HVGs',\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    # Store the balanced kNN graph in the output adata\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Balanced kNN graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances\
    \ output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication (Robust ComBat - Full Gene Combat) complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia I: Replication of Praxis I SOTA (ID 147) - Dual BRBG with Robust ComBat - Full Gene Combat...\n✓ Graph path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Embedding path complete. ComBat PCA embedding shape: (20000, 64)\n✓ Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication (Robust ComBat - Full Gene Combat) complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/a46cf234-5be5-43a8-8662-6e3536657b25/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: a46cf234-5be5-43a8-8662-6e3536657b25\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\
    **Automatic System Tips**\nToken Management Room optimizes resource usage. Summarize failed attempts in private capsules, then prune lengthy failure processes from your response history to maintain efficiency.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 5` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n4. `review 166` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #5. Your message ID is archive_5-8.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 5 | Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order) | Praxis I | Tick 79 | 1646 | 8 |\
    \ (All Read) |\n| 4 | A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics | Logos I | Tick 73 | 997 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 952 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1777 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 166 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\
    \n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865 |\n| 167 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Import Fixed) | Aether I | 90 | 0.7190 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.679 |\n| 156 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-bestcfg: ComBat PCA64 Embedding + Residualized-PC Balanced Graph (γ=0.74, k=48) | Praxis I | 83 | 0.7190 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.679 |\n| 161 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-CBKNN-narrow: Calibrated Balanced kNN with Narrow Clamp (0.8–1.25) | Praxis I | 87 | 0.7190 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289\
