tick: 95
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Archive Room. Robust MAD ComBat variants were negative (PCR collapsed), while Sophia I’s robust ComBat showed a high but unbalanced SOTA. I will try a conservative, label-free location-only ComBat for the embedding (mean-shift only, no variance scaling) paired with my residualized-PC BalancedGraph, then manage tokens.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/robust_loc_combat.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  def _to_dense(X):\n      return X.toarray() if sp.issparse(X) else np.asarray(X)\n\n  def robust_location_combat_full(adata_in: ad.AnnData, batch_key='batch', eps=1e-8, shrink_mode='ratio'):\n      \"\"\"\n      Robust location-only ComBat on normalized/log1p full-gene matrix (no variance scaling).\n      - For each gene g:\n        • Global center mu_g = median over all cells.\n        • For batch b: m_bg = median of gene g in\
    \ batch b.\n        • Batch effect gamma_hat_bg = m_bg - mu_g.\n        • Shrink gamma via robust scale ratio: shrink = s_g^2 / (s_g^2 + s_bg^2 + eps), where s = MAD.\n        • gamma_star_bg = shrink * gamma_hat_bg.\n        • Correct X[i,g] for cells in batch b: X_corr[i,g] = X[i,g] - gamma_star_bg + mu_g.\n      This avoids per-batch variance scaling (delta), aiming to preserve PCR/label geometry while removing mean shifts.\n      \"\"\"\n      X = _to_dense(adata_in.X)\n      n, p = X.shape\n      batches = np.asarray(adata_in.obs[batch_key].astype('category').values)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n\n      # Robust global stats (per gene)\n      mu = np.median(X, axis=0, keepdims=True)  # (1, p)\n      # MAD-like robust scale\n      abs_dev = np.abs(X - mu)\n      s_global = 1.4826 * np.median(abs_dev, axis=0, keepdims=True) + eps\n      s2g = s_global**2\n\n      # Per-batch median and robust scale\n      med_b, s_b = {}, {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx = np.where(batches\
    \ == b)[0]\n          if idx.size == 0:\n              continue\n          Xb = X[idx, :]\n          mb = np.median(Xb, axis=0, keepdims=True)  # (1, p)\n          s = 1.4826 * np.median(np.abs(Xb - mb), axis=0, keepdims=True) + eps\n          med_b[b], s_b[b] = mb, s\n\n      X_corr = X.copy()\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx.size == 0:\n              continue\n          m_bg = med_b[b]                  # (1, p)\n          s_bg = s_b[b]                    # (1, p)\n          gamma_hat = m_bg - mu            # (1, p)\n          # shrink factor in [0,1]\n          shrink = s2g / (s2g + (s_bg**2))\n          gamma_star = shrink * gamma_hat\n          X_corr[idx, :] = X[idx, :] - gamma_star + mu\n\n      X_corr = np.nan_to_num(X_corr, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n      return X_corr\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/brbg_dual_robustloc.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata\
    \ as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from praxis.auto_gamma_brbg import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _one_hot_batches,\n      _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n      _build_balanced_knn,\n  )\n  from praxis.robust_loc_combat import robust_location_combat_full\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Dual-output with robust location-only ComBat (no variance scaling) for the embedding,\n      plus residualized PCs + BalancedGraph for the graph.\n      \"\"\"\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      gamma = 0.74\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Shared normalization and HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata,\
    \ target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Graph path: residualized PCs on HVGs\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n          Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - gamma * Zhat\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n      # Embedding path: robust location-only ComBat on normalized/log1p full matrix, then PCA on HVGs\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n      X_corr = robust_location_combat_full(adata_emb, batch_key='batch', eps=1e-8)\n      adata_emb.X = sp.csr_matrix(X_corr)\n      adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] =\
    \ hvg_mask\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Zemb = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      # Output\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      adata.uns['brbg_dual'] = {\n          'gamma': float(gamma),\n          'l2': float(l2),\n          'k_total': int(k_total),\n          'metric': metric,\n          'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n          'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n          'embedding': 'Robust location-only ComBat PCA on HVGs',\n          'graph_source': 'Residualized PCA on HVGs',\n      }\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BRBG-Dual-RobustLocComBat: Location-only Robust ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph\"\n\
    tags: \"dual, robust-combat, location-only, residualization, balanced-knn, pca\"\nabstract: \"Embedding uses location-only robust ComBat (median/MAD shrink, no variance scaling) on normalized/log1p full genes (PCA64). Graph uses residualized PC50 (γ=0.74) with equal-quota balanced cosine kNN (k=48, binary). Goal: modest kBET/cell_cycle gains without harming label/PCR.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.brbg_dual_robustloc import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"80-88\"\n    summary: |\n      Publication acceptance, verification, CBKNN, and analysis:\n      - Archive accepted (10/10) for Dual BRBG SOTA (0.7188), added analysis plan; verification EID 156 = 0.7190 (Result UUID cc4bbadf-...).\n      - CBKNN variants (calibrated balanced kNN) tied baseline: EID 158 = 0.7189; EID 161 = 0.7190 (no gain).\n      - Separation test (EID 168, test\
    \ mode): principal angles up to ~81°, modest neighbor overlap (~0.55); ComBat PCA64 nearly zero batch R² per PC; residualized PCs retain small batch R²; cross‑batch fraction higher in ComBat embedding under naive kNN—supports “separation of concerns.”\n```"
thinking_content: "**Documenting system management**\n\nI’m considering how we could document press and publish negative results in the archive. It’s also time to prune older tokens in Token Management since the cooldown has passed. We last pruned at tick 83 and can do so again at tick 95. I’m thinking about proposing a \"batch-specific whitening\" equalization for embedding to manage covariance differences while keeping the means intact. But this might take time to implement—perhaps as an ablation? The last user message was just system info, though.**Proposing standardization methods**\n\nI’m thinking about proposing a \"per-batch z-score gene standardization\" anchored to global robust statistics to prevent PCR from hitting zero. Alternatively, we could try a \"ComBat location-only\" approach with delta set to 1, which avoids over-scaling that can lead to PCR collapse or unnatural label silhouette. I realize we could implement our own robust ComBat variant correcting only for intercept,\
  \ which should allow us to test the \"location-only\" method while maintaining improvements in kBET and cell cycle without harming labels.**Evaluating PCR stability**\n\nIt seems like we can prevent PCR from collapsing to zero, possibly maintaining values around 1.0. This could lead to embeddings that are similar to what we achieved with ComBat-PCA but more robust and stable. Previously, we used ComBat PCA64 in dual mode as our default, focusing on high variance genes (HVGs) after normalization. It appears that our baseline is strong, even if there were warnings. Given that, the \"location-only\" variant might not be necessary, as I prefer to stick with scientifically sound methods.**Finalizing analysis plan**\n\nI’m thinking I shouldn’t chase Sophia's questionable high score. Instead, I’ll focus on finalizing the analysis paper addendum. One action I plan to take is to append a recap of negative results to the archive capsule. I might also suggest reading logos or aether archives to gather\
  \ useful ideas. For the proposed \"two-space union adjacency with per-edge classification,\" I realize there may be potential degradation. I'll ensure the research log is updated for robust negative results and consider pruning earlier heavy analysis ticks between 80 and 90.**Planning pruning and implementation**\n\nIt looks like we previously pruned ticks 62-79, but older ticks remain. I'm considering pruning a large block from 80-88, which includes important summaries like acceptance and verification updates. Since it's been 12 ticks since the last prune, I'm ready to take action in Token Management. \n\nI’ll also implement the \"location-only ComBat robust\" code quickly, creating a new file for this function. The idea is to remove gamma without delta scaling, which should help maintain PCR near 1.0. Let’s prepare and submit this code now, along with necessary commands for pruning."
