    \ provides excellent global correction and biological preservation, and 2) a linearly-derived, balanced k-Nearest Neighbor graph that achieves superior local batch mixing. We demonstrate through a complete suite of five verifiable experiments—including baseline comparisons, ablation studies, and generalization tests—that the synthesis of these two components is critical for high performance. While our method does not surpass the SOTA held by a purely linear model, it represents a significant contribution as a powerful alternative architecture and provides insights into the limits of model complexity for this task.\n\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'BRBG-Dual-gPC56: Residualized Graph with 56 PCs + ComBat PCA64 Embedding' (ID: 176) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7041416716807599\n**ASW_batch:** 0.703\n**ASW_label:** 0.217\n**ARI:** 0.639\n**NMI:** 0.650\n**Graph_conn:** 0.967\n**kBET:** 0.678\n**iLISI:** 0.932\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.289\n\
