parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Research Counter. Status: Dual BRBG remains my frozen default (~0.719; EIDs 156/147). Recent ablations (MAD/location-only ComBat, graph PCs=56, PC-weighted graph) were negative. Packaging is complete (storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py). I’ll append a final consolidated note with code path and EIDs to the archive, then create a brief private handover capsule.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Final consolidation (tick 102): Frozen defaults, EIDs, and code path\n\n  Frozen default (Dual BRBG):\n  - Embedding: sc.pp.combat on normalized/log1p full matrix → PCA64 on HVGs (ComBat numerical warnings benign).\n  - Graph: residualized PCs on HVGs (PC50; γ=0.74, l2=1e-3) → equal-quota balanced cosine kNN (k=48), binary.\n  - Reproducible code: storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py\n\n  Best stable evaluations (all verifiable):\n  - EID 156 (bestcfg): 0.7190 (ARI 0.742, NMI 0.697, ASW_batch 0.703, kBET 0.679, iLISI\
    \ 0.932, cLISI 0.966, PCR 1.000).\n  - EID 147 (γ=0.74, k=48): 0.7188 (near-tie; earlier run).\n\n  Negative results (abbreviated):\n  - Robust ComBat (MAD/loc-only): EIDs 171=0.6036 (PCR 0.000), 172=0.6094 (PCR 0.026), 174=0.6057 (PCR 0.000) → collapsed PCR; reject.\n  - Graph PC56: EID 176=0.7041 → ARI/NMI drop; keep PC50.\n  - PC-weighting w_j=sqrt(1−R²_j): EID 177=0.7154 → ARI/NMI modestly down; mixing unchanged; reject.\n\n  Note: Sophia I’s robust ComBat (EID 166=0.7383) achieved very high kBET/cell_cycle but had ASW_label=0.0 (later fixed in EID 175 to ~0.7188). Our conservative default remains 0.719 with strong balance and minimal knobs.\n\n  Takeaway:\n  - Separation of concerns holds: linear residualized PCs + balanced graph for local mixing; ComBat+PCA for global embedding.\n  - Adding complexity in either path did not yield net gains here; we recommend the frozen defaults above as a strong, parsimonious baseline.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"Handover: Praxis I status at tick 102 (Dual BRBG defaults + EIDs)\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary:\n  - Default method: Dual BRBG (embedding: ComBat+PCA64; graph: residualized PC50 with γ=0.74, l2=1e-3; balanced k=48 cosine, binary).\n  - Best stable scores: EIDs 156/147 ≈ 0.7190. Code: storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py\n  - Key insights: quotas > weights; γ has a narrow ridge (~0.74–0.75); PC>50 in graph degrades ARI/NMI; ComBat variants (robust MAD/loc-only) collapsed PCR.\n  - Negative EIDs: 171 (0.6036), 172 (0.6094), 174 (0.6057), 176 (0.7041), 177 (0.7154).\n  - Accepted archive: “Dual BRBG…” plus consolidated replies (IDs in Archive #5).\n  Next directions (if resumed):\n  - If exploring new gains, consider entirely new embeddings (nonlinear) paired with the same balanced graph, or second dataset generalization when available.\n  - Otherwise, prioritize documentation, reproducibility, and maintenance of the frozen default.\n```"
