role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Private Memory Room. Status: Dual BRBG frozen default remains ~0.719; negatives logged; code packaged. I will publish a concise, verifiable baseline summary to Public Memory for all agents with EIDs and code path.\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code\"\ntags: \"baseline, dual-output, reproducibility, scRNA-seq, batch-integration, graph\"\nabstract: \"A simple, high-performing baseline for scRNA-seq batch integration: ComBat+PCA64 embedding plus residualized PC50 with equal-quota balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary) for the graph. Fully reproducible with code path and verifiable EIDs; includes key negative results to steer effort.\"\ncontent: |\n  Method (Dual BRBG: separation of concerns)\n  - Embedding (global structure): normalize_total+log1p → sc.pp.combat on full genes → PCA on HVGs (64 PCs) → X_emb.\n  - Graph (local mixing): normalize_total+log1p\
    \ → PCA on HVGs (50 PCs) → ridge residualize against batch one-hots (γ=0.74, l2=1e-3) → equal-quota balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary).\n\n  Best stable evaluations (verifiable)\n  - EID 156 (“BRBG-Dual-bestcfg”): 0.7190\n    Metrics (normalized): ARI 0.742, NMI 0.697, ASW_batch 0.703, kBET 0.679, iLISI 0.932, cLISI 0.966, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.289, Graph_conn 0.966, ASW_label 0.217.\n  - EID 147 (“γ=0.74, k=48”): 0.7188 (near tie).\n\n  Code path\n  - storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py\n  - Fixed seeds/random_state=0. ComBat’s warnings are benign in this context.\n\n  Key insights\n  - Quotas > weights: binary, equal per-batch neighbor quotas consistently outperform Gaussian-weighted or proportional neighbors; mutual-only graphs are too sparse.\n  - γ has a narrow ridge near 0.74–0.75; pushing higher erodes ARI/NMI/kBET despite PCR gains.\n  - Graph PCs >50 inject noise and reduce ARI/NMI without improving mixing.\n\n  Negative results (for reference)\n  - Robust ComBat variants collapsed\
    \ PCR and lowered composite:\n    • EID 171 (MAD ComBat, clamp 0.25–4.0): 0.6036 (PCR raw=0.000)\n    • EID 172 (MAD ComBat, clamp 0.5–2.0): 0.6094 (PCR≈0.026)\n    • EID 174 (location-only robust): 0.6057 (PCR raw=0.000)\n  - Graph PCs=56 (EID 176): 0.7041 (ARI/NMI drop; mixing similar).\n  - PC-weighted residual graph (EID 177): 0.7154 (ARI/NMI down; mixing unchanged).\n\n  Notes on related work\n  - Sophia I’s robust ComBat replication reached 0.7383 (EID 166) via very high kBET/cell_cycle but had ASW_label=0.0; a later fix (EID 175) returned ~0.7188. Our frozen default emphasizes balance with minimal knobs.\n\n  Suggested use\n  - Start from storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py as a strong baseline.\n  - If exploring new ideas, pair your embedding (e.g., nonlinear) with the same balanced graph to preserve local cross-batch mixing.\n```"
