    \ spot)\n          lam=0.9,          # mild scaling of per-PC R^2\n          k_total=48,\n          metric='cosine'\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Lineage Research Log (Adaptive residualization results)\n  New results:\n    - EID 185 (per-PC adaptive; gamma_max=0.74, lam=0.9): 0.7209\n      Metrics: ASW_batch 0.703 | ASW_label 0.217 | ARI 0.732 | NMI 0.694 | Graph_conn 0.972 | kBET 0.679 | iLISI 0.938 | cLISI 0.970 | PCR 1.000 | Cell_cycle 0.302\n    - EID 184 (per-PC adaptive; gamma_max=0.75, lam=1.0): 0.7193\n  Comparison vs frozen default (EIDs 156/147 ≈ 0.7190):\n    - Small but consistent gains in Graph_conn (+0.006) and cLISI (+0.004); ARI/NMI preserved; batch mixing unchanged.\n  Takeaway:\n    - Per-PC adaptive γ_j (bounded) improves slightly over uniform γ. Conservative settings (gamma_max=0.74, lam=0.9) outperform more aggressive ones.\n  Packaging:\n    - Frozen best adaptive pipeline saved at storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py.\n\
    \  Current recommendations:\n    - Preferred: best_dual_brbg_adapt.py (0.7209).\n    - Stable baseline: best_dual_brbg.py (≈0.7190).\n  Notes:\n    - BIVG HVG underperformed (EID 182 = 0.7146).\n    - Robust ComBat variants collapsed PCR (EIDs 171/172/174).\n    - Graph PCs >50 degraded ARI/NMI (EID 176).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 5}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update: Per-PC adaptive residualization slightly improves Dual BRBG\n  - EID 185 (Adaptive; gamma_max=0.74, lam=0.9): 0.7209\n    Normalized metrics: ASW_batch 0.703, ASW_label 0.217, ARI 0.732, NMI 0.694, Graph_conn 0.972, kBET 0.679, iLISI 0.938, cLISI 0.970, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.302.\n    Result UUID: 84579e3d-995a-4b7d-a6b6-f1642d6a8023\n  - EID 184 (Adaptive; gamma_max=0.75, lam=1.0): 0.7193 (weaker than conservative)\n    Normalized metrics: ASW_batch 0.703, ASW_label 0.217, ARI 0.732, NMI 0.694, Graph_conn 0.972, kBET 0.680, iLISI 0.938, cLISI 0.970, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.286.\n   \
    \ Result UUID: fed15612-0fcc-4eda-ba91-e45752031d57\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - Bounded per-PC γ_j gently de-emphasizes batch-predictable PCs without harming biological geometry, yielding small gains in Graph_conn and cLISI at constant ARI/NMI.\n  - Conservative settings (γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9) align with our global γ sweet spot and outperform a more aggressive (0.75, 1.0).\n\n  Code path (frozen):\n  - Adaptive dual: storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py (EID 185 settings).\n  - Non-adaptive dual (frozen baseline ≈ 0.719): storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py.\n\n  Negative references (for completeness):\n  - BIVG HVG (batch-invariant HVG) underperformed: EID 182 = 0.7146.\n  - Robust ComBat variants (MAD/location-only) collapsed PCR (EIDs 171/172/174).\n  - Graph PCs=56 reduced ARI/NMI: EID 176 = 0.7041.\n\n  Recommendation:\n  - For reproducible high performance with minimal knobs, use the adaptive dual (EID 185 config). If robustness across datasets is a concern, keep both adaptive and non-adaptive\
    \ as fallback baselines.\n```"
