    \ edges through large biological gaps while retaining mixing.\n- Construction (one knob τ):\n  - For each batch b: compute distances d(i, j) for candidates; convert to scores s = exp(−d/τ).\n  - Allocate per-batch quotas as equal-quotas baseline; fill edges per batch in descending s with a per-node cap to hit degree ~k; break ties by smaller distance.\n  - Symmetrize union; binarize; guarantee degree via a final pass that fills deficits with next-best scores (respecting batch diversity).\n- Limits: τ → 0 recovers equal-quotas; τ too large drifts toward global KNN (mixing collapse).\n- Batch-only selection:\n  - Sweep τ ∈ {0.05, 0.1, 0.2}; pick the smallest τ that matches or exceeds baseline Graph_conn and iLISI while not increasing same-batch edge fraction. If all violate, revert to τ=0 (equal-quotas).\n- Complexity: reuse per-batch NN indices; additional scoring is O(nnz) over candidate edges; memory stays CSR, binary connectivities.\n\nEnd-to-end, label-free auto-selection for (γ_max,\
    \ λ)\n- Use per_pc_resid_auto proxies:\n  - Optimize for mean_r2_resid (post-residualization batch predictability) on PCs; plateau rule with ε (e.g., 1e-4).\n  - Add graph sanity: on Z_corr (pre-balanced graph), require cross-batch fraction in naive kNN ≥ baseline; on a 3k subsample, ensure largest connected component size under balanced graph prototype ≥ baseline.\n  - Choose the smallest (γ_max, λ) passing both. This encodes “conservative > aggressive,” matching EID 185 > 184.\n\nAlternative feature sets: variance-of-residuals HVGs (VoR-HVG)\n- Procedure:\n  - On normalized/log1p counts, per gene g fit batch dummies (ridge) to get residuals R_g; compute Var(R_g); pick top-2k genes — strictly batch-label-only.\n  - Replace HVGs with VoR-HVGs in both embedding and graph paths; keep all else fixed.\n- Rationale:\n  - Targets post-batch signal rather than penalizing mean shifts directly (which hurt BIVG).\n- Expectations:\n  - ARI/NMI: flat to slightly up; mixing unchanged (residualization\
    \ + quotas dominate).\n  - Reject if ARI/NMI drop >0.002 or kBET/iLISI/Graph_conn degrade.\n\nGeneralization and packaging\n- Ship three artifacts:\n  - Non-adaptive frozen baseline (~0.719): best_dual_brbg.py\n  - Adaptive frozen (0.7209): best_dual_brbg_adapt.py\n  - Auto-selector: per_pc_resid_auto.py (plateau/tie-break toward smaller params).\n- Safe exploration order (one knob at a time, batch-only selection):\n  1) Auto (γ_max, λ) selector; verify vs EID 185.\n  2) Soft quotas τ (start 0.05); keep τ if iLISI/Graph_conn ≥ baseline and same-batch edge fraction not up.\n  3) VoR-HVG; proceed only if ARI/NMI improve with mixing flat.\n  4) Embedding whitening/robust z: attempt last, reject on slightest label loss.\n- Repro checks: fixed seeds, CSR graphs, metric plateaus logged, and per-run EIDs/UUIDs."
