- text: "Closing synthesis and prioritized plan\n\nWhere we stand\n- Frozen non-adaptive Dual BRBG ≈ 0.719 (robust, minimal knobs).\n- Per-PC adaptive residualization (conservative) improved to 0.7209 (EID 185), mainly via small Graph_conn/cLISI gains with ARI/NMI preserved.\n- Negative lines: robust ComBat variants (PCR collapse), graph PCs > 50 (ARI/NMI drop), PC post-weighting (no gain), BIVG HVGs (small net loss).\n\nCore hypotheses to push beyond 0.72\n- Gentle, label-free adaptivity pays off when bounded and conservative (γ_max < 0.75, λ < 1).\n- Enforcing cross-batch locality structurally is right; we may still prune pathological edges with a single soft parameter τ without sacrificing mixing.\n- “Use only what remains after batch” could help at the feature level if we target residual variance (VoR-HVG) rather than penalizing between-batch means (BIVG mistake).\n- Embedding path is near-optimal; any normalization that flattens useful variation (whitening, heavy robust scaling) risks\
    \ ARI/NMI.\n\nExperiment plan (one knob at a time; accept only with clear criteria)\n\n1) Label-free auto-selector for (γ_max, λ)\n- Mechanism: use mean_r2_resid plateau on PCs (post-residualization) with tie-break toward smaller params; enforce batch-only graph proxies (cross-batch fraction in naive kNN, connectivity) not worse than baseline.\n- Target grid: γ_max ∈ {0.72, 0.74, 0.75}, λ ∈ {0.8, 0.9, 1.0}; choose smallest pair on the plateau.\n- Acceptance: if selected params match or beat EID 185 on full eval or are neutral and simpler to justify; otherwise keep EID 185.\n\n2) Soft quotas (single τ)\n- Construction: per-batch candidate neighbors scored s = exp(−d/τ); water-filling to expected per-batch quotas; symmetrize; binarize. τ → 0 recovers equal quotas.\n- Sweep τ ∈ {0.05, 0.1, 0.2} at γ_max/λ from the auto-selector (or EID 185).\n- Acceptance: iLISI and Graph_conn ≥ baseline; same-batch edge fraction not higher; ARI/NMI within −0.002. If any violation, revert to τ = 0.\n\n\
    3) Variance-of-residuals HVGs (VoR-HVG)\n- Procedure: regress out batch dummies per gene (ridge) on normalized/log1p counts; rank genes by residual variance; pick top 2,000; plug into Dual BRBG (adaptive).\n- Acceptance: ARI/NMI up ≥ 0.003 with iLISI/kBET/Graph_conn no worse than −0.003 and PCR ≈ 1.0; otherwise revert to standard HVGs.\n\n4) Embedding preprocessing (last resort)\n- Whitening (sphering) after ComBat PCA or robust per-gene z-scores before PCA.\n- Acceptance: strict—no ARI/NMI loss (>0.002) and no mixing degradation (>0.005). Expect neutral/negative; run only if earlier steps plateau.\n\nEvaluation, proxies, and guardrails\n- Batch-only proxies (no labels) guide knob choice: mean_r2_resid plateau, cross-batch fraction in naive kNN (k=15, cosine), connectivity on a 3k subsample.\n- Full evaluations confirm; reject on any consistent ARI/NMI or mixing regression beyond thresholds above.\n- Keep CSR graphs, fixed seeds, and log result UUIDs; sub-sample proxies to manage compute.\n\
    \nGeneralization and packaging\n- Ship both frozen pipelines:\n  - best_dual_brbg.py (~0.719) and best_dual_brbg_adapt.py (0.7209).\n- Include per_pc_resid_auto.py with the plateau rule; recommend it as default selector to avoid per-dataset overfitting.\n- Document negative results, rationale, and stop conditions to prevent rabbit holes.\n\nStop rule and publication\n- Timebox: if none of τ or VoR-HVG yields ≥ +0.002 absolute score over 0.7209 within a modest sweep, freeze the adaptive default as “final” for this dataset.\n- Prepare an appendix update: auto-selector details, τ design, VoR-HVG method, EIDs/UUIDs, and metric deltas; emphasize parsimony and label-free selection."
thinking_content: '**Evaluating preprocessing strategies**


  I’m looking at embedding preprocessing like whitening or robust z-scores and planning to test only if earlier steps plateau, accepting results only if there''s no label drop. I see risks like overfitting to the heart dataset and tying to heuristics, so I need to keep changes minimal. I''ll have a generalization plan to test on a second dataset later and document updates with new EIDs and paths while monitoring memory constraints. Lastly, I''ll set stop criteria: if nothing exceeds a +0.002 absolute score after attempts, I’ll freeze.'
