tick: 110
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Reflection Chamber. Next step: implement label-free auto-selection of per-PC adaptive residualization (γ_max, λ) and evaluate it within Dual BRBG. Then compare to EID 185 (0.7209).\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/brbg_dual_adaptive_auto.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.auto_gamma_brbg import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n      _get_hvg_mask,\n      _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _build_balanced_knn,\n  )\n  from praxis.per_pc_resid_auto import adaptive_residualize_auto\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Dual BRBG with label-free auto-selection of per-PC adaptive residualization params.\n        - Graph path:\
    \ PCs on HVGs (50) → auto-select (gamma_max, lambda) via mean_r2_resid plateau → adaptive residualization → balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary).\n        - Embedding path: ComBat on full genes (post normalize/log1p) → PCA64 on HVGs.\n      Stores chosen (gamma_max, lambda) and summaries in .uns['brbg_dual_auto'].\n      \"\"\"\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max_list = (0.72, 0.74, 0.75)\n      lam_list = (0.8, 0.9, 1.0)\n      eps_plateau = 1e-4\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Graph path: PCs on HVGs + auto adaptive residualization\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n     \
    \     Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      Zcorr, r2_pre, r2_resid_best, gamma_j, chosen = adaptive_residualize_auto(\n          Zg, batches, l2=l2,\n          gamma_max_list=gamma_max_list, lam_list=lam_list, eps_plateau=eps_plateau\n      )\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n      # Embedding path: ComBat + PCA64 on HVGs\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n      adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Zemb = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      # Output\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D\
    \ is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n\n      adata.uns['brbg_dual_auto'] = {\n          'chosen_gamma_max': float(chosen.get('gamma_max', -1)),\n          'chosen_lambda': float(chosen.get('lam', -1)),\n          'mean_r2_resid': float(chosen.get('mean_r2_resid', -1.0)),\n          'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n          'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n          'k_total': int(k_total),\n          'metric': metric,\n      }\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC-Auto: Label-free per-PC adaptive selection (plateau rule)\"\ntags: \"dual, adaptive, auto-select, residualization, balanced-knn, pca\"\nabstract: \"Dual BRBG with auto-selected per-PC adaptive residualization parameters using a label-free plateau rule on post-residualization batch predictability (mean R^2). Embedding = ComBat+PCA64; graph = adaptive residualized PCs (50) + balanced kNN (k=48, cosine).\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.brbg_dual_adaptive_auto import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Lineage Research Log (Auto-adaptive residualization)\n  Implemented label-free auto-selection for per-PC adaptive residualization:\n    - Module: storage/praxis/per_pc_resid_auto.py (returns Z_corr and chosen params via mean_r2_resid plateau).\n    - Pipeline: storage/praxis/brbg_dual_adaptive_auto.py (Dual BRBG with auto-selected gamma_max, lambda).\n  Submission:\n    - BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC-Auto: evaluates whether the plateau rule recovers conservative settings (e.g., ~gamma_max=0.74, lambda=0.9) and matches/exceeds EID 185 (0.7209).\n  Next (if auto is neutral/positive): explore soft quotas with a single temperature τ and VoR-HVGs as single-knob additions; otherwise keep EID 185 frozen adaptive as default.\n```"
