- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Research Counter. Soft-quota τ=0.05 yielded 0.7199 (neutral vs best 0.7209). VoR-HVG was a nuanced negative. τ=0.10 (EID 198) is running; I’ll log the τ=0.05 result, check τ=0.10 status, and update my research log.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 5}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Result: Soft-quota balanced kNN (τ=0.05) in adaptive Dual BRBG\n  - EID 195: 0.7199\n    Normalized metrics: ASW_batch 0.703, ASW_label 0.217, ARI 0.732, NMI 0.694, Graph_conn 0.972, kBET 0.678, iLISI 0.938, cLISI 0.970, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.294.\n    Result UUID: 76d27dc8-069b-431b-9dbc-9ac75725cb34\n  Interpretation:\n  - Soft quotas (τ=0.05) essentially tie equal-quotas: mixing and label metrics remain at baseline levels; no net gain over the best conservative adaptive config (EID 185 = 0.7209).\n  - Action: keep equal-quotas (τ=0) as default unless τ=0.10 (pending) shows consistent benefit.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{review\
    \ 198}\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Lineage Research Log (soft quota result + status)\n  Soft quotas (adaptive Dual BRBG: gamma_max=0.74, lambda=0.9; PC50; k=48; cosine):\n    - EID 195: τ=0.05 → 0.7199 (neutral vs best 0.7209). Graph_conn/iLISI/ARI/NMI ~ baseline; no improvement.\n    - EID 198: τ=0.10 → pending.\n  VoR-HVG (residual-variance HVGs):\n    - EID 193: 0.7179 (ARI/NMI ↑, but mixing ↓ → composite ↓). Revert to standard HVGs.\n  Summary:\n    - Best remains EID 185 (0.7209). Soft quotas (τ small) are neutral; larger τ under review. Auto-adaptive ~0.7195 (neutral). Packaging complete (frozen baselines + auto-selector).\n  Next:\n    - If τ=0.10 is neutral/negative, freeze EID 185 as final for this dataset and focus on documentation/appendix updates (auto-selector details, negative results).\n```"
thinking_content: '**Consolidating findings**


  I’m finalizing that the best remains EID 185 and noting the soft quota didn''t show improvement. Before concluding, I need to finish evaluating τ=0.10. I might also consider adding to the archives and implementing steps like label-free summaries or token management pruning, as I’m currently at 50% token usage with 134k. I’ll archive the reply with EID 195 results and update the research log. It seems I need a plan to shift focus if no improvement is seen.**Evaluating combined strategies**


  I’m considering a combined approach since using ComBat had issues with ASW_label before, but now it''s comparable at 0.7188 after a fix. It doesn’t seem to be better, so I’ll archive the reply with the soft quota result and update the research log. I could try τ=0.02 for more conservative quotas, but since 0.05 was already practically equal, it’s not worth it. Maybe a change in parameters for adaptive residualization could help, but micro-tuning may not be effective. I’ll finalize the packaging and the "stop rule."**Planning multiple actions**


  I see that the instructions allow for multiple actions in one response. I can archive the result for EID 195 and decide whether to wait for τ=0.10 since cancellation isn’t an option. I’ll also update the research log to summarize findings and return to token management to prune earlier long messages. While I could prune ticks 89–104, many of them are important. Currently, the token usage is 50%, so it’s not critical, but I can propose to finalize and post about our new best result of 0.7209.**Focusing on necessary actions**


  I might add a reply to the public space, but I''ll keep my actions minimal for now. First, I’ll archive the reply with the EID 195 result. Next, I’ll update the research log. If EID 198 finishes later, I can process it, but currently, we don’t have the result. I should mention that the EID 195 result is 0.7199, which shows no improvement over EID 185. I’ll summarize the outcomes and ensure proper formatting in YAML before producing the reply.'
