- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Research Counter. Summary: Adaptive residualization (EID 185) is our best at 0.7209. Auto-adaptive (EID 190) and soft quotas (EIDs 195/198) are neutral. VoR-HVG is a nuanced negative. I will freeze EID 185 as the recommended default, update the archive and public note, and append a brief handover update in private memory.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 5}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Finalization for Human Heart (Dual BRBG, tick 115)\n  - Best result (frozen default): EID 185 = 0.7209\n    Config: per-PC adaptive residualization in graph path (γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9) on PC50; balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary); embedding = ComBat+PCA64 on HVGs.\n    Result UUID: 84579e3d-995a-4b7d-a6b6-f1642d6a8023\n    Code: storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py\n\n  Neutral/negative follow-ups:\n  - Soft quotas (single τ):\n    • EID 195 (τ=0.05) = 0.7199 (tie). UUID: 76d27dc8-069b-431b-9dbc-9ac75725cb34\n    • EID 198 (τ=0.10) = 0.7195 (tie). UUID:\
    \ c639a4cf-d725-4b13-9cae-2b41a1d81103\n    → Equal-quotas remains default.\n  - Auto-adaptive selection (plateau rule): EID 190 = 0.7195 (neutral). UUID: 08339852-eb9f-40be-8b51-c8d431e7066f\n    → Useful for label-free deployment, but conservative fixed params (EID 185) are stronger here.\n  - VoR-HVG (residual-variance HVGs): EID 193 = 0.7179 (ARI/NMI ↑, mixing ↓; net ↓). UUID: a24c39e0-0308-48ff-a637-fe2e9aeeeea6\n    → Retain standard HVGs.\n\n  Recommendation:\n  - Use best_dual_brbg_adapt.py (EID 185) as the primary pipeline; keep best_dual_brbg.py (~0.719) as the stable fallback.\n  - Negative results (robust ComBat variants, graph PCs>50, PC post-weighting, BIVG, VoR-HVG, soft quotas) are documented to avoid unproductive directions.\n\n  Next steps:\n  - Consolidate code + README; maintain both frozen baselines and the auto-selector utility for future datasets. No further knobs were found to improve over 0.7209 without trade-offs.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\
    \n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Final baseline update:\n  - Best config: EID 185 = 0.7209 (adaptive residualization in graph path with γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9; PC50; k=48; cosine; binary; embedding = ComBat+PCA64).\n  - Neutral: soft quotas (τ=0.05 → 0.7199; τ=0.10 → 0.7195); auto-adaptive (plateau) ~0.7195.\n  - Negative: VoR-HVG (0.7179), robust ComBat variants, PCs>50, PC post-weighting, BIVG HVGs.\n  - Code: storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py (primary); storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py (fallback).\n  Use these as reproducible baselines; further tweaks showed no consistent gain.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (tick 115):\n  - Final default: EID 185 = 0.7209 (adaptive γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9). Code frozen: storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py\n  - Neutral: soft quotas τ=0.05/0.10; auto-adaptive ~0.7195.\n  - Negative: VoR-HVG (mixing down), robust ComBat variants (PCR collapse), PCs>50 (ARI/NMI\
    \ drop), PC post-weighting, BIVG.\n  - Plan: Freeze for this dataset; maintain baselines + auto-selector for generalization; prioritize documentation and support.\n```"
