role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Research Counter. 207 (fused min) = 0.7177: slight ARI/NMI gains (0.735/0.700) but kBET/ASW_batch down vs EID 185 (0.7209). Equal-quotas with adaptive residualization remains best so far. I’ll check 208 (geomean fusion) and try a harmonic-mean fusion, which is closer to min but still requires partial agreement from both views.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{review 208}\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Praxis Log (tick 122)\n  Fusion trials on dual BRBG (adaptive PCs + ComBat PCA64):\n  - EID 207 (fused min): 0.7177\n    ARI/NMI 0.735/0.700 (↑ vs 185), kBET 0.637 (↓), iLISI 0.935 (≈), cLISI 0.971 (↑), ASW_batch 0.693 (↓).\n    Conclusion: min fusion slightly helps label metrics but hurts mixing; net below EID 185 (0.7209).\n  - EID 208 (geometric-mean fusion): pending.\n  Next: test harmonic-mean fusion (closer to “min” behavior, but still penalizes single-view-only neighbors).\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage\
    \ write praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_fused_harm.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\n  from praxis.brbg_common import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict\n  )\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn_fused_harm(Z_corr, Z_emb, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', extra=4):\n      \"\"\"\n      Equal per-batch quotas using fused per-batch distances:\n      Candidate set = union of top (per_batch+extra) neighbors from Z_corr and Z_emb (within each batch).\n      Fused distance df = harmonic_mean(dc, de) when both present; otherwise min(dc, de).\n      Harmonic mean stays closer to the smaller distance than geometric/arith., preserving mixing while adding agreement\
    \ signal.\n      \"\"\"\n      Z_corr = np.asarray(Z_corr, dtype=np.float32)\n      Z_emb  = np.asarray(Z_emb,  dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z_corr.shape[0]\n      per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0])))\n\n      nn_corr, nn_emb = {}, {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx.size == 0:\n              continue\n          k = min(per_batch + extra + 1, idx.size)\n          nnc = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nne = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nnc.fit(Z_corr[idx]); nne.fit(Z_emb[idx])\n          nn_corr[b] = (idx, nnc)\n          nn_emb[b]  = (idx, nne)\n\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train, nnc = nn_corr[b]\n          _,         nne = nn_emb[b]\n          k = min(per_batch + extra + 1, idx_train.size)\n\n          d_c, ind_c = nnc.kneighbors(Z_corr,\
    \ n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          g_c = idx_train[ind_c]\n          d_e, ind_e = nne.kneighbors(Z_emb, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          g_e = idx_train[ind_e]\n\n          for i in range(n):\n              cand = {}\n              # corr-view\n              for gj, dj in zip(g_c[i], d_c[i]):\n                  if gj == i: continue\n                  prev_c, prev_e = cand.get(gj, (np.inf, np.inf))\n                  cand[gj] = (min(prev_c, float(dj)), prev_e)\n              # emb-view\n              for gj, dj in zip(g_e[i], d_e[i]):\n                  if gj == i: continue\n                  prev_c, prev_e = cand.get(gj, (np.inf, np.inf))\n                  cand[gj] = (prev_c, min(prev_e, float(dj)))\n              # Fuse with harmonic mean when both finite; else min\n              items = []\n              for gj, (dc, de) in cand.items():\n                  if np.isfinite(dc) and np.isfinite(de) and (dc > 0.0) and (de > 0.0):\n                      df\
    \ = float(2.0 / (1.0/dc + 1.0/de))\n                  else:\n                      df = min(dc, de)\n                  items.append((gj, df))\n              items.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\n              for gj, df in items[:per_batch]:\n                  a, c = (i, gj) if i < gj else (gj, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (df < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = df\n\n      if not pairs_min_dist:\n          return None, None\n\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C, D\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Dual BRBG with fused two-view balanced graph (harmonic-mean fusion):\n        - Graph view: residualized PCs (adaptive\
    \ per-PC: gamma_j=min(0.74, 0.9*R^2_j)), PCs=50.\n        - Embedding view: ComBat on normalized/log1p + PCA64 (HVGs).\n        - Equal-quota balanced kNN per batch using dfused=harmonic_mean(dc, de) (fallback to min if one missing).\n      \"\"\"\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      extra = 4\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Graph view\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(Xg): Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n\
    \      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n\n      # Embedding view\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n      adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Zemb = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      # Fused equal-quota balanced graph\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_fused_harm(Zcorr, Zemb, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, extra=extra)\n\n      # Output\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      adata.uns['brbg_dual_adapt_fused_harm'] = {\n          'gamma_max': float(gamma_max), 'lambda': float(lam), 'l2': float(l2),\n          'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric, 'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph), 'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n          'fusion': 'harmonic-mean(dc, de) with min fallback', 'extra': int(extra)\n      }\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-BRBG-Adapt-FusedHarm: Two-View Equal-Quota Graph (k=48, harmonic fusion)\"\ntags: \"dual, adaptive, fused, harmonic-mean, balanced-knn, cosine\"\nabstract: \"Dual BRBG with equal-quotas balanced kNN built from fused per-batch distances using harmonic mean of residualized-PC and ComBat-PCA64 per-batch distances (fallback to min if one is missing). Seeks ARI/NMI gains with less mixing loss than geometric fusion.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.brbg_dual_adapt_fused_harm import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n\
    ```"
thinking_content: '**Planning improvements and experiments**


  I need to make an identity statement and conduct a brief analysis of the results for 207, which showed some improvement in ARI/NMI but lost on ASW_batch/kBET. The fused-min approach seems to favor label metrics, which may not be worth it overall. For 208, I''m hypothesizing that requiring agreement might reduce cross-batch mixing. I''ll also save the research log update for 207 results, and propose testing a cautious variant like "mean-of-views." We can submit one more run while managing our evaluation slots.**Exploring fusion methods**


  The "Automatic System Tips" suggest not to give up, which makes me think about testing "max fusions." I noticed that the min method picks the best of two distances and yields good mixing. In contrast, geomean seems more conservative and may reduce mixing while improving labels. For example, the 207 results showed min improved ARI/NMI but decreased on kBET. I''m now considering trying a harmonic mean, which penalizes when one view is large. However, it might be dominated by smaller distances, so I need to evaluate all these options further.**Testing harmonic mean fusion**


  I''m calculating that the harmonic mean (HM) of two numbers is 2/(1/d1 + 1/d2). If d1 is small (like 0.1) and d2 is large (10), the HM would be around 0.198. This is larger than the min value of 0.1 but much smaller than the max value of 10. It seems that HM is closer to min, which preserves mixing while using both views. This approach could keep cross-batch edges and improve ARI/NMI slightly. So, I think we can propose testing the HM fusion as "FusedHarmonic." I''ll implement this quickly while keeping some parameters constant for comparison!**Analyzing top results**


  I need to analyze the table of top results. We have a SOTA score of 0.7383 from Sophia I with "Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat," but it has an ASW_label of 0.0, which seems strange. The high composite score comes from PCR at 1.0, but we also noted earlier that there may be a bug. Our best remains at 0.7209 for adaptability. We should approach this but maybe not immediately. For next actions, I''ll review 208, log 207 results, save the fused harmonic code, and submit the new evaluation for "Dual-BRBG-Adapt-FusedHarm."**Crafting harmonic code**


  I’m getting ready to write the code for harmonic fusion and I plan to build on the existing skeleton. I need to ensure that I import the required functions correctly. I’ll replicate parts from the fused_geom module with some minor changes, remembering to use proper YAML quoting. My final message will include several commands: reviewing 208, updating the research log for 207, saving the harmonic fusion code, and submitting it with the right title and import path, while also mentioning debugging options. Let''s implement this efficiently!'
