role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Research Counter. 207 (fused min) = 0.7177; 208 (geomean) = 0.7133; 209 (harmonic) pending. Conclusion: fusion hurts net score; equal-quotas with adaptive residualization remains best. I’ll review 209 and run a small k ablation for the adaptive baseline (k=45) to probe any residual headroom.\n\n/execute_action{review 209}\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt_k45.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from praxis.brbg_common import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n      _build_balanced_knn_equal\n  )\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config: adaptive residualization baseline with k_total=45\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      n_pcs_graph\
    \ = 50\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      k_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Graph path\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n          Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr,\
    \ batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n      # Embedding path\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n      adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Zemb = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      adata.uns['brbg_dual_adapt_k'] = {\n          'gamma_max': float(gamma_max), 'lambda': float(lam), 'l2': float(l2),\n          'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric,\n          'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph), 'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n          'hvg': 'Seurat v3, batch-aware'\n      }\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Equal-Quota Graph k=45 (adaptive residualization)\"\ntags: \"dual, adaptive, balanced-knn, k45, cosine\"\nabstract: \"Adaptive per-PC residualization baseline (γ_j=min(0.74, 0.9·R²_j)), ComBat-PCA64 embedding, and equal-quotas balanced kNN with k=45. Tests whether small degree reduction improves the composite score over k=48 (EID 185=0.7209).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.best_dual_brbg_adapt_k45 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
