parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Archive Room. Best remains EID 185 = 0.7209. Small-degree and fusion variants underperformed. I identified a flaw in my balanced graph builder: for k not divisible by number of batches, my per-batch ceiling created more neighbors than requested (e.g., k=45 still produced 48). I will implement an exact balanced-quotas graph: distribute k_total exactly as q per batch plus r extras rotating across batches per node. This may yield a small but principled improvement.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/brbg_common.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X\
    \ = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n      Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n      return Z\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(cats)\n      n = cats.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, uniq.shape[0]), dtype=np.float64)\n      col = {u:i for i,u in enumerate(uniq)}\n      for i, b in enumerate(cats):\n          B[i, col[b]] = 1.0\n      return B, uniq\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      K = B.shape[1]\n      BtB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(K)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BtB, B.T @ Z)   # (K x d)\n      Zhat = B @ W                        # (n x d)\n      # per-PC R^2\n      Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n\
    \      SSE = np.sum((Z - Zhat)**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n      SST = np.sum(Zc**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n      R2 = 1.0 - (SSE / SST)\n      return Zhat, np.clip(R2, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n  # Existing equal-quotas (ceil) builder (kept for compatibility)\n  def _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0])))\n\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0:\n              continue\n          k = min(per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)  # +1 for potential self\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in\
    \ range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]\n              di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:per_batch]\n              di = di[mask][:per_batch]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n      if not pairs_min_dist:\n          return None, None\n\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C, D\n\n  # Existing min-quota + global fill (kept)\n  def _build_balanced_knn_minq(Z, batches, k_total=48, min_per_batch=2, metric='cosine'):\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0:\n              continue\n          k = min(min_per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]\n              di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:min_per_batch]\n              di = di[mask][:min_per_batch]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n         \
    \             pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n      fill_each = max(0, k_total - int(min_per_batch * uniq.shape[0]))\n      if fill_each > 0:\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(fill_each + 1, n), metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z)\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=min(fill_each + 1, n), return_distance=True)\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = inds[i]\n              di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:fill_each]\n              di = di[mask][:fill_each]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n      if not pairs_min_dist:\n          return None, None\n\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n\
    \          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C, D\n\n  # New: exact balanced quotas (q per batch + r extras per node), rotating extras across batches per node\n  def _build_balanced_knn_equal_exact(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      B = uniq.shape[0]\n      if B == 0 or k_total <= 0:\n          return None, None\n\n      q = k_total // B\n      r = k_total % B\n\n      # Pre-fit per-batch NNs up to max needed neighbors (q + 1 extra + self)\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for bi, b in enumerate(uniq):\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0:\n              continue\n          kmax = min(q + 1 + 1, idx_train.size)  # q + possible extra + self\n          nn =\
    \ NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kmax, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=kmax, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n\n          for i in range(n):\n              # Rotate extras for fairness: r batches get +1 neighbor for node i\n              order = [(bi + i) % B for bi in range(B)]\n              extras = set(order[:r])\n              # select k_b for this batch index\n              k_b = q + (1 if bi in extras else 0)\n\n              g = neigh_global[i]\n              di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:k_b]\n              di = di[mask][:k_b]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n\
    \      if not pairs_min_dist:\n          return None, None\n\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C, D\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt_equal_exact.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from praxis.brbg_common import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n      _build_balanced_knn_equal_exact\n  )\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config: adaptive residualization + exact balanced quotas (k_total exactly enforced)\n     \
    \ n_pcs_emb = 64\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Graph PCs + adaptive residualization\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n          Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg\
    \ - Zhat * gamma_vec\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal_exact(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n      # Embedding (ComBat + PCA64 on HVGs)\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n      adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Zemb = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      adata.uns['brbg_dual_adapt_equal_exact'] = {\n          'gamma_max': float(gamma_max), 'lambda': float(lam), 'l2': float(l2),\n          'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric,\n          'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph), 'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n\
    \          'hvg': 'Seurat v3, batch-aware', 'quotas': 'exact q per batch + rotating r extras'\n      }\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Equal-Quota Graph (Exact k=48) with Adaptive Residualization\"\ntags: \"dual, adaptive, balanced-knn, exact-quotas, cosine\"\nabstract: \"Fixes balanced graph degree to exactly k_total: distribute q=floor(k/B) per batch plus r=k%B rotating extras per node. Combined with adaptive per-PC residualization (γ_j=min(0.74, 0.9·R²_j)) and ComBat-PCA64 embedding. Tests whether exact degree improves the composite score over EID 185 (0.7209).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.best_dual_brbg_adapt_equal_exact import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
thinking_content: '**Exploring graph optimization**


  I''m considering a two-stage graph approach that utilizes a balanced graph to connect both cross-batch edges and within-batch neighbors, which could help maintain local structure. It''s interesting that we already keep equal quotas per batch, suggesting that within-batch edges will add to our same-batch edges perfectly. I remember that using binary edges has worked well in the past. Oh, and I wonder about different distance metrics, like testing correlation distance; maybe that could yield useful insights!I''m considering another approach using diffusion or manifold densification by calculating neighbors and their connections while weighing distances. Since we mostly use binary edges, I wonder if some adaptive weighting could help label silhouette while keeping in mind that it might lead to mixing issues. There''s also the challenge of ensuring balanced quotas without oversampling sparse areas. Maybe I could look into improving residualization by incorporating low-rank removal and adjusting
  our existing gamma calculations based on R². It''s all quite complex!I''m thinking of trying ComBat on highly variable gene (HVG) masked features before PCA. While we already apply ComBat to the dense full matrix, I should ensure that the HVG mask is set correctly before this step. I''ve noted that using a higher number of PCs can be tricky, especially since PC56 harmed our Adjusted Rand Index results. It might be useful to test slight adjustments between 48 and 50 PCs. I''m also keeping an eye on our token usage, as we don''t want to overextend ourselves!I''m thinking about using BalancedGraph with equal quotas, but considering how to round the per-batch neighbor count when the total isn''t divisible by the number of batches. For example, with four batches and k set to 48, we end up with 12 per batch. I''m checking to see if we''re replicating neighbors correctly. The algorithm currently computes per-batch neighbors for each batch, which results in a set number of edges. I realize this
  affects the total degree and could lead to discrepancies.I''m identifying a bug in how we calculate ''k'' within our algorithm. We need to adjust it to ensure we''re distributing remaining quotas across batches to meet the exact `k_total`. By implementing a BalancedEqualExact algorithm, I plan to pick neighbors smartly, ensuring fairness without bias. I also need to code the function carefully to avoid affecting existing functions but ensure everything runs smoothly. Additionally, I''ll refine the parameters slightly and set everything up for robust testing with the necessary documentation and storage updates. It''s a lot, but I''m feeling good about it!I''m planning to merge functions from `brbg_common.py`, including `_build_balanced_knn_equal` and `_build_balanced_knn_minq`, along with the new `_build_balanced_knn_equal_exact`. My next steps involve writing the updated file while ensuring we preserve existing functions since other modules rely on them. I''ll also write the new code file
  that utilizes the exact function. It''s crucial to manage our token usage wisely, as we still have some margin. Let''s get these commands drafted and finalize the process efficiently!'
