tick: 134
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Research Counter. Whitening ComBat PCs yields new SOTA 0.7293 (EID 220). Soft whitening at alpha=0.7 scored 0.7287; alpha=0.85 dropped to 0.7256. I’ll review alpha=0.9 when ready and queue alpha=0.8 to complete the sweep, then document SOTA in the Archive.\n\n`/execute_action{review 227}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_embed_softwhiten_a080.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.brbg_common import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n      _build_balanced_knn_equal\n  )\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def _soft_whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', alpha=0.8, eps=1e-8):\n      Z = adata_emb.obsm[key]\n      var = adata_emb.uns.get('pca', {}).get('variance', None)\n      if var is None:\n  \
    \        return Z\n      scale = np.power(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None), 0.5 * float(alpha))\n      Zw = Z / scale\n      Zw -= Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      return Zw\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Graph identical to EID 185; embedding uses soft whitening (alpha=0.8)\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      alpha = 0.8\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Graph view (unchanged)\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(Xg): Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n      # Embedding view: ComBat + PCA64 + soft whitening\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n      adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Zemb = _soft_whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', alpha=alpha, eps=1e-8)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.8) + Equal-Quota Graph\"\ntags: \"dual, adaptive, embedding-soft-whiten, balanced-knn, cosine\"\nabstract: \"Keep EID 185 graph; modify only the embedding with soft whitening alpha=0.8 (var^{-alpha/2}). Completes the 0.7/0.8/0.85/0.9 sweep to refine the mixing vs label/cell-cycle trade-off.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.brbg_dual_adapt_embed_softwhiten_a080 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (tick 134): Whitened ComBat Embedding lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293\n\n  Summary:\n  - New SOTA: EID 220 (tau=0.95 whitening on ComBat-PCA64 embedding) = 0.7293, UUID 9018bf47-80eb-4958-8d6b-ebbed5f90d1a.\n  - EID 223 (tau=1.0) = 0.7292, UUID 49efef67-cb29-4a14-a99f-b0140f6dd0af\
    \ (tied).\n  - Trade-off: mixing metrics surge (ASW_batch≈0.839, kBET≈0.906) while ASW_label↓ and Cell_cycle↓; ARI/NMI stable.\n  - Soft whitening sweep to balance trade-offs:\n    • EID 224 (alpha=0.7) = 0.7287, UUID 625c7e54-0bfc-4770-b42b-675d058444a9 (ASW_label/Cell_cycle partially recover).\n    • EID 225 (alpha=0.85) = 0.7256, UUID 28810ee0-7fc7-42da-82c5-91af20bb5fea (worse).\n    • EID 227 (alpha=0.9) = pending; EID 226/228 (alpha=0.8 or variants) pending (see Research Counter).\n  - Code paths:\n    • Whitening (tau): storage/praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten.py (tau param).\n    • Soft whitening: storage/praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_embed_softwhiten.py (alpha=0.7), _a085.py (0.85), _a090.py (0.9), _a080.py (0.8).\n\n  Recommendation:\n  - Freeze tau≈0.95 as default SOTA (0.7293) with full EID/UUID; keep adaptive residualized graph unchanged.\n  - Soft whitening alpha≈0.7 is a viable alternative when ASW_label/Cell_cycle conservation matters with minimal score loss.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating embedding results**


  I found that PC56 had negative results for graph embedding. However, we didn''t test dimensions for the embedding, and it could be interesting to try ComBat PCA50 whitened. Since we whiten the data, truncating dimensions might remove weaker principal components, possibly harming label silhouette. After adjusting the embedding, I noticed a change; reducing dimensions might improve labeling. It seems there''s a trade-off between ASW_label adjustment and mixing, which complicates the analysis.**Analyzing alpha values**


  I noticed that soft whiten at 0.7 produced a score of 0.7287, which is slightly below 0.7293. I’m thinking maybe there''s a combination that achieves similar mixing but with a better label. An alpha around 0.8 could yield a label of 0.17 and mixing of 0.87, but I saw 0.85 performed worse than 0.7. The numbers seem a bit inconsistent, which makes it tricky. I might test alpha values of 0.8 or 0.65 to find the best balance; a final run at alpha 0.8 could be useful.**Planning next steps**


  I''ll run alpha at 0.8 as a second slot, but only if concurrency allows it, since we''re running 227 in one slot right now. I want to craft a clear action plan: first, review the results of 227 when they''re available. Next, I''ll submit alpha at 0.8. I plan to update the archive with the new SOTA of 0.7293 and its details. Additionally, I might start revising the paper or draft a short note on "Whitened ComBat Embedding for BRBG." I''ll record these updates and keep the explanations concise to follow the YAML quoting rules.'
