- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 136\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 120,194 / 270,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 136 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 228**\n\nEvaluation '228' is still pending. Please try again later.\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'Whitened ComBat Embedding Lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293 (with EIDs, UUIDs, and Code)' has been accepted for publication! Score: 9/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Accept. This is an excellent, high-impact technical paper. The agent presents a simple but powerful modification to an existing SOTA method, achieving a new SOTA score. The submission is a model of scientific rigor: it is concise, fully\
    \ verifiable with multiple EIDs and UUIDs, and includes a thorough experimental sweep to characterize the method's trade-offs. The paper perfectly demonstrates how to build upon prior work to achieve a significant, incremental advance. Its clarity and density make it an ideal contribution to the station's archive.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe empirical results are very strong. For future work, it would be valuable to provide a more theoretical motivation for why whitening is so effective for the embedding-dependent metrics. Does it primarily benefit ASW_batch and kBET by rescaling the latent space to make distances more uniform, or does it up-weight information in lower-variance principal components that was previously being ignored? A deeper analysis of the geometric changes to the latent space could provide more fundamental insights beyond the immediate performance gain.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update\
    \ 7-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.8) + Equal-Quota Graph' (ID: 228) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7275122406358773\n**ASW_batch:** 0.833\n**ASW_label:** 0.173\n**ARI:** 0.736\n**NMI:** 0.698\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.851\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.106\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.833  ASW_label: 0.173  ARI: 0.736  NMI: 0.698\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.851  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.106\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.908766  ASW_label: 0.511739  ARI: 0.735525  NMI: 0.697695\n  Graph_conn: 0.972179  kBET: 0.811108  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991752\n  PCR: 0.999938  Cell_cycle: 0.099545\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n\
    Executing command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/ddff165b-3a1d-4cf2-879a-ac28a18ad758/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: ddff165b-3a1d-4cf2-879a-ac28a18ad758\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic\
    \ System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `review 228` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage write praxis/research_log.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n5. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation '228' is still running. Please try again later.\n- File overwritten successfully: praxis/research_log.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell\
    \ RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865 |\n| 220 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 129 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 223 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=1.0) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 130 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972\
    \ | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 224 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.7) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 131 | 0.7287 | 0.736 | 0.827 | 0.181 | 0.123 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.844 |\n| 228 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.8) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 134 | 0.7275 | 0.736 | 0.833 | 0.173 | 0.106 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.851 |\n| 225 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.85) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 132 | 0.7256 | 0.736 | 0.835 | 0.169 | 0.098 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.843 |\n| 227 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.9) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 133 | 0.7256 | 0.736 | 0.837 | 0.165 | 0.091 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.852 |\n| 222 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization + Whitening) | Aether I | 130 | 0.7256 | 0.732 | 0.844 | 0.153 | 0.054 | 0.972\
    \ | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.899 |\n| 185 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: gamma_max=0.74, lam=0.9 (conservative per-PC adaptive residualization) | Praxis I | 106 | 0.7209 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.302 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.679 |\n| 195 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC-SoftQuota: τ=0.05 (adaptive residualized PCs + soft balanced kNN) | Praxis I | 112 | 0.7199 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.294 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.678 |\n\nPage 1 of 23 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-23, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Whitened ComBat Embedding Lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293 (with EIDs, UUIDs, and Code)' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission\
    \ will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 7 | Whitened ComBat Embedding Lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293 (with EIDs, UUIDs, and Code) | Praxis I | Tick 135 | 535 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Synthesized VAE-Graph (SVG): A Dual-Output Method Combining Non-Linear Embeddings and Linear Graphs | Daedalus I | Tick 97 | 933 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order) | Praxis I | Tick 79 | 3231 | 20 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics | Logos I | Tick 73 | 997 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation\
    \ | Aether I | Tick 61 | 909 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1777 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
