tick: 136
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Archive Room. I will run a label-free geometry analysis (test mode) to address the reviewer’s suggestion: quantify how whitening affects latent-space anisotropy and neighbor structure using only batch labels (allowed). I’ll compare ComBat+PCA64 vs whitened and soft-whitened embeddings on:\n- Axis variance anisotropy (top-5 vs bottom-5), participation ratio\n- kNN (cosine) neighbor batch entropy and cross-batch fraction\n- kNN distance uniformity (per-cell CV)\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Embedding Whitening Geometry Analysis (test mode)\"\ntags: \"analysis, whitening, embedding, geometry, neighbors\"\nabstract: \"Label-free analysis of ComBat-PCA64 vs whitened/soft-whitened embeddings: axis variance anisotropy, participation ratio, kNN batch entropy/cross-batch fraction, and kNN distance uniformity (cosine). Provides geometric insight into why whitening boosts mixing metrics.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def _normalize_log1p(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _get_hvg_mask(adata):\n      # Prefer provided batch-aware HVGs if available\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          m = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n          if m.sum() > 0:\n              return m\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n  def _combat_pca64(adata, hvg_mask):\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n  \
    \    _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n      adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=64, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      var = adata_emb.uns.get('pca', {}).get('variance', None)\n      return Z, var\n\n  def _whiten(Z, var, tau=1.0, eps=1e-8):\n      if var is None:\n          return Z\n      scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None))\n      Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n      Zw -= Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      return Zw\n\n  def _soft_whiten(Z, var, alpha=0.7, eps=1e-8):\n      if var is None:\n          return Z\n      scale = np.power(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None), 0.5 * float(alpha))\n      Zw = Z / scale\n      Zw -= Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      return Zw\n\n  def _participation_ratio(var):\n      v = np.asarray(var, dtype=float)\n      s1 = (v.sum())**2\n      s2 = (v**2).sum() + 1e-12\n     \
    \ return float(s1 / s2)\n\n  def _anisotropy_ratio(Z):\n      # sum of top-5 axis variances / sum of bottom-5 axis variances\n      Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      v = np.var(Zc, axis=0, ddof=1)\n      if v.size < 10:\n          return float('nan')\n      top = np.sort(v)[-5:].sum()\n      bot = np.sort(v)[:5].sum() + 1e-12\n      return float(top / bot)\n\n  def _knn_stats(Z, batches, k=30, metric='cosine'):\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k+1, Z.shape[0]), metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      # drop self\n      neigh_idx = []\n      neigh_dist = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          mask = inds[i] != i\n          neigh_idx.append(inds[i][mask][:k])\n          neigh_dist.append(dists[i][mask][:k])\n      neigh_idx = np.array(neigh_idx, dtype=object)\n      neigh_dist = np.stack(neigh_dist, axis=0)\n\n      # cross-batch fraction and batch entropy\n     \
    \ uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      logK = np.log(len(uniq) + 1e-12)\n      cross_frac = []\n      ent = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = batches[i]\n          nb = neigh_idx[i]\n          bnb = batches[nb]\n          cross_frac.append(np.mean(bnb != bi))\n          # entropy over neighbor batch distribution\n          counts = np.array([(bnb == u).sum() for u in uniq], dtype=float)\n          p = counts / max(1, counts.sum())\n          # add tiny epsilon to avoid log 0\n          p = np.clip(p, 1e-12, 1.0)\n          ent.append(-(p * np.log(p)).sum() / max(logK, 1e-12))\n      cross_frac = float(np.mean(cross_frac))\n      batch_entropy = float(np.mean(ent))\n\n      # distance uniformity: per-cell CV of neighbor distances, then mean across cells\n      mean_d = neigh_dist.mean(axis=1)\n      std_d = neigh_dist.std(axis=1, ddof=1)\n      cv = (std_d / (mean_d + 1e-12)).mean()\n      return {\n          'cross_batch_frac': cross_frac,\n          'batch_entropy_norm': batch_entropy,\n\
    \          'knn_dist_cv': float(cv),\n          'mean_knn_dist': float(mean_d.mean())\n      }\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      print(\"=== Embedding Whitening Geometry Analysis (label-free) ===\")\n      print(f\"Dataset shape: {adata.shape}\")\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"batch labels required\"\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Prep normalized counts and HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n\n      # Baseline ComBat+PCA64\n      Z_base, var = _combat_pca64(adata, hvg_mask)\n      # Variants\n      Z_tau95 = _whiten(Z_base, var, tau=0.95)\n      Z_tau100 = _whiten(Z_base, var, tau=1.0)\n      Z_a07 = _soft_whiten(Z_base, var, alpha=0.7)\n      Z_a08 = _soft_whiten(Z_base, var, alpha=0.8)\n\n      # Axis variance metrics\n      def axis_var(Z):\n          Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n          return np.var(Zc, axis=0, ddof=1)\n\n      var_base\
    \ = axis_var(Z_base)\n      pr_base = _participation_ratio(var_base) if var is not None else float('nan')\n      print(f\"[Base PCA64] PR={pr_base:.3f} Anisotropy(top5/bot5)={_anisotropy_ratio(Z_base):.3f}\")\n\n      for name, Z in [\n          (\"tau=0.95\", Z_tau95),\n          (\"tau=1.0\", Z_tau100),\n          (\"alpha=0.7\", Z_a07),\n          (\"alpha=0.8\", Z_a08),\n      ]:\n          v = axis_var(Z)\n          pr = _participation_ratio(v)\n          aniso = _anisotropy_ratio(Z)\n          stats = _knn_stats(Z, batches, k=30, metric='cosine')\n          print(f\"[{name}] PR={pr:.3f} Aniso={aniso:.3f} | \"\n                f\"cross_frac={stats['cross_batch_frac']:.3f} \"\n                f\"entropy={stats['batch_entropy_norm']:.3f} \"\n                f\"knn_dist_cv={stats['knn_dist_cv']:.3f} \"\n                f\"mean_knn_dist={stats['mean_knn_dist']:.3f}\")\n\n      return \"Analysis completed\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating kBET improvements**


  I can compute global kBET improvements using neighbors from embedding alone, but I notice the evaluation method utilizes an integrated graph. The test mode is supposed to print the "kNN batch entropy" as a proxy. Since this is in test mode, I need to make sure the function returns a string. According to the earlier specification, if the test function is present, the evaluation should return NaN, but it captures the print statements.**Planning storage module actions**


  I’m outlining the actions needed for our storage module in praxis/embed_analysis.py. I’ll create a function to run analysis with given adata and options for whitening. First, I’ll compute PCA64 to evaluate variance explained and create a whitened embedding. Then, for each embedding, I need to calculate the axis variance distribution, participation ratio, mean neighbor batch entropy with k=30, and standard/mean of kNN distances. Finally, I’ll print the metrics and submit a test script that processes adata, running ComBat and PCA while managing pre-whitening.**Creating submission for analysis**


  I’m preparing to create a submission for analysis without needing to change the integrated graph since we’re in test mode, which will print the results. My action plan: First, I’ll move to the research area using the command ''/execute_action{goto research}''. Next, I’ll write the content for praxis/embed_analysis.py, including the necessary functions. I’ll submit the first version titled "Embedding Whitening Geometry Analysis (test mode)," which will include the test function. In the test, I plan to build adata_emb from adata, but I’m considering if normalization and HVG selection are necessary for the embedding.**Implementing ComBat analysis**


  The data indicates that I should run ComBat on normalized/log1p counts using highly variable genes (HVGs) and store the HVG mask. I’ll perform PCA on these HVGs to compute variance per principal component. For uniformity, I''ll whiten using tau values of 1.0, 0.95, and soft alpha values of 0.7 and 0.8. Each variant will involve calculating the 30 nearest neighbors with cosine distance. For each cell, I’ll assess batch distributions, compute mean batch entropy, and determine mean distances. Lastly, I’ll compute a pairwise distance measure and print results to address the reviewer’s concerns about rescaling and variance weighting.**Planning metric computations and submission**


  I’m planning to show changes in participation ratio (PR) and neighbor distance coefficient of variation (CV) since whitening reduces anisotropy and makes neighborhoods more uniform. I won''t be able to demonstrate label-specific effects without labels, but the NMI/ARI stability is helpful. I’ll compute the dot product of PCA contributions, although printing the basic results should suffice. For now, I’ll schedule a test evaluation and update the archive later. I need to write the storage file and submit the test after creating the appropriate code with necessary functions. I''ll keep an eye on the token budget but feel secure.'
