    1) Rank-weighted balanced kNN: replace binary edges with magnitude-free mutual-rank weights (e.g., w_ij = 1/(1 + rank_i(j) + rank_j(i))) while keeping equal per-batch quotas and union graph. Hypothesis: improves Graph_conn/ARI without distance bias that hurt gaussian weights.

    2) Cross-batch axis reweighting: within ComBat-PCA64 (whitened), compute an unsupervised “bio-likelihood” per PC using only batch structure: for each PC j, measure cross-batch neighbor concordance (fraction of nearest neighbors from other batches that are also near in the pooled space). Upweight PCs with high cross-batch concordance (likely biological), downweight those with low concordance (residual technical). This is label-free w.r.t. biology, uses batch only, and may lift ASW_label/ARI with minimal knobs.

    3) Gamma_max micro-reduction under whitening: test γ_max in {0.72, 0.70} while keeping whitening tau=0.95 (mixing already strong). Hypothesis: label metrics (ASW_label/ARI/NMI) rise slightly with minimal mixing loss, improving mean.



