role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Reflection Chamber. I will implement the first prioritized idea: rank-weighted balanced kNN (mutual-rank weights on the quota-union graph) as a single, minimal change to the SOTA Dual BRBG pipeline, and evaluate it against the frozen default (EID 244).\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/dual_whitened_adaptpc_rank.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  EPS = 1e-8\n\n  # -------- Utilities --------\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top=2000):\n      if 'batch_hvg'\
    \ in adata.var.columns:\n          m = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n          if m.sum() > 0:\n              return m\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n      return svd.fit_transform(X)\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      m = cats.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, m), dtype=float)\n      B[np.arange(n), inv] = 1.0\n      return B, cats\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @\
    \ B\n      M = BTB + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1])\n      W = np.linalg.solve(M, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat, W\n\n  # -------- Balanced kNN: quota-union rank-weighted --------\n  def _balanced_knn_ranked(Z, batches, k_total=45, metric='cosine'):\n      \"\"\"\n      Build equal-quota per-batch kNN, union edges, then assign symmetric mutual-rank weights:\n        w_ij = 1 / (1 + rank_i(j) + rank_j(i)), with floor w_min = 1 / (1 + 2*k_total).\n      Distances remain symmetric minimum distances. Returns (connectivities CSR (weighted), distances CSR).\n      \"\"\"\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      nb = len(uniq)\n      base = k_total // nb\n      rem = k_total % nb\n      # Distribute remainder to first 'rem' batches to total k_total neighbors per node\n      quota = {b: base + (i < rem) for i, b in enumerate(uniq)}\n\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n      # Per-batch\
    \ neighbor search and union by keeping min distance per undirected edge\n      for b in uniq:\n          q = quota[b]\n          if q <= 0:\n              continue\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0:\n              continue\n          k = min(q + 1, idx_train.size)  # +1 to allow self; will drop later\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]\n              di = dists[i]\n              # Drop self if present\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:q]\n              di = di[mask][:q]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j:\n                      continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a,\
    \ c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n      if not pairs_min_dist:\n          return None, None\n\n      # Build adjacency lists to compute per-node ranks by distance\n      nbrs = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          nbrs[i].append((j, d))\n          nbrs[j].append((i, d))\n\n      # Rank maps: for each node, rank neighbors by ascending distance (1-based)\n      rank_map = [{} for _ in range(n)]\n      for i in range(n):\n          if not nbrs[i]:\n              continue\n          nbrs[i].sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\n          for r, (j, _) in enumerate(nbrs[i], start=1):\n              rank_map[i][j] = r\n\n      # Compute symmetric mutual-rank weights with a floor\n      w_min = 1.0 / (1.0 + 2.0 * max(1, k_total))\n      rows_c, cols_c, data_c = [], [], []\n      rows_d, cols_d, data_d = [], [], []\n\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          ri\
    \ = rank_map[i].get(j, len(nbrs[i]) + 1)\n          rj = rank_map[j].get(i, len(nbrs[j]) + 1)\n          w = 1.0 / (1.0 + ri + rj)\n          if w < w_min:\n              w = w_min\n          # Symmetric entries\n          rows_c.extend([i, j]); cols_c.extend([j, i]); data_c.extend([w, w])\n          rows_d.extend([i, j]); cols_d.extend([j, i]); data_d.extend([d, d])\n\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      C = coo_matrix((data_c, (rows_c, cols_c)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = coo_matrix((data_d, (rows_d, cols_d)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      return C, D\n\n  # -------- Main pipeline: whitened embedding + adaptive per-PC residualized graph + rank-weighted quotas --------\n  def run_pipeline_ranked(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                          n_pcs_emb=64, alpha=0.95,\n                          n_pcs_graph=50, gamma_max=0.74, lam=0.9, l2=1e-3,\n                          k_total=45, metric='cosine', random_state=0) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Dual BRBG variant:\n\
    \        - Embedding: normalize/log1p → ComBat → PCA (n_pcs_emb) on HVGs → soft-whiten by std^alpha (alpha≈0.95)\n        - Graph: TruncatedSVD (n_pcs_graph) on HVGs → ridge batch-fit → adaptive per-PC shrink Zcorr = Z - gamma_j * Zhat\n                 with gamma_j = min(gamma_max, lam * R2_j) → equal-quota balanced kNN with mutual-rank weights.\n      \"\"\"\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n      assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      hvg = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg.sum() < 10:\n          hvg = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Graph path\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg]\n      if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n          Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Zg, l2=l2)\n      # R^2 per PC\n      Zc = Zg - Zg.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      Zhatc = Zhat - Zhat.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      varZ = np.var(Zc, axis=0) + EPS\n      varRes = np.var(Zc - Zhatc, axis=0)\n      R2 = np.clip(1.0 - varRes / varZ, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_j.reshape(1, -1)\n\n      C, D = _balanced_knn_ranked(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n      # Embedding path (ComBat + PCA + soft-whiten)\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n      adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Zemb = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      std = np.std(Zemb - Zemb.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True), axis=0) + EPS\n      Zemb = Zemb / (std ** alpha)\n\n      # Outputs\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata,\
    \ use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      adata.uns['dual_brbg_whitened_rank'] = {\n          'n_pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb), 'alpha': float(alpha),\n          'n_pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph), 'gamma_max': float(gamma_max),\n          'lam': float(lam), 'l2': float(l2), 'k_total': int(k_total),\n          'metric': metric, 'weights': 'mutual-rank 1/(1+ri+rj)', 'w_min': float(1.0 / (1.0 + 2.0 * max(1, k_total)))\n      }\n      return adata\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Default config aligned with EID 244 except for rank-weighted connectivities\n      return run_pipeline_ranked(adata,\n                                 n_pcs_emb=64, alpha=0.95,\n                                 n_pcs_graph=50, gamma_max=0.74, lam=0.9, l2=1e-3,\n                                 k_total=45, metric='cosine')\n\
    ```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-BRBG-Whitened: Rank-Weighted Balanced kNN (k=45)\"\ntags: \"dual, whitening, rank-weighted, balanced-knn, cosine\"\nabstract: \"Single-change variant of the 0.7296 SOTA: keep equal per-batch quotas and union edges, but set connectivities via mutual-rank weights w_ij = 1/(1 + rank_i(j) + rank_j(i)) (magnitude-free), with floor to preserve mixing. Hypothesis: improves ARI/NMI/ASW_label without harming mixing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.dual_whitened_adaptpc_rank import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
