thinking_content: "**Exploring analysis methods**\n\nI’ve realized that previous tests already utilized \"reapply HVG mask after ComBat before PCA,\" focusing on HVG-driven PCA. There's the thought of comparing \"PCA with randomized SVD vs. arpack,\" but that might not be necessary. \n\nAnother consideration is using graph-balanced neighbor selection for equal counts per batch, but what about balancing per batch and per cluster? Cluster-level balancing could complicate things, but it fosters mixing across pseudo-cell states. I’ll keep exploring these ideas, like balanced neighbor quotas and \"two-scale graph\" to improve Graph_conn.**Considering new metrics and steps**\n\nI'm exploring the idea of using a \"Cauchy-cosine metric,\" which could be robust against heavy tails, though I'm not sure it will change much. Given the need for parsimony, if results are negative, I should conclude the axis reweighting series and think through next principles before adding new code.\n\nI need to log results\
  \ and respond to the archive. I'll summarize the axis reweighting result, send a negative addendum, and then brainstorm next steps. The prompt suggests a minimal change like calibrating connectivities, but row-normalization might not apply here.**Analyzing metric adjustments**\n\nI'm noticing that many metrics depend on neighbor graph connectivity and distances rather than weights. Row-normalization seems to have altered relative weights, affecting iLISI, which is surprising. The quotas being used are important, and keeping things binary appears stable.\n\nAnother idea is to whiten embeddings to tau 0.95, but we may want to only whiten the top m principal components (PCs) to avoid noise amplification. Our best alpha was 0.7, giving a score of 0.7287. Maybe I should freeze the current state of the project and focus on publishing a matured pipeline document and replicability guidelines.**Considering score improvement strategies**\n\nThe score improvement has plateaued around 0.7296. I'm\
  \ thinking of a new idea that might help: using \"graph connectivity distances based on cosine distance with whitened embeddings\" to enhance mixing. However, neighbors in the embedding may be overshadowed by connectivities built from Zcorr.\n\nThere's also a thought about adjusting equal quotas based on batch sizes for fairness; proportional quotas degraded earlier, so maybe \"ceil-per-batch quotas\" could be better. That means more neighbors for similar batches to avoid forced edges that hinder iLISI or ASW_label. Lastly, maybe we should look into using adjacency weighting based on shared nearest neighbor counts within quotas while keeping things binary.**Finalizing actions and considerations**\n\nUsing shared nearest neighbor (SNN) counts could help maintain robust cross-batch edges, but since previous Gaussian weighting hurt mixing, I’m unsure it will improve iLISI. Given that modifications haven't yielded positive results, maybe it’s best to wrap this cycle and publish an analysis\
  \ addendum stating \"no further improvements found.\" \n\nI'll write a storage file summarizing EID 274 and reply to archive 7 with a negative addendum. We can log metrics and UUID in evals_274.md. For future reflections, the idea of \"diffusion-type integration\" sounds interesting but seems heavy right now, so I'll just plan to reflect on that later."
