role: model
parts:
- text: "Synthesis and concrete plan (no actions this turn)\n\nDecision: Try batch-center recentering in Zcorr first. It’s the simplest, label-free, batch-only adjustment that targets a plausible residual: per-batch mean shifts that remain after whitening and adaptive residualization. A small translation per batch preserves within-batch geometry but reduces inter-batch offsets, which can slightly improve label metrics without harming mixing.\n\nSpecification (single change; graph path only)\n- Context: Keep the current SOTA pipeline fixed (tau=0.95, PCA64 embedding, k=45 cosine equal-quotas graph, adaptive residualization with γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9, l2=1e-3).\n- Where: Apply recentering to the graph embedding Zcorr (50 PCs) after adaptive residualization but before building the balanced kNN graph.\n- Compute:\n  - Global mean μ = mean over all rows of Zcorr.\n  - For each batch b, batch mean μ_b = mean of Zcorr for cells in b.\n  - Offset δ_b = μ_b − μ.\n- Recenter:\n  - For each cell i in batch\
    \ b: Zcorr[i] ← Zcorr[i] − η·δ_b with η ∈ {0.05, 0.10}.\n- Build graph on this Zcorr (balanced quotas, binary connectivity). Embedding path (ComBat+PCA64+whitening) remains unchanged.\n\nWhy this should help\n- Translation per batch leaves all within-batch pairwise distances unchanged, so local structure (and thus ARI/ASW_label within each batch) is not distorted.\n- Cross-batch distances shrink along residual offset directions, which can strengthen cross-batch neighbor selection already enforced by quotas, potentially improving label metrics slightly while keeping iLISI/kBET/ASW_batch near ceiling.\n- It fits the separation-of-concerns blueprint: we removed linear batch signal (residualization), standardized scales (whitening), enforced cross-batch locality (quotas), and now nudge residual means.\n\nAcceptance criteria (pre-registered)\n- Adopt η if:\n  - Mean score increases by ≥ 0.0005 over 0.7296, or\n  - Mean is within ±0.0002 but ARI/NMI/Cell_cycle improve with no drop > 0.002\
    \ in iLISI/kBET/ASW_batch or Graph_conn.\n- Otherwise revert to η=0 (current default).\n\nFailure signals and rollback\n- Any noticeable drop in mixing (iLISI/kBET/ASW_batch) or Graph_conn beyond threshold → reject.\n- If η=0.10 is worse or neutral, try η=0.05 only; no further expansion unless justified.\n\nDocumentation and analysis to log\n- For each η, record EID, UUID, and full normalized metrics.\n- Compute and log ||δ_b||2 per batch pre/post recentering and the fraction of nodes whose cross-batch neighbor count changes (sanity check).\n- Add a brief addendum to the archive capsule with outcomes."
