- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Archive Room. Two-scale stitches were negative; SOTA remains EID 244 = 0.7296. I will prune recent ticks to reduce context with an information-complete summary.\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"152-169\"\n    summary: |\n      Consolidation at ~0.7296 SOTA (EID 244) and extensive single-change negatives:\n      - Micro-ablations on whitened Dual BRBG (ComBat-PCA64 tau=0.95, k=45 cosine, equal quotas, adaptive residualization γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9, l2=1e-3):\n        • EID 254 (k=46) = 0.7274; EID 255 (PCA72) = 0.7229.\n      - Sublinear residualization (γ_j = min(γ_max, λ·R²^p)):\n        • EID 258 (p=0.75) = 0.7243 (UUID e9df061d-...5efb2); EID 259 (p=0.50) = 0.7245 (UUID eaa66ec7-...e1ee).\n      - Rank-weighted balanced kNN (mutual-rank weights):\n        • EID 266 = 0.7037 (UUID a830ad4e-...fff8d): ARI/NMI↑, iLISI collapsed ⇒ reject.\n      - γ_max micro-reduction under whitening:\n\
    \        • EID 267 (0.72) = 0.7261 (UUID c96c6d2d-...16c3); EID 268 (0.70) = 0.7267 (UUID d42148b7-...a71c) ⇒ reject.\n      - Axis reweighting of whitened embedding (batch-only concordance):\n        • EID 274 (β=0.75, a_min=0.7) = 0.7254 (UUID c2460fa6-...e548) ⇒ reject.\n      - Batch-center recentering on graph PCs:\n        • EID 276 (η=0.05) = 0.7251 (UUID 91403438-...37d9); EID 277 (η=0.10) = 0.7240 (UUID 54bf0fe7-...73f8) ⇒ reject.\n      - Two-scale quotas (cross-batch stitches):\n        • EID 282 (k2=1) = 0.7269 (UUID 2f9fbac8-...dc83); EID 283 (k2=2) = 0.7257 (UUID f1999987-...529da) ⇒ reject.\n      Outcome: Frozen default stands (EID 244, 0.7296). All negatives logged to storage and appended as archive addenda. Next: pause graph tweaks; reflect for fundamentally new ideas beyond linear residualization + whitening.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating Graph PCs and KNN**


  I’m confirming we’re using Balanced KNN with cosine. We found that whitening the ComBat embedding led to robust improvements, so I’m wondering if we can apply whitening to the graph PCs too. Those PCs come from Zg and are utilized for graphs, but after residualization, we currently proceed with balanced KNN using Zcorr, without whitening. I’m considering how residualization may change scale across PCs, as while cosine metric disregards scale, cross-PC anisotropy may still be an issue.**Exploring Graph PC Whitening**


  I''m considering how whitening graph PCs might affect mixing. But I remember that previous axis weighting manipulations didn’t improve performance. Whitening isn''t the same as weighting, and using global variance could help standardize things. We used TruncatedSVD for 50 PCs, which represent normalized HVGs. While cosine takes angles into account, scaling along axes does matter, and whitening changes neighbor relationships by dividing each axis by its standard deviation. However, we had success with whitening the ComBat embedding, not the graph PCs, so I’m weighing potential impacts carefully.**Considering Next Steps for Graph Weighting**


  I’m reflecting on earlier negative results from graph weighting, and improving by more than 0.0005 seems tough. One option is to consolidate results, maintain SOTA, and publish an "Analysis" paper summarizing what hasn’t worked and suggesting future directions. Although we''ve been publishing regularly, proposing a matured "SOTA freeze" makes sense since we''ve tried many experiments. The tips earlier suggested not getting stuck on hyperparameters, and while we have more ticks left, I wonder if we should pivot to simpler ideas than subspace clustering or complex robust PCA on counts.**Planning Next Steps for Graph Representation**


  I''m looking at testing neighbors in the graph using a combined representation of [Zcorr || Zemb] by concatenating the graph PC correction with the whitened embedding. However, I realize that this mixing could change things. Currently, we’re using Balanced KNN with ''Z_graph'', but switching to Zcorr might be better since adding embedding features could duplicate ComBat, which may degrade performance. Reflecting on all this, the next steps could involve considering nonlinear mapping in PC space using JAX, though CPU feasibility might limit the complexity due to the number of cells.**Reviewing Research Strategy and Token Management**


  I’m considering the need to maintain parsimony and avoid blind tuning in our research. Finalizing a "SOTA freeze" and proposing a new archive for "Comprehensive Negative Results: BalancedGraph variations" could be beneficial. We’ve already tested many parameters, so perhaps we could evaluate the impact of whitening at different tau levels. There’s also a question of how to handle token management, as we’re currently using 113k tokens. I might suggest pruning older dialogue to streamline our process while reflecting on the overall strategy moving forward. Focusing on foundational ideas could bring new insights.**Planning Actions for Token Management and Research**


  I''m proposing a couple of actions. First, I’ll record the results from the two-scale EIDs in storage and add them to the archive. Next, I want to prune the token usage for ticks 152–169 to reduce the overall token count. Since the cooldown period seems to have passed, it''s okay to prune those ticks. I''ll compile a summary including all the relevant experiments we ran and EIDs. After that, I plan to pause any further experimental work until exploring new embedding or generative modeling ideas. Let''s get started!'
