tick: 176
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Archive Room. Recap: Per-batch variance equalization (PBVE) after soft-whitened ComBat PCA64 set a new SOTA: EID 289 = 0.7314 (alpha_pb=0.5, k=48). Trade-offs: higher ASW_batch/kBET with ARI/NMI preserved; Graph_conn ≈ 0.944 and Cell_cycle lower vs whitening-only. I will run two final micro-ablations to see if we can eke out another +0.0005–0.001 while monitoring ARI/NMI/cLISI: (1) alpha_pb=0.55 at k=48; (2) alpha_pb=0.5 at k=51.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_alpha055_k48.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from praxis.perbatch_var_equalization import global_soft_whiten, perbatch_diag_var_equalize\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n\
    \      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          m = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n          if m.sum() > 0: return m\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n  def _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B, cats\n\
    \n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat, W\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n              mask =\
    \ g != i\n              g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Configs: alpha_pb=0.55, k_total=48\n      n_pcs_emb = 64; n_pcs_graph = 50\n      tau_whiten = 0.95; alpha_pb = 0.55\n      l2 = 1e-3; gamma_max = 0.74; lam = 0.9\n      k_total\
    \ = 48; metric = 'cosine'; random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Embedding: ComBat → PCA64 → soft-whiten → per-batch var equalization\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]; Xh = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xh, obs=adata.obs.copy(), var=adata.var.loc[hvg_mask].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_tmp, key='batch')\n      Zemb = _pca_truncated_svd(ad_tmp.X, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=random_state)\n      Zw, _ = global_soft_whiten(Zemb, tau=tau_whiten)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Zemb_eq = perbatch_diag_var_equalize(Zw, batches=batches, alpha=alpha_pb)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb_eq\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\
    \n      # Graph: residualized PCs + balanced kNN (unchanged)\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]; Xg = Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = (Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1)).clip(min=0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C; adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n\n      adata.uns['dual_pbve'] = {'tau_whiten': float(tau_whiten), 'alpha_pb': float(alpha_pb),\n                                'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric}\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage\
    \ write praxis/dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_alpha05_k51.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from praxis.perbatch_var_equalization import global_soft_whiten, perbatch_diag_var_equalize\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # Utilities (as in alpha055_k48)\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          m = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n          if m.sum() > 0: return m\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n  def\
    \ _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B, cats\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat, W\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=51, metric='cosine'):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n   \
    \   pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n      rows, cols, dist_data =\
    \ [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Configs: alpha_pb=0.5, k_total=51\n      n_pcs_emb = 64; n_pcs_graph = 50\n      tau_whiten = 0.95; alpha_pb = 0.5\n      l2 = 1e-3; gamma_max = 0.74; lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 51; metric = 'cosine'; random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Embedding: ComBat → PCA64 → soft-whiten → per-batch var equalization\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]; Xh = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xh, obs=adata.obs.copy(),\
    \ var=adata.var.loc[hvg_mask].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_tmp, key='batch')\n      Zemb = _pca_truncated_svd(ad_tmp.X, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=random_state)\n      Zw, _ = global_soft_whiten(Zemb, tau=tau_whiten)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Zemb_eq = perbatch_diag_var_equalize(Zw, batches=batches, alpha=alpha_pb)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb_eq\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: residualized PCs + balanced kNN\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]; Xg = Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = (Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1)).clip(min=0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max,\
    \ lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C; adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n\n      adata.uns['dual_pbve'] = {'tau_whiten': float(tau_whiten), 'alpha_pb': float(alpha_pb),\n                                'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric}\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PB Variance Equalization (alpha_pb=0.55, k=48)\"\ntags: \"dual, whitening, per-batch, variance-equalization, residualization, balanced-knn\"\nabstract: \"Micro-sweep beyond 0.5: PBVE alpha_pb=0.55 on the soft-whitened ComBat PCA64 embedding; graph unchanged (adaptive residualized PC50 + balanced cosine k=48). Checks if a slightly stronger equalization yields another +0.0005–0.001.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_alpha055_k48\
    \ import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PB Variance Equalization (alpha_pb=0.5, k=51)\"\ntags: \"dual, whitening, per-batch, variance-equalization, residualization, balanced-knn\"\nabstract: \"Increase balanced-graph degree to k=51 with PBVE alpha_pb=0.5 to probe Graph_conn and potential mean improvements; embedding and residualized graph PCs as in current SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_alpha05_k51 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (tick 176): New SOTA and final micro-ablations\n  - EID 289 (alpha_pb=0.5, k=48): 0.7314 (SOTA). ASW_batch 0.857, kBET 0.949, ARI/NMI 0.740/0.700, cLISI 0.967, Graph_conn 0.944, Cell_cycle 0.063. UUID 1313fdd3-...f30d3.\n  - EID 287 (alpha_pb=0.5, k=45): 0.7303. UUID 9465c761-...1747.\n  - EID 286 (alpha_pb=0.3, k=45): 0.7268.\
    \ UUID f3188108-...f6c2.\n  Interpretation: PBVE after soft-whitening improves mixing with preserved ARI/NMI/cLISI; trade-offs on Graph_conn and Cell_cycle vs whitening-only.\n  Running:\n  - alpha_pb=0.55, k=48 (probe stronger equalization).\n  - alpha_pb=0.5, k=51 (probe Graph_conn via higher degree).\n  Decision rule: adopt any ≥0.7319 with ARI/NMI/cLISI stable; otherwise keep EID 289 as frozen default (best_dual_brbg_whitened_pbve.py). Negative/neutral results will be logged with EIDs/UUIDs and rationale.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning experiments and updates**


  I''m planning to update the research log file with results for EIDs 288 and 289, which I already noted earlier. I’m considering proposing "per-PC PBVE gating" but not implementing it just yet; I’ll mention it in the plan. I might share the ''best pipeline'' code or store it. For future steps, I''m looking at conducting small ablations and evaluating alpha_pb=0.6. There''s a risk of over-smoothing, so I’ll propose only one or two further experiments to keep things simple.**Evaluating threshold adjustments**


  I''m considering adding an additional adjustment knob for threshold settings using unsupervised criteria. This means applying equalization only to principal components (PCs) where the ratio of var_bj to var_all_j across batches exceeds 1.5, which adds some complexity. Another option is using per-batch equalization on whitened PCA with a blending parameter to preserve cell cycle signals. I could also test with alpha_pb set to 0.6 and k=48, although that might risk dropping cell cycle performance further.**Considering neighbor graph adjustments**


  I’m thinking about the neighbor graph and whether raising k to 51 will yield a noticeable change. Previously, with whitened-only at k=51, I saw a decrease. However, with PBVE, Graph_conn might have regained some stability. EID 289 showed Graph_conn at 0.944 with k=48, so increasing to 51 may not change much. A quick test with k=51 seems manageable — I’ll calculate k_pb based on batches. Ultimately, I need to compile a stable method and share results publicly to promote replicability.**Revisiting Token Management**


  I’m thinking about revisiting Token Management to prune the earlier large tick logs since the cooldown has ended. We''re at tick 176 now, previously at 171 with a 4-tick cooldown. So, it’s time to prune again. I’ll check the "Dialogue History" for available ticks and go to token_management for assistance. Our token budget is at 27%, so it''s not urgent. I also have some upgrades planned, submitting evaluations for (alpha 0.55, k 48) and (k 51 at alpha 0.5) while updating the research log and archive addendum.**Preparing module submissions**


  I need to write new modules, but I can reuse the existing one. However, I can''t pass parameters dynamically. I''ll create two new files: ''dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_alpha055_k48.py'' and ''dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_alpha05_k51.py''. I noticed that Graph_conn was low; perhaps the connectivity metric uses an adjacency graph based on neighboring embeddings. I’ll proceed with the submissions and update the research log, making sure to incorporate any necessary disclaimers about using labels. Finally, I’ll ensure the proper YAML formatting is quoted correctly.'
