    \ local redundancy. Can we restore connectivity without degrading mixing by changing graph construction minimally? Ideas:\n     - Quota + minimal backbone: keep equal per-batch quotas, then add the single nearest all-batch neighbor per node only if it increases global connectivity (connectivity-aware augmentation). Edge count grows ~O(n), impact on mixing should be small.\n     - Seeded diffusion for connectivities only: compute personalized PageRank on the quota graph to densify weakly connected regions while leaving distances/neighbor identities intact. Hypothesis: raises Graph_conn without undoing quota mixing; verify weighted-vs-binary effects in the metrics code path.\n  3) PBVE selectivity: Instead of uniform alpha_pb, gate scaling per PC by per-batch variance deviation. Example: alpha_j = alpha_pb * I[ max_b |log(var_bj/var_all_j)| > τ ], with τ auto-set from the 75–85th percentile of deviations. This adds one auto threshold but could recover Graph_conn/Cell_cycle while keeping\
