tick: 180
role: model
parts:
- text: "Implementation sketches, expected effects, and risk controls\n\n1) Linear shared-subspace (multi-set CCA/GCCA) embedding\n- Implementation (sum-correlations GCCA, label-free):\n  - Precompute per-batch PCs: For each batch b, take Z_b ∈ R^{n_b×d} (e.g., d=64) from ComBat+PCA; center each Z_b.\n  - Whiten each Z_b: Ẑ_b = Z_b Σ_b^{-1/2} via EVD of Cov(Z_b)+εI (ε≈1e-6).\n  - Build block covariance S = ∑_{p≠q} (Ẑ_p^T Ẑ_q)/(√(n_p n_q)) and D = blkdiag(I_d,...,I_d).\n  - Solve generalized eigenproblem S v = λ D v with ridge on S if needed (S←S+ρI, ρ≈1e-4). v partitions into {v_b} for each batch.\n  - Project each sample x_b to shared space: y = Ẑ_b v_b (pick top m comps, m≈32 or 48). Concatenate all batches’ y to form X_emb.\n- Why this could help: explicitly maximizes cross-batch correlation for shared axes (biology); should raise ARI/NMI/ASW_label and potentially Cell_cycle (if cycles are shared), while quotas in the graph preserve iLISI/kBET.\n- Guardrails:\n  - Keep d,m modest;\
    \ enforce per-batch whitening (prevents dominance by larger batches).\n  - Compare vs tau=0.95 PBVE embedding; adopt only if mean ≥+0.001 and ARI/NMI/cLISI non-decreasing.\n\n2) Connectivity restoration with minimal change\n- Quota + minimal backbone (cluster-bridge variant):\n  - Build our balanced quota graph C (binary).\n  - Cluster X_emb with MiniBatchKMeans (k_c≈64; small, robust).\n  - For each cluster, add a single within-cluster 1-NN per node (only if the edge doesn’t already exist). Keep edges binary. This adds ≤1 intra-cluster edge per node, tending to connect same-type neighborhoods without knowing labels.\n  - Expected: Graph_conn ↑ toward ~0.96 with negligible mixing loss (clusters span batches, so added edges are not purely same-batch).\n- Alternative backbone: global 1-NN augmentation\n  - For each node, add the nearest neighbor in X_emb irrespective of batch (if not already connected). This ensures a weak global backbone; lower impact but simpler.\n- Seeded diffusion\
    \ (fallback):\n  - Personalized PageRank on C to produce weighted connectivities C’ = α(I−(1−α)P)^{-1} with teleport α≈0.15; keep distances unchanged.\n  - Risk: weighted edges previously underperformed; if used, binarize after diffusion by keeping top-k incoming weights per node to preserve structure.\n\n3) PBVE selectivity (auto-gated per PC)\n- Compute deviation d_j = max_b |log(var_bj/var_all_j)| on whitened PCs.\n- Auto-threshold τ = quantile(d, q=0.80). Define α_j = α_pb if d_j > τ else 0 (α_pb=0.5).\n- Apply per-batch scaling only on PCs with α_j>0:\n  Z_b[:, j] ← (Z_b[:, j] − μ_j)·(var_all_j/var_bj)^{α_j/2} + μ_j\n- Expected: keep ASW_batch/kBET gains; recover some Cell_cycle and Graph_conn; aim for +0.0003–0.0007 mean. No new free knobs; τ is auto.\n\n4) HVG refinements (minimal, label-free)\n- Intersection-of-HVGs (IHVG):\n  - Run scanpy HVG with batch_key; if available, prefer adata.var['highly_variable_intersection']; else compute per-batch HVG masks and select genes with\
    \ frequency ≥ f (e.g., ≥2/4 batches), then take top 2000 by dispersion within that set.\n  - Expected: slight ARI/NMI/ASW_label ↑; mixing neutral.\n- Mean-shift pruning:\n  - On normalized/log1p, compute SSB and SSW per gene; drop top q% genes by SSB/(SSB+SSW) (e.g., q=2.5–5%), then refill to 2000 by next best HVGs.\n  - Expected: stabilize Cell_cycle/ASW_label; minimal impact on mixing.\n\n5) GCCA + milder residualization on graph PCs\n- If GCCA reduces batch-predictability R² per PC, our adaptive γ_j will naturally shrink. Optionally cap γ_max at 0.70 (from 0.74) only if R² has broadly fallen; this can lift ASW_label/ARI without harming kBET due to quotas.\n\nPrioritized path (single-change trials)\n- T1: Cluster-bridge augmentation on current PBVE α=0.5, k=48. Success = Graph_conn ≥0.96, no loss in ARI/NMI/cLISI, mean ≥0.732.\n- T2: PBVE auto-gating (τ=80th percentile). Success = mean ≥0.7319 and Cell_cycle/Graph_conn non-decreasing vs EID 289.\n- T3: Mean-shift pruning for HVGs (q=0.03).\
    \ Success = ASW_label/Cell_cycle ↑ with mean non-decreasing.\n- T4: GCCA embedding (m≈32–48), graph unchanged. Success = ARI/NMI/ASW_label/Cell_cycle ↑, mean ≥0.732.\n\nOperational notes\n- Keep edges binary after any augmentation (weights previously hurt). Ensure added edges are symmetric.\n- Log all EIDs/UUIDs. Adopt only with ≥+0.001 or clear secondary-metric wins under guardrails."
thinking_content: "**Continuing reflection**\n\nI’m thinking about our current reflection session and how we need to avoid station actions during these ticks. It’s important to dive deep into the proposed ideas and focus on implementation details like theoretical expectations, risk management, and how metrics interact. I should also think through specific algorithms and some pseudocode, keeping in mind resource constraints, such as no GPU access and a half-hour time limit. I'll evaluate how metrics will utilize connectivity and distances, as earlier observations have shown that weighted graphs can perform worse than binary ones.**Analyzing graph connectivity**\n\nI’m considering how PPR on a binary graph could lead to a denser weighted graph while the distances stay the same. The Graph_conn metric typically looks at the fraction of nodes with connections across batches or just in the largest connected component. In OpenProblems v2, connectivity is often assessed based on nodes linked within\
  \ each cell type in the kNN graph. Weighted edges may not improve the situation, and reducing quotas could decrease Graph_conn again. There’s an idea for a minimal backbone to ensure complete connectivity using MST edges across all cells.**Reflecting on connectivity metrics**\n\nI’m looking into previous metrics for graph connectivity, where connectivities are tested within label connectivity. The challenge is that we can't actually use labels since they're computed internally. Graph_conn was high before with equal quotas, sitting at 0.972, and balanced quotas even reached 0.980. Now, after PBVE, it dropped to 0.944, possibly due to changes in the embedding becoming more isotropic. Balanced quotas aim for equal distribution per batch, which might lead to certain rare cells having fewer connections, and a minimal backbone may help connect components.**Exploring graph connectivity without labels**\n\nI'm realizing that without labels, my goals become tricky, especially for connectivity metrics.\
  \ While using Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) on distances might enhance Graph_conn across subgraphs, the label-specified metrics may not see improvement if the edges aren’t aligned with those labels. True biological neighborhoods could benefit from adding nearest neighbor edges across batches, but this could also decrease cLISI. Currently, Graph_conn is around 0.944, indicating it's not disconnected, but I need to ensure connectivity remains within the same cell types. Overall, adding edges to nearest neighbors may not directly help Graph_conn.**Contemplating graph connectivity and methods**\n\nIt seems Graph_conn may have decreased due to embedding equalization compressing clusters, leading to fewer in-type edges. A solution could be to use a slightly higher k value—previously tested at k=51, which provided a minor increase in Graph_conn. I’m considering how seeded diffusion or PPR might boost connectivity weights but remembering Graph_conn deals with unweighted connections. I'll then discuss\
  \ specific implementations like GCCA and MCCA while ensuring we maintain a linear complexity for larger datasets, carefully structuring my plans as I evaluate the potential effects on metrics like ARI/NMI and Graph_conn improvements.**Reviewing implementation and metrics**\n\nI'm analyzing how normalization impacts measurement, particularly Graph_conn values for different EIDs, noticing a range difference of -0.028. Improving Graph_conn to 0.96 could incrementally raise performance, so I'd like to implement a \"quota + minimal backbone\" approach. This involves building a Balanced Graph and considering cluster-based connections to approximate labels without directly using them. \n\nI’ll provide pseudocode for the cluster-backbone, suggesting parameters like l=1 and ensuring to add edges that limit extra connections. Lastly, I need to draft reflection tick content and propose testing methods for gene selection."
