- text: "Closing synthesis and concrete next steps\n\nWhat likely moves the needle next\n- Connectivity, not mixing, is the bottleneck after PBVE. The quota graph is deliberately sparse and cross-batch; per-batch equalization reduced redundant local links, nudging Graph_conn down. A minimal, structure-aware densification that keeps edges binary and balanced is the safest way to regain Graph_conn without harming iLISI/kBET.\n- Uniform PBVE (α_pb=0.5) helped mixing but slightly depressed Cell_cycle/Graph_conn. Targeting only discrepant PCs should retain mixing gains while reducing side effects.\n\nTwo minimal, single-change designs to try first\n1) Cluster-bridge augmentation (graph-only; binary; label-free):\n   - Space: Zcorr (graph PCs after adaptive residualization), metric: cosine.\n   - Steps:\n     1) KMeans on Zcorr (k_c≈64, fixed seed).\n     2) For each cluster c:\n        - Take nodes I_c; extract subgraph C[I_c] from the balanced quota graph.\n        - If subgraph has >1 component,\
    \ build a simple spanning tree over components (via nearest-pair distances in Zcorr) and add exactly one binary edge per tree edge (symmetric) using the closest cross-component node pair. Record corresponding distances in D.\n   - Rationale: Repairs micro-fragmentation within locally coherent regions without biasing toward same-batch or reweighting magnitudes.\n   - Success gate: Graph_conn ≥ 0.96 with ARI/NMI/cLISI non-decreasing; mean ≥ 0.732. If neutral, try the even simpler “global 1-NN augmentation” (add each node’s single nearest Zcorr neighbor if absent) as a fallback.\n\n2) PBVE auto-gating (embedding-only; no new manual knob):\n   - In the soft-whitened ComBat PCA64 space, compute per-PC deviation d_j = max_b |log(var_bj/var_all_j)|.\n   - Robust auto-threshold τ (e.g., median(d) + 1.5·MAD or 80th percentile). Set α_j = 0.5 if d_j > τ else 0, then apply per-batch scaling only on gated PCs.\n   - Expected: Retain ASW_batch/kBET; recover some Cell_cycle/Graph_conn; aim for +0.0003–0.0007\
    \ mean without regressions.\n   - Success gate: mean ≥ 0.7319 and Cell_cycle/Graph_conn non-decreasing vs EID 289; ARI/NMI/cLISI unchanged or better.\n\nLow-touch HVG refinement (third, if needed)\n- Mean-shift pruning: On normalized/log1p, compute SSB/(SSB+SSW) per gene, drop top 3% most batch-shifted, refill to 2000 with next-best HVGs. Expected small ASW_label/Cell_cycle gains; mixing neutral. Adopt only if mean non-decreasing.\n\nShared-subspace alignment (defer; higher complexity)\n- Avoid classical multiset CCA (needs correspondences). Two viable label-free linear options:\n  - Covariance barycenter basis over batches (principled pooled PCA).\n  - Centroid-aligned Procrustes in whitened ComBat space (match batchwise centroids; orthogonal maps).\n- Pair with current graph (adaptive γ_j naturally shrinks if batch R² falls). Adopt only with ≥ +0.001 mean and no biology regressions.\n\nDiagnostics and guardrails (label-free)\n- Connectivity: component count, size of second-largest\
    \ component, Laplacian λ2, added-edge count per node.\n- PBVE gating: fraction of PCs gated, distribution of d_j, naive kNN cross-batch fraction in X_emb (should stay high).\n- HVGs: distribution of SSB/(SSB+SSW) before/after; ensure diversity.\n- Always keep edges binary and symmetric; avoid weighted connectivities unless binarized afterward.\n\nDecision discipline\n- Single-change trials only; log EIDs/UUIDs and negatives.\n- Adopt changes only if they meet the explicit gates above. Otherwise, keep EID 289 (0.7314) frozen and pivot to a fundamentally different, still-parsimonious idea."
