tick: 183
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, in the Research Counter. Recap: New SOTA remains EID 289 = 0.7314 (PBVE α=0.5, k=48). Follow-ups: Cluster-bridge graph augmentation was neutral (EID 307 = 0.7309). PBVE auto-gating was negative (EID 308 = 0.7255). Mean-shift HVG pruning (q=3%) is running (EID 311).\n\nI’ll launch one more conservative HVG-pruning variant (q=2%) while 311 runs, to probe if lighter pruning improves Cell_cycle/ASW_label without harming the mean.\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_hvgms02_k48.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  from praxis.hvg_meanshift_prune import compute_hvg_meanshift_mask\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum,\
    \ inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B, cats\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat, W\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      k_pb = max(1,\
    \ int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      if not pairs_min_dist:\
    \ return None, None\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Dual BRBG with soft-whitened ComBat PCA64 + PBVE (alpha=0.5) and balanced kNN (k=48),\n      using mean-shift HVG pruning with prune_frac=0.02.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Configs\n      base_n = 2000\n      buffer = 300\n      prune_frac = 0.02\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      tau_whiten = 0.95\n      alpha_pb = 0.5\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\
    \      hvg_mask = compute_hvg_meanshift_mask(adata, batch_key='batch', base_n=base_n, buffer=buffer, prune_frac=prune_frac)\n      if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n          hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding: ComBat → PCA64 → soft-whiten → PBVE alpha=0.5\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      Xh = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xh, obs=adata.obs.copy(), var=adata.var.loc[hvg_mask].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_tmp, key='batch')\n      Zemb = _pca_truncated_svd(ad_tmp.X, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=random_state)\n\n      Zc = Zemb - Zemb.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      Ccov = (Zc.T @ Zc) / max(1, Zc.shape[0] - 1)\n      S, U = np.linalg.eigh(Ccov)\n      S = np.maximum(S, 0.0)\n      S_pow = np.power(S + 1e-8, -0.5 * tau_whiten)\n      T = (U * S_pow) @ U.T\n      Zw = Zc @ T\n\n      var_all = Zw.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      Zemb_eq = Zw.copy()\n\
    \      for b in np.unique(batches):\n          idx = (batches == b)\n          Zb = Zw[idx, :]\n          var_b = Zb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n          s = np.power(var_all / var_b, 0.5 * alpha_pb)\n          Zemb_eq[idx, :] = Zb * s\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb_eq\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: PCA50 → residualize (adaptive γ) → balanced kNN k=48\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      Xg = Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = (Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1)).clip(min=0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32),\
    \ batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PBVE 0.5 with Mean-Shift HVG Pruning (q=2%, k=48)\"\ntags: \"dual, hvg, mean-shift, pbve, whitening, balanced-knn\"\nabstract: \"Conservative HVG refinement: drop top 2% most batch-shifted genes by SSB/(SSB+SSW), refill to 2000, then run PBVE α=0.5 embedding and residualized PC50 + balanced cosine kNN (k=48). Goal: improve ASW_label/Cell_cycle without lowering the mean.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_hvgms02_k48 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (tick 183): Added conservative HVG mean-shift pruning variant\n  - Running EID 311 (q=3%) and new submission (q=2%) to\
    \ test if lighter pruning improves ASW_label/Cell_cycle while keeping the mean ≥ EID 289=0.7314.\n  - If both are neutral/negative, retain EID 289 as frozen default and pivot to fundamentally different embeddings only if they meet adoption gates (≥+0.001 mean without biology regressions).\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering experiment scheduling**


  I’m wondering if we could schedule more experiments since I can run up to two concurrent evaluations, but it looks like we don’t have any running right now. The table confirms that evaluation 311 is actively running, so we could submit one more experiment. The component-bridge augmentation variant might be easier to implement than the cluster-bridge, especially since the Graph_conn metric didn’t improve before. I need to be cautious with this single change regarding edges.**Exploring experiment options**


  Earlier, it seemed increasing k from 48 to 51 didn’t yield much improvement. The 1-NN augmentation adds k+1 edges per node, but it may not be very balanced across batches. We need to be careful with our two concurrent experiments since there’s only one slot available. I’m thinking about creating a variant for "global 1-NN augmentation on Zcorr after PBVE 0.5 with balanced k=48." This might help improve Graph_conn more effectively than the other approaches.**Evaluating experiment changes**


  Reflecting on the gating idea, it seems the cluster-bridge approach didn''t improve Graph_conn, and the augmentation wasn''t helpful. It might be worth testing HVG mean-shift for ASW_label/Cell_cycle with q=2%, so I’ll set this as the second experiment to run. I''ll prepare a storage file for the experiment along with a YAML file that references earlier modules but adjusts prune_frac. I need to document all planned experiments in the research log, but I''ll wait for results before logging them officially.'
