parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 184\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 103,299 / 270,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 184 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PBVE 0.5 with Mean-Shift HVG Pruning (q=3%, k=48)' (ID: 311) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7110727773000057\n**ASW_batch:** 0.856\n**ASW_label:** 0.160\n**ARI:** 0.657\n**NMI:** 0.667\n**Graph_conn:** 0.945\n**kBET:** 0.854\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.070\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.856  ASW_label:\
    \ 0.160  ARI: 0.657  NMI: 0.667\n  Graph_conn: 0.945  kBET: 0.854  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.070\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.919077  ASW_label: 0.503810  ARI: 0.656727  NMI: 0.666918\n  Graph_conn: 0.945805  kBET: 0.814377  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.990433\n  PCR: 0.999850  Cell_cycle: 0.068856\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 311\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code was successfully fixed and is now running without crashing. The evaluation has been running for over 5 minutes without errors.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported a function from `storage/praxis/hvg_meanshift_prune.py` that contained a bug. Specifically, the function `compute_hvg_meanshift_mask()` was trying to access a column called `'dispersions_norm'` that doesn't exist when using Scanpy's `flavor='seurat_v3'` for highly variable gene selection.\n\n**The bug (line 52 of hvg_meanshift_prune.py):**\n```python\ndisp = adata.var['dispersions_norm'].to_numpy()\n\
    ```\n\n**The issue:**\n- When `sc.pp.highly_variable_genes()` is called with `flavor='seurat_v3'`, it creates columns: `variances`, `variances_norm`, `highly_variable_rank`, etc.\n- The column `dispersions_norm` only exists for the `seurat` flavor (NOT `seurat_v3`)\n- The code was using the wrong column name for the Seurat v3 flavor\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the column name from `'dispersions_norm'` to `'variances_norm'` to match what Scanpy actually creates when using the Seurat v3 flavor:\n\n**Fixed code (submission_v2.py, line 53):**\n```python\ndisp = adata.var['variances_norm'].to_numpy()\n```\n\nAdditionally, I copied the entire `compute_hvg_meanshift_mask()` function and its helper functions (`_sum0`, `_sumsq0`, `_ssb_ssw`) into the submission file, applied the fix, and updated the main `eliminate_batch_effect_fn()` to use the corrected version.\n\n## Result\n- The code now runs without the `KeyError: 'dispersions_norm'` exception\n- The evaluation has been running successfully\
    \ for over 5 minutes\n- The batch integration algorithm is executing as intended with the mean-shift HVG pruning working correctly\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\nfrom praxis.dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_hvgms_k48 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as _original_eliminate_batch_effect_fn\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# Fixed version of compute_hvg_meanshift_mask\ndef _sum0(X):\n    return np.asarray(X.sum(axis=0)).ravel() if sp.issparse(X) else X.sum(axis=0)\n\ndef _sumsq0(X):\n    if sp.issparse(X):\n        X2 = X.multiply(X)\n        return np.asarray(X2.sum(axis=0)).ravel()\n    else:\n        return np.einsum('ij,ij->j', X, X)\n\ndef _ssb_ssw(X, batches):\n    \"\"\"Compute SSB and SSW per gene on normalized/log1p\
    \ X.\"\"\"\n    n, p = X.shape\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    sum_all = _sum0(X); sumsq_all = _sumsq0(X)\n    mu_all = sum_all / max(1, n)\n    var_all = np.maximum(0.0, sumsq_all / max(1, n) - mu_all**2)\n\n    SSB = np.zeros(p, dtype=np.float64)\n    SSW = np.zeros(p, dtype=np.float64)\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        nb = int(idx.size)\n        if nb == 0:\n            continue\n        Xb = X[idx, :]\n        sum_b = _sum0(Xb); sumsq_b = _sumsq0(Xb)\n        mu_b = sum_b / max(1, nb)\n        var_b = np.maximum(0.0, sumsq_b / max(1, nb) - mu_b**2)\n        SSB += nb * (mu_b - mu_all)**2\n        SSW += (nb - 1) * var_b\n    return SSB, SSW\n\ndef compute_hvg_meanshift_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, batch_key='batch', base_n=2000, buffer=300, prune_frac=0.03):\n    \"\"\"\n    Label-free HVG refinement:\n    1) Run Seurat v3 HVG with batch_key to get (base_n + buffer) candidates (ranked by variances_norm).\n    2) Take the top base_n, compute per-gene\
    \ g = SSB/(SSB+SSW) on normalized/log1p X.\n    3) Drop the top prune_frac fraction by g (most batch-shifted), and refill from the next-ranked candidates to keep base_n genes.\n    Returns boolean mask of length n_vars with exactly base_n True.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert batch_key in adata.obs, \"batch key missing\"\n    n_vars = adata.n_vars\n    # HVG candidates with buffer\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key=batch_key, n_top_genes=min(base_n + buffer, n_vars), inplace=True)\n    # Rank by normalized variance descending (seurat_v3 uses variances_norm, not dispersions_norm)\n    disp = adata.var['variances_norm'].to_numpy()\n    order = np.argsort(disp)[::-1]\n    cand = order[:min(base_n + buffer, n_vars)]\n\n    # Initial top base_n set\n    top_init = cand[:min(base_n, cand.size)]\n\n    # Compute SSB/(SSB+SSW) on normalized/log1p matrix (expect upstream normalization applied)\n    X = adata.X\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs[batch_key].astype('category').values)\n\
    \    SSB, SSW = _ssb_ssw(X, batches)\n    denom = np.maximum(SSB + SSW, 1e-8)\n    g = SSB / denom\n\n    # Among top_init, identify worst (highest g)\n    drop_k = max(1, int(round(prune_frac * base_n)))\n    worst_idx = np.argsort(g[top_init])[::-1][:drop_k]\n    to_drop = set(top_init[worst_idx].tolist())\n\n    # Refill from the remaining candidates beyond the first base_n\n    refill = []\n    for j in cand[base_n:]:\n        if j in to_drop:\n            continue\n        refill.append(j)\n        if len(refill) >= drop_k:\n            break\n\n    # Construct final selection\n    keep_list = [j for j in top_init if j not in to_drop]\n    keep_list += refill\n    if len(keep_list) < min(base_n, cand.size):\n        # If not enough refill available (rare), backfill from the rest of genes by dispersion\n        for j in order:\n            if j in keep_list or j in to_drop:\n                continue\n            keep_list.append(j)\n            if len(keep_list) >= base_n:\n    \
    \            break\n\n    keep_list = keep_list[:base_n]\n    mask = np.zeros(n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    mask[np.array(keep_list, dtype=int)] = True\n    return mask\n\n# Main function with fixed HVG computation\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Dual BRBG with soft-whitened ComBat PCA64 embedding + PBVE (alpha=0.5) and balanced kNN graph (k=48),\n    using mean-shift HVG pruning (drop top 3% most batch-shifted genes, refill to 2000).\n    \"\"\"\n    from praxis.dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_hvgms_k48 import (\n        _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n        _pca_truncated_svd,\n        _one_hot_batches,\n        _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n        _build_balanced_knn\n    )\n\n    # Configs\n    base_n = 2000\n    buffer = 300\n    prune_frac = 0.03\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    tau_whiten = 0.95\n    alpha_pb = 0.5\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n \
    \   assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize and compute HVG mask with mean-shift pruning (FIXED VERSION)\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    hvg_mask = compute_hvg_meanshift_mask(adata, batch_key='batch', base_n=base_n, buffer=buffer, prune_frac=prune_frac)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Embedding: ComBat on HVGs → PCA64 → soft-whiten → PBVE alpha=0.5\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    Xh = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xh, obs=adata.obs.copy(), var=adata.var.loc[hvg_mask].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_tmp, key='batch')\n    Zemb = _pca_truncated_svd(ad_tmp.X, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=random_state)\n\n    # Soft-whiten\n    Zc = Zemb - Zemb.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    Ccov = (Zc.T @ Zc) / max(1, Zc.shape[0] - 1)\n    S, U = np.linalg.eigh(Ccov)\n \
    \   S = np.maximum(S, 0.0)\n    S_pow = np.power(S + 1e-8, -0.5 * tau_whiten)\n    T = (U * S_pow) @ U.T\n    Zw = Zc @ T\n\n    # PBVE alpha=0.5\n    var_all = Zw.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    Zemb_eq = Zw.copy()\n    for b in np.unique(batches):\n        idx = (batches == b)\n        Zb = Zw[idx, :]\n        var_b = Zb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n        s = np.power(var_all / var_b, 0.5 * alpha_pb)\n        Zemb_eq[idx, :] = Zb * s\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb_eq\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph: PCA50 on HVGs → residualize (adaptive γ) → balanced kNN k=48\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    Xg = Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = (Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1)).clip(min=0.0)\n \
    \   R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/18a82a6a-ec57-4203-8a3c-aa22862f4435/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 18a82a6a-ec57-4203-8a3c-aa22862f4435\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343:\
    \ RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write praxis/dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_hvgms02_k48.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage write praxis/research_log.md` (in Research Counter); YAML\
