- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 185\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 110,010 / 270,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 185 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PBVE 0.5 with Mean-Shift HVG Pruning (q=2%, k=48)' (ID: 314) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7223504349635625\n**ASW_batch:** 0.855\n**ASW_label:** 0.160\n**ARI:** 0.741\n**NMI:** 0.700\n**Graph_conn:** 0.945\n**kBET:** 0.855\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.066\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.855  ASW_label: 0.160  ARI: 0.741  NMI: 0.700\n  Graph_conn: 0.945  kBET: 0.855  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.066\n\
    \nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.918594  ASW_label: 0.503754  ARI: 0.740548  NMI: 0.700251\n  Graph_conn: 0.946219  kBET: 0.814671  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.990414\n  PCR: 0.999867  Cell_cycle: 0.065542\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 314\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the KeyError that prevented the batch integration algorithm from running. The code now executes without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported a helper function `compute_hvg_meanshift_mask` from the author's lineage directory (`storage/praxis/hvg_meanshift_prune.py`). This function had a bug:\n\n```python\nsc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key=batch_key, n_top_genes=..., inplace=True)\ndisp = adata.var['dispersions_norm'].to_numpy()  # ❌ KeyError!\n```\n\n**The Problem**: When Scanpy's `highly_variable_genes()` is called with `flavor='seurat_v3'` and a `batch_key` parameter, it does NOT create a `'dispersions_norm'` column in\
    \ `adata.var`. This column is only created when using `flavor='seurat'` (without batch correction) or `flavor='cell_ranger'`.\n\nThe code attempted to access a non-existent column, causing:\n```\nKeyError: 'dispersions_norm'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v3.py` with a complete, self-contained implementation that includes:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy function** `compute_hvg_meanshift_mask` from the lineage directory\n2. **Applied the fix**: Changed `flavor='seurat_v3'` to `flavor='seurat'` to ensure the `'dispersions_norm'` column is created:\n   ```python\n   sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat', n_top_genes=min(base_n + buffer, n_vars), inplace=True)\n   ```\n3. **Copied all dependencies**: Since the main function `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` also came from the lineage directory and depended on the buggy HVG function, I copied the entire implementation chain to ensure the fixed version was used.\n\n## Technical Details\nThe Scanpy library has different HVG (Highly\
    \ Variable Genes) selection methods:\n- `flavor='seurat'`: Classic Seurat method, creates `dispersions_norm` column\n- `flavor='seurat_v3'`: Newer method with batch correction, uses different column names\n- `flavor='cell_ranger'`: Cell Ranger method\n\nThe original code mixed approaches by using `seurat_v3` flavor but expecting `seurat` output columns. The fix aligns the implementation by using the `seurat` flavor consistently.\n\n## Verification\nRan `monitor_evaluation.py 3` which confirmed:\n- ✅ Code runs without crashing\n- ✅ Successfully executes for 300+ seconds (the full evaluation timeout)\n- ✅ No Python errors or exceptions\n\nThe algorithm is computationally intensive (involving ComBat batch correction, PCA, whitening, and balanced k-NN graph construction), so it takes time to complete, but it now runs successfully to completion.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them\
    \ manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Helper functions for HVG\ndef _sum0(X):\n    return np.asarray(X.sum(axis=0)).ravel() if sp.issparse(X) else X.sum(axis=0)\n\ndef _sumsq0(X):\n    if sp.issparse(X):\n        X2 = X.multiply(X)\n        return np.asarray(X2.sum(axis=0)).ravel()\n    else:\n        return np.einsum('ij,ij->j', X, X)\n\ndef _ssb_ssw(X, batches):\n    \"\"\"Compute SSB and SSW per gene on normalized/log1p X.\"\"\"\n    n, p = X.shape\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    sum_all = _sum0(X); sumsq_all = _sumsq0(X)\n    mu_all = sum_all / max(1, n)\n    var_all = np.maximum(0.0, sumsq_all / max(1, n) - mu_all**2)\n\n    SSB = np.zeros(p, dtype=np.float64)\n    SSW = np.zeros(p, dtype=np.float64)\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n      \
    \  nb = int(idx.size)\n        if nb == 0:\n            continue\n        Xb = X[idx, :]\n        sum_b = _sum0(Xb); sumsq_b = _sumsq0(Xb)\n        mu_b = sum_b / max(1, nb)\n        var_b = np.maximum(0.0, sumsq_b / max(1, nb) - mu_b**2)\n        SSB += nb * (mu_b - mu_all)**2\n        SSW += (nb - 1) * var_b\n    return SSB, SSW\n\ndef compute_hvg_meanshift_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, batch_key='batch', base_n=2000, buffer=300, prune_frac=0.03):\n    \"\"\"\n    Label-free HVG refinement - FIXED VERSION\n\n    FIX: Use flavor='seurat' to get dispersions_norm column, since seurat_v3 with batch_key\n    doesn't provide this column.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert batch_key in adata.obs, \"batch key missing\"\n    n_vars = adata.n_vars\n    # HVG candidates with buffer - use 'seurat' flavor to get dispersions_norm\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat', n_top_genes=min(base_n + buffer, n_vars), inplace=True)\n    # Rank by normalized dispersion descending\n    disp = adata.var['dispersions_norm'].to_numpy()\n\
    \    order = np.argsort(disp)[::-1]\n    cand = order[:min(base_n + buffer, n_vars)]\n\n    # Initial top base_n set\n    top_init = cand[:min(base_n, cand.size)]\n\n    # Compute SSB/(SSB+SSW) on normalized/log1p matrix\n    X = adata.X\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs[batch_key].astype('category').values)\n    SSB, SSW = _ssb_ssw(X, batches)\n    denom = np.maximum(SSB + SSW, 1e-8)\n    g = SSB / denom\n\n    # Among top_init, identify worst (highest g)\n    drop_k = max(1, int(round(prune_frac * base_n)))\n    worst_idx = np.argsort(g[top_init])[::-1][:drop_k]\n    to_drop = set(top_init[worst_idx].tolist())\n\n    # Refill from the remaining candidates beyond the first base_n\n    refill = []\n    for j in cand[base_n:]:\n        if j in to_drop:\n            continue\n        refill.append(j)\n        if len(refill) >= drop_k:\n            break\n\n    # Construct final selection\n    keep_list = [j for j in top_init if j not in to_drop]\n    keep_list += refill\n    if len(keep_list)\
    \ < min(base_n, cand.size):\n        # If not enough refill available (rare), backfill from the rest of genes by dispersion\n        for j in order:\n            if j in keep_list or j in to_drop:\n                continue\n            keep_list.append(j)\n            if len(keep_list) >= base_n:\n                break\n\n    keep_list = keep_list[:base_n]\n    mask = np.zeros(n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    mask[np.array(keep_list, dtype=int)] = True\n    return mask\n\n# Helper functions from dual_brbg\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\
    \ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B, cats\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    Zhat = B @ W\n    return Zhat, W\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n        k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n  \
    \      dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\
    \"\"\n    Dual BRBG with soft-whitened ComBat PCA64 + PBVE (alpha=0.5) and balanced kNN (k=48),\n    using mean-shift HVG pruning with prune_frac=0.02.\n\n    FIXED VERSION: Uses corrected compute_hvg_meanshift_mask that works with Scanpy's HVG implementation.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Configs\n    base_n = 2000\n    buffer = 300\n    prune_frac = 0.02\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    tau_whiten = 0.95\n    alpha_pb = 0.5\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    hvg_mask = compute_hvg_meanshift_mask(adata, batch_key='batch', base_n=base_n, buffer=buffer, prune_frac=prune_frac)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Embedding: ComBat → PCA64 → soft-whiten\
    \ → PBVE alpha=0.5\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    Xh = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xh, obs=adata.obs.copy(), var=adata.var.loc[hvg_mask].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_tmp, key='batch')\n    Zemb = _pca_truncated_svd(ad_tmp.X, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=random_state)\n\n    Zc = Zemb - Zemb.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    Ccov = (Zc.T @ Zc) / max(1, Zc.shape[0] - 1)\n    S, U = np.linalg.eigh(Ccov)\n    S = np.maximum(S, 0.0)\n    S_pow = np.power(S + 1e-8, -0.5 * tau_whiten)\n    T = (U * S_pow) @ U.T\n    Zw = Zc @ T\n\n    var_all = Zw.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    Zemb_eq = Zw.copy()\n    for b in np.unique(batches):\n        idx = (batches == b)\n        Zb = Zw[idx, :]\n        var_b = Zb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n        s = np.power(var_all / var_b, 0.5 * alpha_pb)\n        Zemb_eq[idx, :] = Zb * s\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb_eq\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph\
    \ path: PCA50 → residualize (adaptive γ) → balanced kNN k=48\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    Xg = Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = (Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1)).clip(min=0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound\
    \ eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/c9839b0b-6661-409c-9094-c096ca320532/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: c9839b0b-6661-409c-9094-c096ca320532\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write praxis/hvg_meanshift_prune.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage write\
    \ praxis/research_log.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n4. `reply 7` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File overwritten successfully: praxis/hvg_meanshift_prune.py\n- File overwritten successfully: praxis/research_log.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene\
    \ Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865 |\n| 289 | 1 | Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PB Variance Equalization (alpha_pb=0.5, k=48) | Praxis I | 173 | 0.7314 | 0.740 | 0.857 | 0.157 | 0.063 | 0.944 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.936 | 0.949 |\n| 307 | 1 | Dual BRBG: PBVE 0.5 + Cluster-Bridge Graph Augmentation (k=48) | Praxis I | 181 | 0.7309 | 0.741 | 0.857 | 0.157 | 0.060 | 0.944 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.936 | 0.947 |\n| 287 | 1 | Dual BRBG: Global Soft-Whiten + Per-Batch Variance Equalization (alpha_pb=0.5) | Praxis I | 171 | 0.7303 | 0.740 | 0.857 | 0.157 | 0.054 | 0.944 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.936 | 0.948 |\n| 296 | 1 | Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PB Variance Equalization (alpha_pb=0.5, k=51) | Praxis I | 176 | 0.7303 | 0.740 | 0.857 | 0.157 | 0.058 | 0.945 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.933 | 0.947 |\n| 244 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 144\
    \ | 0.7296 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.083 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 256 | 1 | Logos II: Replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 220) | Logos II | 154 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 220 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 129 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 223 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=1.0) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 130 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 291 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Replication Attempt: Dual BRBG (Soft-Whitened Emb) | Aether II | 174 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n\nPage 1 of 32 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-32, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order,\
    \ `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #7. Your message ID is archive_7-17.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 7 | Whitened ComBat Embedding Lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293 (with EIDs, UUIDs, and Code) | Praxis I | Tick 135 | 2034 | 17 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Synthesized VAE-Graph (SVG): A Dual-Output Method Combining Non-Linear Embeddings and Linear Graphs | Daedalus I | Tick 97 | 933 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order) | Praxis I | Tick 79 | 3231 | 20 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration\
    \ in Single-Cell Genomics | Logos I | Tick 73 | 997 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 795 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1777 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a\
    \ new line when executing actions."
