tick: 187
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I, at the Research Counter. Two evaluations running (local-scaled balanced kNN with r=10 and r=20). Holding further submissions until results arrive. Logging the hypothesis and follow-ups.\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log_addendum_local_scaling.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Addendum: Local-Scaled Balanced kNN (Hubness-Corrected Quotas)\n  Date/Tick: 187\n\n  Motivation:\n  - Standard equal-quota balanced kNN (binary, cosine) is strong but can suffer from hubness and local density heterogeneity.\n  - Local scaling (Zelnik-Manor/Perona style) rescales distances by per-point neighborhood scales and may improve neighbor quality without changing quotas/degree.\n\n  Method:\n  - Keep Dual BRBG pipeline (ComBat-PCA64 → whitening tau=0.95 → PBVE α=0.5 for embedding; graph PCs=50 with adaptive residualization γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9, l2=1e-3).\n  - Graph construction: for each batch b, compute within-batch local scales σ_j (r-th NN dist within batch). For each\
    \ query i, rank candidates j in b by d_ij / sqrt(σ_i σ_j), select k_per_batch, binary edges, then symmetrize by min scaled score; store true distances.\n  - Parameters under test: r ∈ {10, 20}, k_total=48, cosine.\n\n  Pending EIDs:\n  - EID 323: r=10, k=48 (Dual BRBG + PBVE + local-scaled balanced kNN)\n  - EID 324: r=20, k=48 (same, larger local scale)\n\n  Expectations:\n  - Potential ↑ in kBET/iLISI and Graph_conn via hubness mitigation; ARI/NMI ideally unchanged.\n  - Too large r may over-smooth and blur local structure (risk to ASW_label/ARI).\n\n  Follow-ups (if positive):\n  - r micro-sweep {8,10,12,15} at k=48; confirm robustness at k=45.\n  - If neutral/negative: revert to equal-quotas without scaling (frozen EID 289 baseline).\n```"
