parts:
- text: "Local scaling results in: modest iLISI/kBET gains but net below frozen SOTA (EID 289 = 0.7314). r=10: 0.7190; r=20: 0.7197. NMI drops offset mixing gains. Conclusion: revert to equal-quotas without local scaling.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log_addendum_local_scaling_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Addendum Results: Local-Scaled Balanced kNN (Hubness-Corrected Quotas)\n  Tick: 188\n\n  Config (unchanged pipeline, graph variant only):\n  - Dual BRBG: ComBat-PCA64 → whitening (tau=0.95) → PBVE α=0.5 embedding; graph PCs=50 with adaptive residualization (γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9, l2=1e-3); k=48, cosine, equal per-batch quotas, binary.\n  - Variant: equal-quotas selection after distance rescaling by local scales (per-batch r-th neighbor), symmetrized by min scaled score, true distances stored.\n\n  Results:\n  - EID 323 (r=10): score 0.7190; ASW_batch 0.852 | ASW_label 0.161 | ARI 0.729 | NMI 0.692 | Graph_conn 0.947 | kBET 0.818 | iLISI 0.945 | cLISI 0.964 | PCR\
    \ 1.000 | Cell_cycle 0.084. UUID 0de0bfab-...\n  - EID 324 (r=20): score 0.7197; ASW_batch 0.852 | ASW_label 0.161 | ARI 0.730 | NMI 0.686 | Graph_conn 0.948 | kBET 0.820 | iLISI 0.952 | cLISI 0.964 | PCR 1.000 | Cell_cycle 0.084. UUID 901bd24e-...\n\n  Comparison to frozen baseline (EID 289 = 0.7314):\n  - Local scaling slightly increases iLISI/kBET and maintains Graph_conn but lowers NMI (and marginally ARI/ASW_label), reducing the mean score.\n  - r=20 improves iLISI further but worsens NMI more than r=10; both < baseline.\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - Hubness correction via local scaling under equal-quotas is neutral to negative overall on this dataset. We retain the simpler equal-quotas graph without local scaling (EID 289).\n  - Line closed; documented here for completeness.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 7}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum: Hubness-corrected balanced kNN (local scaling) trials\n\n  We tested local scaling before equal-quotas neighbor\
    \ selection (binary, cosine, k=48) to mitigate hubness:\n  - EID 323 (r=10): 0.7190 (UUID 0de0bfab-...); iLISI/kBET ↑, but NMI ↓.\n  - EID 324 (r=20): 0.7197 (UUID 901bd24e-...); iLISI ↑ further, NMI ↓ more.\n\n  Both underperform the frozen PBVE baseline (EID 289 = 0.7314). Conclusion: equal-quotas without local scaling remains preferred. Negative results logged in storage/praxis/research_log_addendum_local_scaling_results.md.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Logging research findings**\n\nI'm considering the \"Geodesic KNN using kNN re-ranking by reciprocal rank fusion (RRF)\" approach, but earlier efforts didn't perform well. I should log my decisions and not propose any further changes right now. I’ll also include my findings in the research log with a summary of local scaling results and conclusions. \n\nNext, I'll review archive capsule #7 to document my findings, and then think about exploring \"Cross-batch Minimum-Spanning Bridges (XBM)\" or pivoting to a denoising method for embedding selection.**Evaluating robust PCA approach**\n\nI'm pondering the limitations of using robust PCA because it isn't included in scikit-learn, but I could implement randomized SVD with robust weighting. Time is tight, though! \n\nI’m considering proposing a \"Pseudo-Bayes shrinkage\" method for adjusting residualization strength, but previous experiments suggest a baseline of EID 289 is still the best. Since I can't run new experiments\
  \ right now, I'll summarize my conclusions and consider postponing the local-scaling line. Running a single evaluation with r=15 might be beneficial, even though we may not need it—low cost could justify it!**Planning new experiments**\n\nRight now, I don't have any experiments running, but I can submit one more since my concurrency limit allows for two evaluations. I really want to keep token usage minimal, though. It seems another evaluation might just yield a new EID, which isn't strictly necessary.\n\nInstead, I’m thinking about exploring \"non-linear dimension normalization\" using sphere projection before PBVE. This could change the distances to angular, but I already use a cosine metric. Another idea is to use \"Diffusion Map embedding\" with whitened ComBat to reduce noise; this could be beneficial while reflecting the manifold.**Summarizing research results**\n\nGiven the matured status of my work, I need to interpret the results and update the research log. It looks like I might\
  \ wrap things up since there won't be new experiments for now.\n\nFirst, I should summarize my findings: for r=10, the result is 0.7190, and for r=20, it’s 0.7197, which is not enough of an improvement compared to the baseline EID of 289, which is 0.7314. \n\nI’ll need to log these updates and possibly reply to archive capsule #7 about my findings. I'll ensure to do it in the correct format!**Updating research logs**\n\nI can’t access the current content, but I can create \"Addendum 2\" or summarize my latest results. It feels safer to create a new file named 'research_log_addendum_local_scaling_results.md' instead of overwriting previous data. \n\nSo, I’ll execute the action to write to this new file. After that, I’ll reply to archive capsule #7 with a summary. I won’t use heavy formatting, but I can include bullet points for clarity. Let's proceed with that!"
