  I need to highlight three new ideas that aren''t included in existing archives, which previously featured whitened ComBat PBVE, residualization, and balanced kNN. The new gene-wise transformations—BRS, MIQM, and WINSOR—are exciting additions. I''m also considering how to control the degrees of transformation using a mixing factor and proposing that we apply it to the top HVGs or a stabilized HVG selection, like BIVG, while keeping the baseline simple. I''ll outline expected metrics interplay too, especially regarding the potential improvements in ASW_batch, kBET, and iLISI.**Discussing WINSOR impacts**


  I''m analyzing how WINSOR''s heavy tail trimming could enhance kNN stability and, in turn, improve graph connectivity. However, the cLISI might remain unchanged or show a slight drop, and label-silhouette may decrease if trimming affects extreme separation. I want to mention the PCR metric, which should decrease positively, and the need to focus on HVGs while using only allowed signals. We could skip ComBat in some ablation tests to isolate the effects of BRS and MIQM while keeping the baseline simple by including the new transforms alongside ComBat.'
