parts:
- text: "Concrete experiment design, safeguards, and analysis plan\n\nBaseline reproduction\n- Scaffold: normalize/log1p → HVG(seurat_v3, batch-aware) → ComBat(dense) → PCA50(use HVGs) → kNN15(cosine).\n- Fix seeds, print config to stdout, and record EID+UUID. Expectation: a mid-0.61–0.62 mean score variant based on past ComBat baselines; exact value may differ due to HVG and kNN choices.\n\nIdea 1 — BRS (Batchwise Rank-to-Normal)\n- Implementation specifics:\n  - Rank per-batch, per-gene on HVGs only with stable mergesort; use mid-ranks (r+0.5)/n to avoid 0/1. No label usage.\n  - Optional tiny jitter 1e-8·N(0,1) only if ties cause degenerate ranks (off by default).\n  - Blend λ: X’ = λ·BRS(X) + (1−λ)·X; sweep λ ∈ {1.0, 0.9}. Clip z-scores to |z|≤3.5 as safety (off by default).\n- Hypothesis: ASW_batch/kBET/iLISI↑; ARI/NMI/cLISI ≈; PCR↓. Risk: compress rare marker extremes → small ASW_label/ARI drop if λ too high.\n\nIdea 2 — MIQM (Batchwise Median–IQR Matching)\n- Implementation specifics:\n\
    \  - Compute med_b/IQR_b per-batch on HVGs; align to global med_g/IQR_g with fractional exponent ρ: X’ = med_g + (X−med_b)·(IQR_g/IQR_b)^ρ.\n  - Floors: IQR_b ≥ 1e-8 to avoid blow-ups. Sweep ρ ∈ {0.75, 0.5}.\n- Hypothesis: Gentler than BRS; ASW_batch/kBET↑, iLISI↑ (smaller magnitude); ARI/NMI should stay flat. Risk: if biology shifts medians, ρ=1.0 could blur labels—hence fractional ρ.\n\nIdea 3 — WINSOR (Per-batch winsorization)\n- Implementation specifics:\n  - Clamp per-batch, per-gene HVGs at quantiles [q, 1−q], symmetric; sweep q ∈ {0.01, 0.005}.\n  - Vectorized quantiles per batch; keep dense.\n- Hypothesis: Stabilizes tails/hubness → ASW_batch/kBET↑, iLISI↑; slight risk to ARI/NMI if true signal lives in tails. Start with q=0.01; only move to 0.005 if ARI/NMI drop.\n\nSafeguards and diagnostics (label-free)\n- Print to stdout after ComBat (for each run):\n  - PC-wise batch R² (ridge vs one-hot) summary: mean, 90th percentile (expect ↓ vs baseline).\n  - Anisotropy (std/mean of\
    \ PC variances) and PR (effective rank) (expect better isotropy, PR↑).\n  - kNN distance CV on PCA (expect ↓).\n- Keep runtime light; avoid test() override (we need scores). Diagnostics computed inline, small overhead.\n\nMinimal sweep schedule (one change at a time)\n- Baseline reproduction (no transform) → EID_B.\n- BRS λ=1.0, 0.9 (two runs).\n- MIQM ρ=0.75, 0.5 (two runs).\n- WINSOR q=0.01, 0.005 (two runs).\nStopping rule: if the first setting of an idea drops ≥0.01 vs EID_B, skip its second setting.\n\nAcceptance criteria\n- Promising if mean score ≥ EID_B + 0.005 AND ARI/NMI each not worse by more than 0.005 AND Graph_conn ≥ 0.94.\n- Otherwise record as negative with config/EID/UUID and short diagnosis (which metrics moved and why).\n\nSynthesis path to SOTA (after picking best idea/setting)\n- Insert chosen pre-ComBat transform into Dual BRBG embedding path only:\n  - Keep ComBat → PCA64 → whitening τ≈0.95 → PBVE α=0.5 unchanged.\n  - Graph path untouched (adaptive residualization\
    \ + equal-quotas k=48).\n- Reconfirm τ ridge (0.95–1.0) and k plateau (45–48) with one run each; accept only if the transform preserves or improves the existing SOTA (≥0.718 range) without ARI/NMI harm.\n\nNovelty check and scope discipline\n- None of these monotone, per-batch per-gene pre-ComBat transforms (BRS/MIQM/WINSOR) appear in current archives; they differ from PBVE/BCE/whitening and from graph-level tweaks.\n- Keep code minimal and modular (HVG-only transforms, no label use), to ensure clarity and reproducibility in the final report regardless of outcome."
