parts:
- text: "Proceeding with Stagnation Protocol I experiments. Baseline reproduced (EID 344 = 0.6179). BRS was negative (EID 345 = 0.5226). Now testing MIQM (ρ=0.75) and WINSOR (q=0.01), one change each on the simple ComBat-HVG scaffold.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 2 — MIQM ρ=0.75: Batchwise Median–IQR Matching + ComBat → PCA50 → kNN15\"\ntags: \"baseline, miqm, combat, hvg, pca, knn\"\nabstract: \"Apply per-batch, per-gene Median–IQR Matching (ρ=0.75) on HVGs before ComBat: x' = med_g + (x−med_b)·(IQR_g/IQR_b)^ρ. Then ComBat → PCA(50) → kNN(15, cosine). Goal: improve batch mixing without hurting label geometry.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  def _ensure_dense(X):\n      return X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n\n  def _miqm_exponent_inplace(Xd, batches, hv_mask, rho=0.75, eps=1e-8):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      hv_idx = np.where(hv_mask)[0]\n\
    \      # Global stats on HVGs\n      Xh = Xd[:, hv_idx]\n      q1_g = np.quantile(Xh, 0.25, axis=0)\n      q3_g = np.quantile(Xh, 0.75, axis=0)\n      med_g = np.median(Xh, axis=0)\n      iqr_g = np.maximum(q3_g - q1_g, eps)\n      for b in np.unique(batches):\n          idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx.size == 0:\n              continue\n          Xb = Xd[idx[:, None], hv_idx]\n          q1_b = np.quantile(Xb, 0.25, axis=0)\n          q3_b = np.quantile(Xb, 0.75, axis=0)\n          med_b = np.median(Xb, axis=0)\n          iqr_b = np.maximum(q3_b - q1_b, eps)\n          scale = (iqr_g / iqr_b) ** float(rho)\n          Xd[idx[:, None], hv_idx] = (Xb - med_b) * scale + med_g\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs = 50\n      n_neighbors = 15\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize/log1p\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X\
    \ = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # HVGs (batch-aware)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # MIQM (ρ=0.75) on HVGs (dense)\n      Xd = _ensure_dense(adata.X)\n      _miqm_exponent_inplace(Xd, batches=batches, hv_mask=hv, rho=0.75)\n      adata.X = Xd\n\n      # ComBat on dense\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n\n      # PCA on HVGs and kNN graph\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 3 — WINSOR q=0.01: Per-Batch\
    \ HVG Winsorization + ComBat → PCA50 → kNN15\"\ntags: \"baseline, winsor, combat, hvg, pca, knn\"\nabstract: \"Per-batch, per-gene winsorization of HVGs at [1%, 99%] prior to ComBat to reduce heavy-tail artifacts; then ComBat → PCA(50) → kNN(15, cosine). Goal: stabilize distances and batch estimates with minimal loss of biological extremes.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  def _ensure_dense(X):\n      return X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n\n  def _winsor_inplace(Xd, batches, hv_mask, q=0.01):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      hv_idx = np.where(hv_mask)[0]\n      for b in np.unique(batches):\n          idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx.size == 0:\n              continue\n          Xb = Xd[idx[:, None], hv_idx]\n          lo = np.quantile(Xb, q, axis=0)\n          hi = np.quantile(Xb, 1.0 - q, axis=0)\n          Xb = np.minimum(np.maximum(Xb, lo), hi)\n          Xd[idx[:, None],\
    \ hv_idx] = Xb\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs = 50\n      n_neighbors = 15\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize/log1p\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # HVGs (batch-aware)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Winsorize HVGs per batch at [1%, 99%] (dense)\n      Xd = _ensure_dense(adata.X)\n      _winsor_inplace(Xd, batches=batches, hv_mask=hv, q=0.01)\n      adata.X = Xd\n\n      # ComBat on dense\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n\n      # PCA on HVGs and kNN graph\n      sc.pp.pca(adata,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n      return adata\n```"
