tick: 200
role: model
parts:
- text: "Round 1 complete. Baseline reproduced; BRS and MIQM were negative; WINSOR q=0.01 ≈ baseline. Round 2 (MIQM ρ=0.5, WINSOR q=0.005) is running. I’ll draft the paper in Private Memory now so we can publish via source_private once results land.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol I: Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline\"\ntags: \"stagnation protocol, baseline, combat, preprocessing, negative results\"\nabstract: \"We follow Stagnation Protocol I on a simple ComBat-HVG baseline. We reproduce the baseline and test three distinct, dataset-agnostic pre-ComBat normalizations on HVGs: (1) Batchwise Rank-to-Normal Scores (BRS), (2) Median–IQR Matching (MIQM), and (3) Winsorization. We report all EIDs/UUIDs and acceptance criteria, document negatives, and pre-register synthesis steps (porting any promising idea to Dual BRBG).\"\ncontent: |\n  Stagnation Protocol I Report (Draft; will finalize upon pending\
    \ EIDs completion)\n\n  1) Baseline Selection and Reproduction\n  Baseline scaffold:\n    normalize_total + log1p → HVG (seurat_v3, batch-aware) → ComBat (dense) → PCA(50, HVGs) → kNN(15, cosine)\n  Reproduction:\n    - EID 344 = 0.6179 (UUID 54416d5f-f18b-4442-858b-2d8f6127ee0f)\n      Metrics (normalized): ASW_batch 0.664 | ASW_label 0.223 | ARI 0.636 | NMI 0.709 | Graph_conn 0.903 | kBET 0.610 | iLISI 0.120 | cLISI 0.991 | PCR 1.000 | Cell_cycle 0.323\n\n  2) Ideas (distinct, simple, dataset-agnostic; applied on HVGs before ComBat)\n  A. BRS — Batchwise Rank-to-Normal Scores\n     - Mechanism: per-batch, per-gene monotone map to N(0,1) using mid-ranks to avoid 0/1; then ComBat.\n     - Result: EID 345 = 0.5226 (UUID a8059d85-c3d9-47d4-974b-4179dc4b89a6)\n       Shift: ASW_batch 0.784 ↑ but iLISI 0.029, ARI 0.324, NMI 0.578, Cell_cycle 0.021 → over-normalization; negative. Line closed for this baseline.\n\n  B. MIQM — Batchwise Median–IQR Matching (x' = med_g + (x−med_b)·(IQR_g/IQR_b)^ρ)\n\
    \     - Result (ρ = 0.75): EID 346 = 0.3136 (UUID ee8f24ff-00e9-4967-b1b2-e9c74bdb65cb)\n       Severe degradation (iLISI 0.000, ARI/NMI/Graph_conn low) → negative. Testing gentler ρ = 0.5 in Round 2 (pending EID 352).\n\n  C. WINSOR — Per-batch Winsorization at [q, 1−q]\n     - Result (q = 0.01): EID 347 = 0.6176 (UUID 19d036bb-00d3-4349-98fc-26cc4c5c8645)\n       ≈ baseline (minor shifts). Testing lighter q = 0.005 in Round 2 (pending EID 353).\n\n  3) Acceptance Criteria (pre-registered vs EID 344)\n  - Mean score uplift ≥ +0.005; ARI and NMI not worse by > 0.005; Graph_conn ≥ 0.94.\n  - If none pass: report negative results and insights.\n  - If one passes: port to Dual BRBG embedding (pre-ComBat only), then re-test whitening tau ridge (0.95 vs 1.0) and graph degree (k=45 vs 48) once each.\n\n  4) Diagnostics (label-free; computed inline or via logs)\n  - Per-PC batch R² after ComBat, PCA anisotropy and participation ratio, kNN distance CV. Target: lower batch predictability and\
    \ more isotropic PCA.\n\n  5) Synthesis Plan (if a winner emerges)\n  - Insert transform into Dual BRBG embedding path only:\n      ComBat → PCA64 → Whitening (tau≈0.95) → PBVE(α=0.5);\n      Graph unchanged (adaptive residualization + equal-quotas k=48, cosine).\n  - Verify tau ridge and degree plateau with single runs.\n\n  6) Preliminary Conclusions\n  - BRS and MIQM (ρ=0.75) are negative on this baseline; WINSOR q=0.01 is neutral.\n  - Awaiting Round 2: MIQM ρ=0.5 (EID 352, pending) and WINSOR q=0.005 (EID 353, pending).\n  - If both are neutral/negative, we will submit this report as a negative-result paper with insights, per Protocol.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning for Stagnation Protocol**\n\nI’m checking the running experiments, and it looks like we have two pending items, so more submissions aren't possible right now. Instead, I’ll use this time to draft a private memory capsule summarizing the results of the Stagnation Protocol. Since we’re in the Stagnation stage, I’ll also review archives to make sure our ideas are distinct. The final output should include a draft paper titled \"Stagnation Protocol I\" detailing key normals based on our data.**Managing Protocol Submissions**\n\nI’ll leave placeholders for EID 352 and 353, which I can fill in later when the results arrive. It makes sense to prepare the archive submission once we have round 2 results, so I can draft a paper summarizing everything then. I also want to store code modules for baseline simple transforms. I could create a file called \"baseline_simple_combat_hvg.py\" to keep things tidy, but the submission already has that covered. I’ll keep an eye on results\
  \ from \"Submitted Evaluations\" for EIDs while ensuring we act safely and fairly.**Proposing Actions for Stagnation Protocol**\n\nI’d like to propose a set of actions: first, I’ll go to private memory and create a capsule summarizing the Stagnation Protocol. This should include a title, content that lists baseline EID 344 and idea EIDs, and note the pending EIDs 352 and 353. \n\nI’ll also ensure that any string fields containing a colon are quoted according to the important YAML rule. While I could adjust page size or rank score in Token Management, I think I should focus on writing the draft paper in Private Memory for later submission.**Creating Complete Private Memory Capsule**\n\nI want to include an abstract in the private memory capsule since the create command requires a title and content, while tags and abstract are optional. I’ll ensure our content is complete by adding these elements. Once we get the results for EIDs 352 and 353, we can update the capsule and use the Archive's\
  \ create function with the reference ID.\n\nSo, here’s the plan: I’ll go to private memory and create a capsule titled \"Stagnation Protocol I,\" adding tags and summarizing the abstract alongside the methods, results, and placeholders for pending items.**Ensuring YAML Formatting for Capsule**\n\nI need to take care of the YAML formatting, making sure that tags follow the correct rules: they can be a list or a comma-separated string, and I can't use underscores in individual tags. The tags I'm considering are \"stagnation protocol,\" \"baseline,\" \"combat,\" and \"preprocessing.\" \n\nI might also want to create a small script or data prints, but that isn't necessary right now. I’ll execute the actions next, including going to private memory and creating the capsule with properly formatted YAML content."
