- text: "Proceeding to finalize and publish the Stagnation Protocol I report with full results and EIDs.\n\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Round 2 results finalized):\n\n  • Baseline (ComBat-HVG scaffold): EID 344 = 0.6179 (UUID 54416d5f-f18b-4442-858b-2d8f6127ee0f)\n    Metrics (norm): ASW_batch 0.664 | ASW_label 0.223 | ARI 0.636 | NMI 0.709 | Graph_conn 0.903 | kBET 0.610 | iLISI 0.120 | cLISI 0.991 | PCR 1.000 | Cell_cycle 0.323\n\n  Idea 1 — BRS (Batchwise Rank-to-Normal on HVGs, pre-ComBat)\n  • EID 345 = 0.5226 (UUID a8059d85-c3d9-47d4-974b-4179dc4b89a6)\n    Shift: ASW_batch ↑0.784, but iLISI 0.029, ARI 0.324, NMI 0.578, Cell_cycle 0.021 → over-normalization harmed biology and mixing. Line closed.\n\n  Idea 2 — MIQM (Median–IQR Matching on HVGs, pre-ComBat)\n  • ρ=0.75: EID 346 = 0.3136 (UUID ee8f24ff-00e9-4967-b1b2-e9c74bdb65cb)\n  • ρ=0.5:  EID 352 = 0.3294 (UUID 7a392618-8da8-4d28-acb4-7f1899de70f9)\n    Both severe degradations: iLISI 0.000, Graph_conn\
    \ very low, ARI/NMI far below baseline → over-alignment. Line closed.\n\n  Idea 3 — WINSOR (Per-batch HVG winsorization, pre-ComBat)\n  • q=0.01:  EID 347 = 0.6176 (UUID 19d036bb-00d3-4349-98fc-26cc4c5c8645) ≈ baseline\n  • q=0.005: EID 353 = 0.6158 (UUID 2e03dd5e-e350-4512-80c6-8e398193216e) slight ↓ from baseline\n    Neutral to mildly negative; acceptance criteria not met. Line closed.\n\n  Acceptance criteria (vs EID 344): mean ≥ +0.005 uplift; ARI/NMI not worse by >0.005; Graph_conn ≥ 0.94. None of the ideas passed.\n\n  Insights:\n  - Monotone per-gene pre-ComBat transforms (BRS/MIQM) can break ComBat’s EB assumptions or distort multi-gene covariance needed for PCA, collapsing iLISI and label metrics despite improved batch silhouettes.\n  - Light winsorization is largely neutral under this scaffold; ComBat already stabilizes marginal tails sufficiently after log1p on HVGs.\n  - Conclusion: For this dataset, pre-ComBat per-gene monotone normalizations are not a useful direction.\
    \ Future exploration should focus on representation-level changes (e.g., embedding whitening/PBVE) or graph design (balanced kNN) rather than pre-normalizing gene marginals.\n\n  Per Protocol: We will publish this as a negative-result paper with full EIDs/UUIDs and acceptance criteria.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol I Report: Pre-ComBat Monotone Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline (Negative Results with EIDs)\"\ntags: \"stagnation protocol, baseline, combat, preprocessing, negative results\"\nabstract: \"We reproduced a simple ComBat-HVG baseline (EID 344=0.6179) and tested three pre-ComBat HVG normalizations: Batchwise Rank-to-Normal (BRS), Median–IQR Matching (MIQM), and Winsorization. BRS was strongly negative (EID 345=0.5226). MIQM degraded severely (EIDs 346=0.3136, 352=0.3294). Winsorization was neutral-to-slightly negative (EIDs 347=0.6176, 353=0.6158). None met pre-registered acceptance criteria (≥+0.005\
    \ over baseline with stable ARI/NMI, Graph_conn≥0.94). We conclude such per-gene monotone pre-normalizations are not promising here and recommend focusing on representation/graph-level methods.\"\nsource_private: 8\n```"
