  \ for EIDs 352 and 353. This capsule currently states \"pending EIDs,\" so finalizing that content is essential.**Updating capsule and preparing report**\n\nUpdating the private capsule is essential because using the source_private will include the current content, including pending results, which doesn't really help. I plan to execute an action to append the Round 2 results and final conclusions to capsule #8. Then, I'll move to the Archive Room to create an archive capsule with a title and abstract that refers to this updated capsule. I'll provide tags too, summarizing the negative results and the baseline reproduction for clarity. This way, everything will be organized chronologically!**Detailing EIDs and metrics**\n\nI need to include all relevant EIDs and details in the report. I'll write down the EIDs: 344 (baseline), 345 (BRS), 346 (MIQM 0.75), 352 (MIQM 0.5), 347 (WINSOR 0.01), and 353 (WINSOR 0.005). I should add their scores and any key metrics to explain the results. Including\
  \ high-level pseudocode for the methods is a good idea, but referencing the EIDs should suffice for clarity. Plus, while keeping within the token budget, I can mention \"lessons learned\" as potential improvements.**Preparing the reply for Private Memory Room**\n\nI’m drafting a reply that will summarize the Round 2 results, including the EIDs while noting that none passed the acceptance criteria, which is negative. I’ll document insights like how pre-ComBat monotone transforms break ComBat assumptions, BRS normalizing tails, and MIQM dropping to 0.0. \n\nThen, I’ll submit to the Archive with the title \"Stagnation Protocol I Report: Pre-ComBat Monotone Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline (Negative Results with EIDs)\" and an abstract discussing reproduction and negative outcomes. \n\nFinally, I’ll include relevant tags and ensure the formatting for YAML is correct!"
