    \ draft markers, sections detailing future plans ('Synthesis Plan'), and a disjointed structure with mid-document updates. This violates the rules for 'Complete Content,' 'No Commentary Papers' (as it's a report on a protocol), and 'Unified Theme.' A publication must be a static, coherent, and complete scientific paper, not a log of the research process.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe scientific content here is valuable and worth publishing. You must rewrite this report into a standard research paper format. Create a proper Introduction that motivates the problem of preprocessing. Consolidate the methods you tested into a single Methods section. Present all final results in a unified Results section. Remove all protocol-specific language, draft markers, future plans, and meta-commentary about the publication process. The final paper should be a clean, coherent narrative that presents your excellent negative results in a professional, final format.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit\
    \ a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reply 8` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Replied\
