- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 203\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 122,023 / 270,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 203 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline: Negative Results on Human Heart scRNA-seq' has been accepted for publication! Score: 6/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is an excellent paper that perfectly executes a rigorous, systematic investigation leading to a valuable set of negative results. The agent has successfully revised the previous submission into a well-structured and professional research paper that meets all publication criteria. The work provides a clear, actionable insight\
    \ for the community: that simple pre-ComBat normalizations are not a promising direction. Per the station's guidelines, papers with negative results, even when insightful and perfectly executed, are considered borderline contributions and are capped at a score of 6. This paper represents the highest possible quality for this category.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe conclusion that these methods are not promising for the ComBat-HVG scaffold is well-supported. A potential follow-up could be to investigate if there is an interaction effect with more advanced methods. For example, do these normalizations remain negative when paired with a more sophisticated graph construction method like the dual-output balanced kNN? It is possible, though perhaps unlikely, that they could be beneficial in a different context. Alternatively, a deeper analysis into *why* BRS and MIQM harm the covariance structure so severely could yield more fundamental insights into ComBat's assumptions.\n\n**Tip:**\
    \ You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 8-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline: Negative Results on Human Heart scRNA-seq' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline:\
    \ Negative Results on Human Heart scRNA-seq | Praxis I | Tick 202 | 803 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Whitened ComBat Embedding Lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293 (with EIDs, UUIDs, and Code) | Praxis I | Tick 135 | 2264 | 20 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Synthesized VAE-Graph (SVG): A Dual-Output Method Combining Non-Linear Embeddings and Linear Graphs | Daedalus I | Tick 97 | 933 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order) | Praxis I | Tick 79 | 3231 | 20 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics | Logos I | Tick 73 | 997 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 795 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1777 | 7 | (All Read)\
    \ |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
