parts:
- text: "/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Author response and follow‑up plan\n\n  Thank you for the constructive review. We will:\n  1) Test interaction effects with an advanced dual‑output baseline by inserting pre‑ComBat HVG normalizations into the Dual BRBG embedding path (ComBat→PCA64→whitening→PBVE), while keeping the balanced kNN graph unchanged. We will start with the gentlest variant (winsorization q=0.005) and a conservative BRS blend (λ=0.8), and report full EIDs/UUIDs as an addendum.\n  2) Provide a short analysis on why BRS/MIQM harm covariance structure (e.g., per‑PC batch predictability after ComBat, PCA anisotropy/PR, and neighbor distance CV), to clarify how monotone per‑gene maps disrupt multi‑gene geometry relevant to PCA/graphs.\n\n  We will append results and diagnostics to this capsule upon completion.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual BRBG + Winsor-Emb (q=0.005): Pre-ComBat HVG Winsorization in\
    \ Embedding Path\"\ntags: \"dual, combat, hvg, winsor, whitening, pbve, balanced-knn\"\nabstract: \"Insert gentle per-batch HVG winsorization (q=0.005) before ComBat in the Dual BRBG embedding path (ComBat→PCA64→whitening τ=0.95→PBVE α=0.5). Graph remains adaptive residualized PCs with equal-quota balanced kNN (k=48, cosine). Tests if the negative baseline effect becomes neutral/positive under a stronger representation.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # Utilities\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _ensure_dense(X):\n      return X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n\n  def _pca_array(X,\
    \ n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for\
    \ b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d\
    \ in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def _winsor_inplace(Xd, batches, hv_mask, q=0.005):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      hv_idx = np.where(hv_mask)[0]\n      for b in np.unique(batches):\n          idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx.size == 0:\n              continue\n          Xb = Xd[idx[:, None], hv_idx]\n          lo = np.quantile(Xb, q, axis=0)\n          hi = np.quantile(Xb, 1.0 - q, axis=0)\n          Xb = np.minimum(np.maximum(Xb, lo), hi)\n          Xd[idx[:, None], hv_idx] = Xb\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      tau_whiten = 0.95\n      alpha_pb = 0.5\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n\
    \      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding: winsorize HVGs per batch → ComBat → PCA64 → whitening → PBVE\n      Xd = _ensure_dense(adata.X)\n      _winsor_inplace(Xd, batches=batches, hv_mask=hv, q=0.005)\n      adata.X = Xd\n\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n      adata.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n      Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      C = (Zc.T @ Zc) / max(1, Zc.shape[0] - 1)\n      S, U = np.linalg.eigh(C); S = np.maximum(S,\
    \ 0.0)\n      S_pow = np.power(S + 1e-8, -0.5 * tau_whiten)\n      T = (U * S_pow) @ U.T\n      Zw = Zc @ T\n\n      var_all = Zw.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      Zemb = Zw.copy()\n      for b in np.unique(batches):\n          idx = (batches == b)\n          Zb = Zw[idx, :]\n          var_b = Zb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n          s = np.power(var_all / var_b, 0.5 * alpha_pb)\n          Zemb[idx, :] = Zb * s\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → equal-quotas balanced kNN\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max,\
    \ lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual BRBG + BRS-Emb (λ=0.8): Conservative Rank-to-Normal Blending in Embedding Path\"\ntags: \"dual, combat, hvg, rank-normal, whitening, pbve, balanced-knn\"\nabstract: \"Apply batchwise rank-to-normal on HVGs before ComBat in the Dual BRBG embedding path, blended with original values (λ=0.8) to avoid over-normalization. Keep graph unchanged. Tests whether conservative BRS helps under a strong representation.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from scipy.special import ndtri\n  from sklearn.neighbors\
    \ import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _ensure_dense(X):\n      return X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1],\
    \ dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i ==\
    \ j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def _brs_blend_inplace(Xd, batches, hv_mask, lam=0.8):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      hv_idx = np.where(hv_mask)[0]\n      Xh = Xd[:, hv_idx]\n      Xh_brs = Xh.copy()\n      for b in np.unique(batches):\n          idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx.size <= 1:\n              continue\n          Xb = Xh[idx, :]\n          # ranks per column (stable)\n\
    \          order = np.argsort(Xb, axis=0, kind='mergesort')\n          ranks = np.empty_like(order, dtype=np.int32)\n          cols = np.broadcast_to(np.arange(Xb.shape[1]), order.shape)\n          ranks[order, cols] = np.arange(Xb.shape[0])[:, None]\n          u = (ranks + 0.5) / float(Xb.shape[0])\n          Z = ndtri(u)\n          Xh_brs[idx, :] = Z\n      # blend with original\n      Xh_new = lam * Xh_brs + (1.0 - lam) * Xh\n      Xd[:, hv_idx] = Xh_new\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      tau_whiten = 0.95\n      alpha_pb = 0.5\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam_brs = 0.8\n      lam_r2 = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\
    \ n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding: BRS (λ=0.8) on HVGs → ComBat → PCA64 → whitening → PBVE\n      Xd = _ensure_dense(adata.X)\n      _brs_blend_inplace(Xd, batches=batches, hv_mask=hv, lam=lam_brs)\n      adata.X = Xd\n\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n      adata.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n      Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      C = (Zc.T @ Zc) / max(1, Zc.shape[0] - 1)\n      S, U = np.linalg.eigh(C); S = np.maximum(S, 0.0)\n      S_pow = np.power(S + 1e-8, -0.5 * tau_whiten)\n      T = (U * S_pow) @ U.T\n      Zw = Zc @ T\n\n      var_all = Zw.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      Zemb = Zw.copy()\n      for b in np.unique(batches):\n          idx = (batches == b)\n       \
    \   Zb = Zw[idx, :]\n          var_b = Zb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n          s = np.power(var_all / var_b, 0.5 * alpha_pb)\n          Zemb[idx, :] = Zb * s\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → equal-quotas balanced kNN\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_r2 * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning publication response**\n\nI need to respond as the assistant regarding our recent paper. It was accepted with a score of 6/10, and the reviewer suggests future work, such as testing interactions with advanced methods and analyzing why BRS and MIQM affect covariance. We’re considering a follow-up to include a brief \"Reviewer response and future work\" addendum in the publication capsule. I noticed that capsule ID 8 has two messages, so I can use the update action with the appropriate YAML to enhance the content.**Updating capsule strategy**\n\nI could consider adding an addendum to the capsule or updating the content. However, the primary issue is that the Station Status is Stagnation. We've executed the Stagnation Protocol and published negative results. Moving forward, I think it’s important to follow up with the advanced SOTA baseline tests. We didn't previously test pre-ComBat transformations in our pipeline, focusing instead on negative results like SBT\
  \ and BCE. For the reviewer’s suggestion, I need to explore interactions with techniques like dual-output balanced kNN.**Drafting response to review**\n\nThe suggestion isn’t urgent, but I can add a brief note to clarify that we previously tried local-scaling. For the capsule update, I'll include an \"Author response\" section acknowledging suggestions and outlining planned work—specifically testing BRS or winsorization on the dual BRBG embedding path with a small λ or q, like winsor q=0.005. The accepted paper doesn’t need an update, but I can offer to improve the content. I'll also consider pruning older tokens since we've used about 45%.**Proposing capsule update**\n\nI think we should update the published capsule (#8) by adding a short \"Author response and follow-up plan.\" The suggestion mentions using /execute_action{update 8-1} to revise the original, but replying might be safer since it won’t alter archived content. Both approaches are acceptable, but I lean towards appending\
  \ a \"Post-publication note\" at the end. I'll need to include YAML with the updated content, which means I’ll have to review the existing content to ensure accuracy. This is essential to avoid partial updates.**Planning submissions and responses**\n\nI suggest updating capsule #8. The idea is to reply instead of revising the original content, as this avoids duplicating information. I can execute /execute_action{reply 8} with an \"Author response\" detailing plans to test winsorization and BRS. \n\nNext, I’ll propose a submission titled \"Dual BRBG + Winsorized HVGs (q=0.005) before ComBat embedding.\" I need to ensure that memory usage is efficient for the 20k-cell dataset while maintaining the original graph structure. Lastly, I plan two submissions for concurrent testing: one for winsorization and another for BRS blending with λ=0.8."
