parts:
- text: "Concrete formulations, safeguards, and minimal implementation plans\n\nA) Mean-shift subspace deflation (batch between-means only)\n- Formulation:\n  - Input Z ∈ R^{n×d} (e.g., ComBat-PCA64). Compute total mean μ and batch means μ_b; mixing weights p_b = n_b/n.\n  - Between-batch covariance Σ_btw = ∑_b p_b (μ_b−μ)(μ_b−μ)ᵀ (rank ≤ B−1).\n  - Eigendecompose Σ_btw = UΛUᵀ, take U_k for nonzero eigenvalues (k ≤ B−1).\n  - Deflate batch-mean subspace partially: P_γ = I − γ U_k U_kᵀ, with γ ∈ [0,1].\n  - New embedding Z′ = Z P_γ. Optionally follow with light whitening (τ≈0.95) + PBVE 0.5.\n- Intuition: removes only global mean shifts across batches, preserving within-batch covariance and higher-order structure; far gentler than per-cell residualization.\n- Knobs: γ (one scalar), k (auto = rank(Σ_btw)).\n- Selection (label-free): choose the smallest γ in {0.5, 0.7, 0.9} that:\n  - reduces PC-wise R²_batch by ≥10% vs ComBat-PCA, and\n  - does not drop PR (participation ratio) or top-10 eigenvalues\
    \ by >5% (guard against biology loss).\n- Complexity: O(nd^2 + d^3) with d≈64 → trivial CPU cost.\n\nB) Generalized anti-batch PCA (gPCA) via generalized eigenproblem\n- Formulation:\n  - Let Σ_tot = Cov(Z), Σ_btw as above; define A = Σ_tot and B = Σ_btw + αI (α>0).\n  - Solve A v = λ B v; take top q eigenvectors (q≈64). Z′ = Z V_q.\n  - Optional: light whitening (τ≈0.95) + PBVE 0.5 afterward.\n- Intuition: maximize total variance per unit batch-mean variance; keeps high-variance axes that are least batch-explained. Closed-form, preserves multi-gene geometry.\n- Knobs: α (ridge, e.g., 1e−3..1e−2), q (fixed to 64).\n- Selection (label-free): pick α s.t. cond(B) improved and cumulative vᵀΣ_btw v over chosen q ≤ 10–20% of cumulative vᵀΣ_tot v; monitor PR/anisotropy and R²_batch↓.\n- Complexity: O(d^3) for 64×64 generalized eigendecomp.\n\nC) Contrastive anti-batch PCA (cPCA‑b) as a simpler special case\n- Formulation:\n  - cPCA on Σ_c = Σ_tot − c Σ_btw; eigendecompose to get directions;\
    \ Z′ = Z V_q.\n- Knobs: c ≥ 0; choose c by spectral guardrails as above.\n- Note: Similar behavior to gPCA with different conditioning; keep as backup if gPCA is finicky.\n\nWhy these may lift ARI/NMI without hurting iLISI/Graph_conn\n- They steer the basis away from batch mean directions globally, not per-cell; within-batch covariance and multi-gene relationships (critical to label structure) are retained.\n- Balanced kNN graph on Z′ (and PBVE) should keep local cross-batch mixing high; Graph_conn/iLISI remain strong if spectrum stays healthy.\n\nBatch-sliced spectral alignment (lower priority sketch)\n- Idea: build per-batch kNN Laplacians L_b on Z; align their spectra by finding a global linear map T (d×d) that minimizes ∑_b ||spec(L_b(TZ)) − spec(L̄)||², where L̄ is the average spectrum. Too heavy to optimize directly; a tractable proxy is:\n  - match per-batch covariances to a log-Euclidean SPD barycenter (Σ̄ = exp(∑_b p_b log Σ_b)), then compute a single global whitening w.r.t.\
    \ Σ̄. This is SPD-geodesic CORAL; earlier Euclidean CORAL (BCE) was negative, but log-Euclidean may be milder. Keep as a later experiment due to similarity to BCE.\n\nMinimal test plan (label-free, CPU-feasible)\n- Start from our best embedding backbone (ComBat-PCA64 → whitening τ≈0.95 → PBVE 0.5):\n  1) Replace PCA64 with gPCA(α=1e−3), PBVE, keep graph path unchanged (adaptive residualized PCs + equal-quotas k=48).\n  2) Replace PCA64 with mean-shift deflation P_γ (γ∈{0.5,0.7}), then whitening + PBVE; keep graph path unchanged.\n  3) If (1)/(2) promising, run a one-step ridge/γ refinement.\n- Diagnostics:\n  - PC-wise R²_batch, PR, anisotropy; ensure no collapse; neighbor distance CV and cross-batch entropy.\n- Acceptance target:\n  - ≥ dual baseline (≈0.731 range), with ARI/NMI↑ and iLISI/Graph_conn ≳ baseline; knobs ≤1 scalar.\n\nFailure modes and guardrails\n- Biology aligned with batch means: monitor PR/top eigenvalues; reduce γ or increase α.\n- Ill-conditioned Σ_btw (tiny batches):\
    \ add α ridge; cap k = min(rank, B−1); fall back to cPCA‑b (Σ_c) if gPCA unstable.\n- Over-whitening interaction: if τ=0.95 + new basis hurts ARI, test τ∈{0.9,1.0} once (single run).\n\nIf neither gPCA nor deflation helps\n- Conclude that ComBat-PCA + whitening already optimizes the basis against mean-shift batch structure; further covariance-level steering is redundant. Pivot to non-mean batch artifacts (e.g., within-batch heteroskedasticity modeling) or batch-contrastive graph construction (still with one scalar knob)."
thinking_content: '**Considering CCA implementation**


