parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n# Submission 1: Dual BRBG with generalized anti-batch PCA (gPCA) embedding (α=1e-3)\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual BRBG + gPCA Embedding (alpha=0.001)\"\ntags: \"dual, combat, gPCA, whitening, pbve, balanced-knn\"\nabstract: \"Replace ComBat-PCA64 with generalized anti-batch PCA (gPCA) on ComBat-PCA64: solve Σ_tot v = λ(Σ_btw + αI)v (α=1e−3) to favor high total variance per unit batch-mean variance. Then whitening (τ=0.95) and PBVE (α_pb=0.5). Graph unchanged (adaptive residualized PCs + equal-quota k=48).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy import linalg as la\n\n  # Utilities\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n\
    \      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _ensure_dense(X):\n      return X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n\
    \      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                 \
    \     pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def _cov_centered(Zc):\n      n = Zc.shape[0]\n      return (Zc.T @ Zc) / max(n - 1, 1)\n\n  def _gpca_on_combat_pca(Z, batches, alpha=1e-3, n_comps=64):\n      # Z is centered ComBat-PCA64\n      Sigma_tot = _cov_centered(Z)\n      # Between-batch covariance\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      cats, counts = np.unique(batches, return_counts=True)\n      mu = Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      Sigma_btw = np.zeros((Z.shape[1], Z.shape[1]), dtype=float)\n      for b, nb in zip(cats, counts):\n          idx = (batches == b)\n          mu_b = Z[idx, :].mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n\
    \          delta = (mu_b - mu)\n          Sigma_btw += (nb / n) * (delta.T @ delta)\n      B = Sigma_btw + alpha * np.eye(Z.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      # Generalized eigenproblem: Sigma_tot v = λ B v\n      vals, vecs = la.eigh(Sigma_tot, B)  # returns ascending\n      order = np.argsort(vals)[::-1]      # descending\n      vecs = vecs[:, order]\n      q = min(n_comps, vecs.shape[1])\n      Vq = vecs[:, :q]\n      Z_proj = Z @ Vq\n      return Z_proj\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      tau_whiten = 0.95\n      alpha_pb = 0.5\n      alpha_gpca = 1e-3\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam_r2 = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3',\
    \ batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding path: ComBat → PCA64 → gPCA → whitening → PBVE\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      if sp.issparse(ad_emb.X):\n          ad_emb.X = ad_emb.X.A\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_emb, key='batch')\n      ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      # Center\n      Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      # gPCA projection\n      Zg = _gpca_on_combat_pca(Zc, batches, alpha=alpha_gpca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb)\n      # Whitening (τ)\n      C = (Zg.T @ Zg) / max(Zg.shape[0] - 1, 1)\n      S, U = np.linalg.eigh(C)\n      S = np.clip(S, 0.0, None)\n      S_pow = np.power(S + 1e-8, -0.5 * tau_whiten)\n      T = (U * S_pow) @ U.T\n      Zw = Zg @ T\n      # PBVE\n\
    \      var_all = Zw.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      Zemb = Zw.copy()\n      for b in np.unique(batches):\n          idx = (batches == b)\n          Zb = Zw[idx, :]\n          var_b = Zb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n          s = np.power(var_all / var_b, 0.5 * alpha_pb)\n          Zemb[idx, :] = Zb * s\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → equal-quotas balanced kNN\n      Xg_graph = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Zg_graph = _pca_array(Xg_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg_graph, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg_graph.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_r2 * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg_graph - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n     \
    \ Cg, Dg = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n      return adata\n```\n\n# Submission 2: Dual BRBG with mean-shift subspace deflation (γ=0.7)\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual BRBG + Mean-Shift Deflation Embedding (gamma=0.7)\"\ntags: \"dual, combat, deflation, whitening, pbve, balanced-knn\"\nabstract: \"Deflate batch mean-shift subspace in ComBat-PCA64: compute between-batch covariance Σ_btw and apply Z′ = Z · (I − γ U Uᵀ) with γ=0.7 (U spans Σ_btw). Then whitening (τ=0.95) and PBVE (α_pb=0.5). Graph unchanged (adaptive residualized PCs + equal-quota k=48).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # Utilities\n\
    \  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _ensure_dense(X):\n      return X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB,\
    \ B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j)\
    \ if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def _deflate_meansubspace(Z, batches, gamma=0.7, tol=1e-10):\n      # Z centered n×d\n      n, d = Z.shape\n      cats, counts = np.unique(batches, return_counts=True)\n      mu = Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      Sigma_btw = np.zeros((d, d), dtype=float)\n      for b, nb in zip(cats, counts):\n          idx = (batches == b)\n          mu_b = Z[idx, :].mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n          delta = (mu_b - mu)\n  \
    \        Sigma_btw += (nb / n) * (delta.T @ delta)\n      # Eigen of Sigma_btw\n      S, U = np.linalg.eigh(Sigma_btw)\n      mask = S > tol\n      if not np.any(mask):\n          return Z  # nothing to deflate\n      U_k = U[:, mask]\n      P = np.eye(d) - float(gamma) * (U_k @ U_k.T)\n      return Z @ P\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      tau_whiten = 0.95\n      alpha_pb = 0.5\n      gamma_defl = 0.7\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam_r2 = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \n      # Embedding path: ComBat → PCA64 → mean-shift deflation → whitening → PBVE\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      if sp.issparse(ad_emb.X):\n          ad_emb.X = ad_emb.X.A\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_emb, key='batch')\n      ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      Zdef = _deflate_meansubspace(Zc, batches, gamma=gamma_defl, tol=1e-10)\n      # Whitening (τ)\n      C = (Zdef.T @ Zdef) / max(Zdef.shape[0] - 1, 1)\n      S, U = np.linalg.eigh(C)\n      S = np.clip(S, 0.0, None)\n      S_pow = np.power(S + 1e-8, -0.5 * tau_whiten)\n      T = (U * S_pow) @ U.T\n      Zw = Zdef @ T\n      # PBVE\n      var_all = Zw.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      Zemb = Zw.copy()\n      for b in np.unique(batches):\n          idx = (batches == b)\n          Zb = Zw[idx, :]\n          var_b = Zb.var(axis=0, ddof=1)\
    \ + 1e-8\n          s = np.power(var_all / var_b, 0.5 * alpha_pb)\n          Zemb[idx, :] = Zb * s\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → equal-quotas balanced kNN\n      Xg_graph = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Zg_graph = _pca_array(Xg_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg_graph, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg_graph.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_r2 * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg_graph - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances']\
    \ = Dg\n\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning gPCA implementation**\n\nI need to propose the next steps: implementing the gPCA and mean-shift deflation method, followed by running evaluations. Past performance shows baseline dual BRBG is at 0.7314, while local winsor and BRS were below this. I'll implement the gPCA anti-batch PCA approach on ComBat-PCA64 within the embedding, keeping the graph unchanged. The allowed libraries include numpy and scanpy, and I'll ensure positive definiteness by adding ridge αI to B. It's important to center Z and compute the components correctly.**Implementing gPCA and evaluation**\n\nIt seems we don't need any significant changes for embedding; I’ll keep the linear transform and proceed to whiten using a power of -0.5 tau and PBVE. The plan is to retain neighbors for 'X_emb' and compute them again. The evaluation only requires 'X_emb' and obsp graphs while maintaining the graph path as before. I’ll submit two runs: one for gPCA with α=1e-3 and another mean-shift deflation\
  \ with γ=0.7, ensuring we’re limited to two concurrent evaluations.**Choosing parameters and implementing code**\n\nGiven the two runs allowed, I’m opting for gPCA with α=1e-3 and mean-shift deflation with γ=0.7. This covers two different approaches. I need to implement the code robustly, including proper shaping, ridges, and sorting eigenvalues in descending order. \n\nI’ll compute Σ_tot and Σ_btw as described, using the appropriate methods and scipy functions. After generating Z_proj, I will whiten it and apply PBVE. Defining an equal-quota neighbor approach for k=48 will allow me to reuse the balanced neighbors builder. I'll also check the graph path for the PCA50 on HVGs after the ComBat step.**Setting up embedding and graph paths**\n\nAfter computing ComBat, the embedding uses adata.X. However, for the graph path, we previously took a selection of adata.X[:, hv], then applied PCA50 and residualization. This process uses the normalized/log1p counts instead of ComBat data in the same\
  \ adata object. It’s good practice to follow this earlier structure: after normalization and HV selection, I’ll copy ad_emb for the embedding path and compute Z on it. For the graph path, I'll retain the original adata.X for HVGs, ensuring no modifications are made to it while re-implementing functions inline. Let's also create the necessary YAML blocks.**Implementing essential prints and updates**\n\nWe don't need to worry about minimal prints; friendly messages were useful for configuration earlier, but they're not strictly necessary. I should check for edge cases, particularly if scipy.linalg.eigh is available, which seems fine since SciPy is already used. I can transform generalized eigenproblems into standard ones.\n\nNext, I’ll implement deflation from Σ_btw and calculate the number of eigenvalues greater than 1e-12. I'll set up some responses while ensuring we have the right variables and that the code is correct. The final action includes submissions for gPCA and the second for\
  \ mean-shift deflation. Let's get to coding!"
