- text: "/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"190-195\"\n    summary: |\n      SBT and BCE negatives; micro-ablations setup:\n      - Sliced Batch Transport (SBT) on Dual BRBG:\n        • EID 328 (SBT-Emb, 32 dirs, η=0.2) = 0.7219 (UUID 75383761-...).\n        • EID 329 (SBT-Graph, 32 dirs, η=0.15) = 0.7208 (UUID 4653bd81-...).\n        Outcome: slight ARI/NMI↑ but below baseline; line closed.\n      - Batch Covariance Equalization (BCE/CORAL) on ComBat-PCA:\n        • EID 332 (ρ=0.3) = 0.7244 (UUID 447e7808-...).\n        • EID 333 (ρ=0.5) = 0.7253 (UUID 7c858575-...).\n        Outcome: ASW_batch/kBET↑ but mean↓; line closed.\n      - PBVE micro-ablations prepared (submissions in 195):\n        • k=45 vs 48 and τ=0.96 vs 0.95 (results later at tick 196 show neutral/negative vs EID 289).\n\n  - ticks: \"197-205\"\n    summary: |\n      Stagnation Protocol I (baseline + three ideas), publication, and interaction tests:\n      - Baseline (ComBat-HVG scaffold):\n\
    \        • EID 344 = 0.6179 (UUID 54416d5f-...).\n      - Idea 1 BRS (rank-to-normal HVGs pre-ComBat):\n        • EID 345 = 0.5226 (UUID a8059d85-...); over-normalization; line closed.\n      - Idea 2 MIQM (median–IQR matching pre-ComBat):\n        • ρ=0.75 EID 346 = 0.3136 (UUID ee8f24ff-...).\n        • ρ=0.5  EID 352 = 0.3294 (UUID 7a392618-...); both severe degradations; line closed.\n      - Idea 3 Winsorization pre-ComBat:\n        • q=0.01 EID 347 = 0.6176 (UUID 19d036bb-...).\n        • q=0.005 EID 353 = 0.6158 (UUID 2e03dd5e-...); ≈ baseline; line closed.\n      - Paper (negative results) published (6/10): “Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations…” with full EIDs/UUIDs.\n      - Interaction with Dual BRBG embedding path:\n        • Winsor-Emb q=0.005 EID 361 = 0.7110 (UUID ec6def6c-...).\n        • BRS-Emb λ=0.8 EID 362 = 0.6644 (UUID 430a69c2-...).\n        Outcome: both < Dual BRBG baseline (EID 289 = 0.7314); line closed.\n      - New covariance-level ideas pre-registered and submitted:\n\
    \        • gPCA embedding (Σ_tot v = λ(Σ_btw+αI)v, α=1e-3) → EID 368 (results later).\n        • Mean-shift subspace deflation (γ=0.7) → EID 369 (results later).\n\n  - ticks: \"206-208\"\n    summary: |\n      Covariance-level embedding results and closure:\n      - gPCA Embedding α=1e-3:\n        • EID 368 = 0.7207 (UUID 30937973-...); preserves mixing but < 289.\n      - Mean-shift Deflation γ=0.7:\n        • EID 369 = 0.7203 (UUID b7c28171-...); < 289.\n      - Archived addendum posted summarizing interaction and covariance-level negatives; line closed. Pivot guidance: if continued, explore fundamentally new constraints (batch-contrastive graph or label-free CCA-style projections).\n```"
thinking_content: '**Summarizing key results**


  I need to summarize the results found in entries 206-208. I’ll make sure to include all important outcomes in the summary. For Round 1 stagnation, we have the baseline and various metrics. Round 2 also shows specific outcomes. There’s a paper with negative results getting accepted, and then some details about dual interactions and new variants. I’ll be careful to note that some earlier results were already accounted for.**Preparing summary actions**


  I can include a brief summary if needed, starting with the covariance-level results. The gPCA embedding and mean-shift deflation metrics are relevant. There''s also an earlier result about whitened PBVE becoming the new state-of-the-art, which I should mention for comparison. We’ve made logs and written research capsules while in the stagnation stage, following the Stagnation Protocol. I’ll create prune blocks based on specified criteria, ensuring no overlap with protected ticks or previously pruned entries.**Summarizing selected results**


  I think I should include entries 190-195, specifically noting the PBVE micro ablations and SBT results. The token usage is at 149k out of 270k, which is about 55%. I’ll proceed to prune 190-195, ensuring the "Dialogue History" reflects their existence. For summaries, entry 190 reveals SBT Emb and SBT Graph results, noting that they''re not beneficial. Entries 191-192 cover BCE trials with negative results, which have been archived, and I should reference the acceptance of previous negative results too.**Clarifying submission results and actions**


  For entry 191, we only submitted to BCE and didn''t have results, but 192''s results were accepted. I’ll make sure to mention that. For entries 193-194, I need to fix storage write and remember that I pruned tick 185 earlier. Regarding micro-ablation results with k=45 and tau=0.96, I see that tick 196 has pertinent outcomes, but since it’s protected, I can only reference the outcomes. I can clarify results from 340/341 in block 197-205 as per system messages later.**Summarizing submissions and results**


  I need to keep in mind that entry 196 is protected, but I can summarize 197-205 with context from prior results. For entry 195, we submitted the micro ablations, which is noted. In 197, we executed Stagnation Protocol I and logged baseline results. Then, in 198, I submitted MIQM and WINSOR, with results recorded at 199. Entry 200 sees another submission, followed by round 2 results in 201, which are updated in private memory. Entry 202 confirms a paper acceptance. Lastly, I’ll summarize entries 206-208 to include the gPCA and deflation results.'
