parts:
- text: "Recording QMAP experiments and holding until results return. If promising vs baseline (EID 344 = 0.6179), I’ll port the best λ into Dual BRBG embedding and test τ,k once.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log_addendum_qmap.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Addendum: Batchwise Quantile Mapping (QMAP) before ComBat on HVGs\n  Tick: 212\n\n  Motivation\n  - Prior pre-ComBat per-gene transforms (BRS, MIQM, Winsor) were neutral/negative on the simple ComBat-HVG scaffold.\n  - QMAP aligns each batch’s per-gene distribution to the pooled global shape (not Gaussian), potentially stabilizing ComBat/PCA with less distortion.\n\n  Method (baseline scaffold fixed)\n  - normalize_total + log1p\n  - HVGs (seurat_v3, batch-aware, 2k)\n  - QMAP on HVGs only:\n      For gene j, map each batch’s sorted values to pooled global sorted values (same ranks).\n      Blend X' = λ·QMAP(X) + (1−λ)·X. λ∈{1.0, 0.8}.\n  - ComBat (dense) → PCA(50, HVGs) → kNN(15, cosine)\n\n  Pending EIDs\n  - EID\
    \ 374: QMAP λ=1.0\n  - EID 375: QMAP λ=0.8\n\n  Expectations\n  - ASW_batch/kBET/iLISI ↑; PCR ↓; ARI/NMI/cLISI ≈ flat if λ not too high.\n  - λ=0.8 may preserve label geometry better than λ=1.0.\n\n  Success Criterion vs baseline (EID 344 = 0.6179)\n  - Mean score ≥ +0.005 over baseline, ARI/NMI not worse by >0.005, Graph_conn ≥ 0.94.\n\n  Next (only if promising)\n  - Insert best λ into Dual BRBG embedding (pre-ComBat) and recheck τ∈{0.95,1.0}, k∈{45,48} once each.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to figure out our next move in this multi-agent setup, where I can send commands in YAML. Right now, we've got Station Tick at 212 and two experiments (EID 374 and 375) running for our QMAP baseline. Should I wait for results or act per the Stagnation Protocol? It seems important to log predictions and perhaps prep the upcoming paper summarizing the new ideas, but I must avoid submitting more until those results come in because of the concurrency limit. Got it!**Planning research actions**\n\nI think the best course of action right now is to focus on non-code tasks, like writing a research log addendum and reading the archive document 'Stagnation Synthesis v2' by Daedalus II (EID 371). I also want to ensure we have a solid literature review since Station indicates a \"Stagnation\" status and we need a new baseline while already conducting QMAP. Depending on whether experiments 374 or 375 can beat baseline 344, I’ll craft specific actions.**Organizing\
  \ research tasks**\n\nI need to write the research log addendum titled `research_log_addendum_qmap.md`. There’s this idea for a novel approach using batch-contrastive diffusion maps, but I think it can wait. I also want to review previous EID results for writing, though I can only look at older ones since the current experiments are still running. \n\nI’ll focus on keeping things concise, then I need to ensure I use the correct archive capsule ID for my earlier work on \"Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations…\" It seems I don't have the full list handy.**Finalizing research actions**\n\nI noted that the earlier experiments had IDs like 5 and 7, and the negative results paper likely has a new ID, probably 8 or 9. However, it seems unnecessary to reply right now, so I’ll just focus on writing and waiting. Once the results come, I can preview the EIDs.\n\nI plan to provide a quick analysis of the expected effects of QMAP and its metrics. I'll also write a storage log and perhaps rank authors for\
  \ monitoring. If QMAP shows promise, I might then test it within the dual BRBG pipeline and consider adopting the high baseline from Daedalus II.**Finalizing research actions**\n\nIt looks like our results might surpass our previous benchmarks, but the environment is still indicating stagnation. I plan to write the research log addendum for QMAP and consider proposing a function to use memory since we’ve already created `apply_qmap_global_inplace` in our `simple_batch_transforms`. \n\nI’ll execute the action to store the log. After that, I might review previous work like \"Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations...\" or \"Dual BRBG...\" but it’s not essential. Let’s keep everything concise as I craft this content!"
