    \ - EID 383 (α=0.5): 0.7192 | ASW_batch 0.849 | ARI 0.744 | NMI 0.703 | kBET 0.819 | iLISI 0.935 | Graph_conn 0.946 | PCR 0.983 | UUID 4c496169-...\n  - EID 384 (α=0.3): 0.7209 | ASW_batch 0.850 | ARI 0.744 | NMI 0.703 | kBET 0.825 | iLISI 0.935 | Graph_conn 0.946 | PCR 0.994 | UUID 77998a7c-...\n\n  Comparison\n  - Baseline Dual BRBG (EID 289): 0.7314.\n  - MNN translation slightly boosts kBET but yields lower mean score; no improvement in ARI/NMI/iLISI.\n\n  Conclusion\n  - Global MNN translation is neutral-to-negative in this setting; we retain the simpler Dual BRBG without MNN. Line closed.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum: Global MNN translation on the whitened PBVE embedding (negative)\n\n  We tested a lightweight, label-free MNN translation after whitening + PBVE:\n  - EID 383 (α=0.5): 0.7192 (UUID 4c496169-...).\n  - EID 384 (α=0.3): 0.7209 (UUID 77998a7c-...).\n\n  Both are below the Dual BRBG baseline (EID 289\
    \ = 0.7314). Metrics: kBET improved slightly, but overall mean decreased; ARI/NMI/iLISI unchanged, Graph_conn ~0.946. We conclude global MNN translation is not beneficial here and keep the frozen baseline unchanged. Negative results logged in storage/praxis/research_log_addendum_mnn.md.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Exploring new methods**


  I see that many publications have already been posted, but I can create a small addendum to the existing archive. I need to manage my token usage, as I have a budget of 96k tokens. It might be good to write a research log instead of starting new experiments. One idea is a method I could call "Batch-contrastive neighborhood regularization,” which builds graph edges weighted by batched cross-entropy. However, that might require heavy coding. I could also suggest “Barycentric Whitening.”**Considering alternative methods**


  I’m exploring options like "Graph densification with limited cross-batch second-order edges," but previous attempts didn''t yield good results. Another idea is to drop dimensions of principal components with the highest batch R². We also have preconditioning methods using GLM-PCA or deviance residuals, which might need heavy precomputation. There''s also "Local subspace alignment," which could refine orientation on the whitened ComBat embedding, but it may degrade the results. Perhaps it''s time to pause for other lineages and summarize MNN results in a research log.**Logging results and plans**


  I’m considering exiting or going to the archive to respond to our existing capsule titled "Whitened ComBat Embedding" with the negative results. I need to log everything and create an addendum, avoiding further submissions for now. I might propose a new idea about a label-free CCA method for "Shared Subspace via Regularized GCCA” without any coding for now. My tasks include writing a summary of EIDs 383 and 384 in the research log and replying to capsule 7 with the negative results and key metrics. Let''s get started on that!'
