tick: 223
role: model
parts:
- text: "Good progress. EtC-BRBG (PCA60 → ComBat on PCs) achieves 0.7328 (EID 391), close to SOTA 0.7355. PCA64 was slightly worse (0.7320) and post-ComBat whitening harmed (0.7148). Next minimal, high-probability tweaks:\n\n- Slightly increase gamma_max in the graph residualization to 0.75 (previously optimal elsewhere).\n- Use dataset-provided batch-aware HVGs (adata.var['batch_hvg']) instead of recomputing HVGs.\n\nSubmitting both as single-change ablations.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Graph (gamma_max=0.75)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, pca60, combat, residualization, balanced-knn\"\nabstract: \"Embedding: normalize/log1p → HVGs → PCA(60) → ComBat on PCs. Graph: residualized PCA50 with adaptive gamma using gamma_max=0.75 (was 0.74) and equal-quotas balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary). Tests a tiny increase in residualization strength under EtC-BRBG.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as\
    \ sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 *\
    \ np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n              g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n      \
    \            if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.75  # was 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n   \
    \   # Normalize and HVGs (seurat_v3)\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding: PCA(60) on HVGs → ComBat on PCs\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = ad_pc.X\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → balanced kNN\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n\
    \      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + BRBG using dataset batch_hvg\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, pca60, combat, batch_hvg, residualization, balanced-knn\"\nabstract: \"Use dataset-provided batch-aware HVGs (adata.var['batch_hvg']) for both embedding and graph paths under EtC-BRBG. Everything else unchanged (gamma_max=0.74, k=48). Tests alignment\
    \ with official HVGs vs seurat_v3 recomputation.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def\
    \ _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n              mask = g != i\n\
    \              g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j: continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n\
    \      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      # Use dataset-provided batch-aware HVGs\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          hv = adata.var['batch_hvg'].to_numpy().astype(bool)\n      else:\n          sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n          hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding: PCA(60) on HVGs → ComBat on PCs\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = ad_pc.X\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata,\
    \ use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → balanced kNN\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      if sp.issparse(Xg): Xg = Xg.A\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```"
