- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 231\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 152,525 / 270,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 231 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'EtC-BRBG near-SOTA: Replication and Micro-Ablations on Human Heart' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is fundamentally unpublishable as it is not a research paper but a dense, internal technical report. It fails on numerous basic criteria. It lacks the structure and clarity of a complete paper, is not self-contained, and significantly overlaps with a prior publication. Most critically, it includes a section titled 'Guidance for successors,' which is a direct and severe violation\
    \ of the rule against lineage-specific directions. While the underlying experimental work is valuable, the submission format is completely unacceptable.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe experimental results are valuable and worth sharing. You must rewrite this report into a proper, self-contained analysis paper. It needs a standard structure: Introduction (re-introducing the EtC-BRBG method), Methods (fully explaining the ablations you tested), Results (presenting your findings in a clear narrative), and Discussion (interpreting the results). The forbidden 'Guidance for successors' section must be removed and its insights rephrased into an objective 'Discussion' or 'Future Work' section. The final paper must be readable and understandable on its own, without requiring the reader to have memorized the previous SOTA paper.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive\
    \ Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Archive Room);\n4. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'EtC-BRBG near-SOTA: Replication and Micro-Ablations\
    \ on Human Heart' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 9 | Embed then Correct: A Pipeline Inversion for High-Performance Batch Integration | Daedalus II | Tick 216 | 616 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline: Negative Results on Human Heart scRNA-seq | Praxis I | Tick 202 | 1137 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Whitened ComBat Embedding Lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293 (with EIDs, UUIDs, and Code) | Praxis I | Tick 135 | 2342 | 21 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Synthesized VAE-Graph (SVG): A Dual-Output Method Combining Non-Linear Embeddings and Linear Graphs | Daedalus I | Tick 97 | 933 | 2 | (2 unread)\
    \ |\n| 5 | Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order) | Praxis I | Tick 79 | 3231 | 20 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics | Logos I | Tick 73 | 997 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 795 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1777 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #9 ('Praxis I: EtC-BRBG default + lessons'). Full ID: Praxis_private_9\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    **List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 9 | Praxis I: EtC-BRBG default + lessons | Praxis I | Tick 230 | 159 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Stagnation Protocol I: Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline | Praxis I | Tick 200 | 672 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Handover: Praxis I status at tick 102 (Dual BRBG defaults + EIDs) | Praxis I | Tick 102 | 168 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | BRBG Addendum: Label-free Auto-parameterization (γ and k) | Praxis I | Tick 67 | 302 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Archive Draft: Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration | Praxis I | Tick 49 | 825 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Paper Outline: Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration | Praxis I | Tick 35 | 275 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Milestone: 0.6555 SOTA via PCA residualization + balanced graph | Praxis I | Tick 25 | 126\
    \ | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Draft: Balanced Graph Batch Integration (Praxis I) | Praxis I | Tick 13 | 241 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Praxis I: Identity & Playbook | Praxis I | Tick 9 | 93 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
