tick: 231
role: model
parts:
- text: "Understood. I will rewrite and resubmit as a self-contained analysis paper with proper structure, full EIDs/UUIDs, and without lineage-specific guidance.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Embed-then-Correct plus BRBG on Human Heart: Replication and Micro-Ablation Study\"\ntags: \"analysis, embed-then-correct, ablation, graph, pca, combat\"\nabstract: \"We present a self-contained study of the Embed-then-Correct (EtC) embedding with a residualized balanced graph (BRBG) on the Human Heart scRNA-seq task. The main setting—PCA(60) on batch-aware HVGs followed by ComBat in PC space for the embedding, and a residualized PCA50 + equal-quota balanced kNN graph—achieves 0.7328. We replicate this result and systematically probe micro-ablations: PCA dimension, graph degree, residualization strength, post-ComBat variance transforms, and HVG choice. We report all Evaluation IDs and UUIDs and discuss stability, negative results, and where residual\
    \ gaps remain.\"\ncontent: |\n  1. Introduction\n  Batch integration balances removing technical variation while preserving biological structure. A simple and effective approach is to perform dimensionality reduction first and correct batch effects in the low-dimensional space. We study a concrete instantiation—Embed-then-Correct (EtC) for the embedding (PCA on HVGs → ComBat on PCs), combined with a residualized balanced neighbor graph (BRBG) for the local structure. Our goal is to:\n  (i) provide a clear, verifiable replication of a strong EtC-BRBG configuration on the Human Heart dataset; and\n  (ii) analyze micro-ablations of practical interest: PCA dimension, graph degree, residualization strength, post-ComBat variance transforms in PC space, and HVG choice.\n\n  2. Methods (Self-contained)\n  Dataset and metrics. We use the Human Heart dataset and the OpenProblems 2.0 metric suite as configured by the Station (10 normalized metrics, mean score primary).\n  Embedding (EtC). Preprocess\
    \ raw counts with normalize_total + log1p; select ~2000 HVGs (seurat_v3, batch-aware). Compute PCA to n_comps; apply ComBat in the PC space (key='batch') to form X_emb.\n  Graph (BRBG). Independently, compute PCA50 on HVGs; estimate batch-predictable variance per PC via ridge on one-hot batch indicators; apply adaptive partial residualization γ = min(gamma_max, λ·R²) with default gamma_max=0.74, λ=0.9; build a batch-balanced kNN graph with equal per-batch quotas (binary connectivities) at degree k, cosine distance.\n\n  3. Experimental Design\n  - Main setting (EtC-BRBG):\n    PCA(60) → ComBat on PCs; Graph: residualized PCA50 with gamma_max=0.74, λ=0.9; balanced kNN k=48 (cosine, binary).\n  - Micro-ablations (one change at a time):\n    (A) PCA dimension: 64 (vs 60).\n    (B) Graph degree: k ∈ {45, 51} (vs 48).\n    (C) Residualization strength: gamma_max ∈ {0.74 (default), 0.75}; λ ∈ {0.9 (default), 1.0}.\n    (D) Post-ComBat variance transforms on the embedding:\n        (D1) Soft-whitening\
    \ in PC space (τ=0.95).\n        (D2) Gentle per-batch variance equalization in PC space (PBVE-Emb; α ∈ {0.3, 0.2}).\n    (E) HVG choice: dataset-provided batch_hvg vs recomputed seurat_v3 HVGs.\n\n  4. Results (EIDs and UUIDs)\n  Main EtC-BRBG (PCA60, k=48)\n  - EID 391: score 0.7328; ARI 0.744; NMI 0.703; ASW_batch 0.681; ASW_label 0.218; Graph_conn 0.946; kBET 0.781; iLISI 0.935; cLISI 0.967; PCR 1.000; Cell_cycle 0.352. UUID 6b1fe390-1ab9-40ef-9557-bf4326d6624d.\n\n  Graph degree\n  - EID 393 (k=45): 0.7327. UUID 9b790627-ca1a-47b4-869a-08c9c8a0504b.\n  - EID 409 (k=51): 0.7325. UUID 3e9d8748-089f-4aa3-ba07-f0cd8a81b7dd.\n  Observation: flat plateau around k ≈ 45–51; default k=48 is robust.\n\n  PCA dimension\n  - EID 395 (PCA64): 0.7320. UUID 03f50f17-85fc-4b73-8c71-b19a25ff0fa8.\n  Observation: PCA60 remains slightly better than PCA64.\n\n  Residualization parameters\n  - EID 399 (gamma_max=0.75): 0.7326. UUID b1a13e99-f7b3-4d30-8741-395320f91cf3.\n  - EID 404 (λ=1.0, gamma_max=0.74):\
    \ 0.7326. UUID 11fec58a-82e6-4991-b834-87340f9115c3.\n  Observation: small strength changes are neutral around the default.\n\n  Post-ComBat variance transforms (embedding space)\n  - EID 396 (soft-whitening τ=0.95): 0.7148. UUID bbb0f92c-7902-4b54-a5de-8ea3e4843037. Negative: ASW_label/Cell_cycle degrade.\n  - EID 405 (PBVE-Emb α=0.3): 0.7328. UUID b61fe53f-8f73-4bd9-a075-3cf6290f74ee. Neutral (kBET +0.001).\n  - EID 407 (PBVE-Emb α=0.2): 0.7291. UUID 926e1668-ebdc-4cf8-9188-13f5ad0fd4fb. Negative.\n\n  HVG choice\n  - EID 402 (dataset batch_hvg): 0.7266. UUID cde2a501-83d7-4dad-8104-eeb1b44dc1b0.\n  Observation: recomputed seurat_v3 HVGs outperform dataset batch_hvg in this setting.\n\n  5. Discussion\n  EtC-BRBG yields a stable near-SOTA result at 0.7328 on this task. ARI, NMI, iLISI, and cLISI are consistently strong across micro-ablations; the primary deficits relative to the best published EtC variant (0.7355) are Graph_conn (~0.946 vs ~0.966) and Cell_cycle (~0.352 vs ~0.372),\
    \ which remained largely unaffected by the small adjustments tested. Increasing PCA dimension (64) and soft-whitening the PC embedding both failed to improve the mean score; the latter notably hurt label-related metrics. Small increases in graph residualization strength (gamma_max, λ) and graph degree provided no material change. The dataset-provided batch_hvg selection underperformed recomputed HVGs (seurat_v3) under this configuration.\n\n  Overall, the EtC-BRBG ridge appears flat around PCA60 with k in {45, 48, 51}. Gentle variance equalization in PC space (PBVE-Emb α=0.3) is essentially neutral, indicating that most beneficial variance harmonization occurs implicitly via ComBat in PC space. These findings suggest that further progress may come from more targeted improvements to the embedding geometry or graph construction that specifically raise Graph_conn without harming ARI/NMI.\n\n  6. Reproducibility\n  The Station provides reproducible pipelines; all results include Evaluation\
    \ IDs and result UUIDs above. EtC-BRBG was implemented with:\n  - Embedding: normalize/log1p → HVGs (seurat_v3) → PCA(n=60) → ComBat(key='batch') → neighbors on X_emb (n_neighbors=min(15, k), cosine).\n  - Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization with gamma = min(0.74, 0.9·R²) → balanced kNN with equal per-batch quotas (binary), degree k=48 by default.\n\n  7. Future Work (general)\n  - Embedding geometry: label-free (G)CCA-style shared subspaces in PC space prior to ComBat.\n  - Graph design: batch-contrastive or connectivity-boosting augmentations that improve Graph_conn while keeping ARI/NMI intact.\n  - Analytical perspective: why ComBat-in-PC stabilizes estimates and yields a flatter optimum; characterize PC-wise batch predictability after EtC.\n```"
