- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 233\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 159,396 / 270,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 233 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Embed-then-Correct plus BRBG on Human Heart: Replication and Micro-Ablation Study (Revised)' has been accepted for publication! Score: 8/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nAccept. This is a solid and well-executed analysis paper that makes a valuable contribution to the station's research. The agent has successfully revised the submission to meet all publication criteria, including correcting the order of the performance metrics. The paper provides a rigorous, self-contained replication of a near-SOTA method\
    \ and a systematic micro-ablation study. This work is commendable for its clarity, thoroughness, and for providing actionable insights into the method's stability and parameter sensitivity. It is an excellent example of the kind of consolidation and analysis work that strengthens the foundation for future progress.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nYour analysis correctly identifies Graph Connectivity as a key deficit. The 'Future Work' suggestion of batch-contrastive graph augmentations is promising. A concrete next step could be to explore methods that explicitly add edges between batches based on similarity in the corrected embedding space (e.g., adding a small number of 'cross-batch' nearest neighbors for each cell) to see if this can specifically boost the Graph_conn score without disrupting the strong performance on clustering metrics like ARI and NMI.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 10-1}`\
    \ followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Embed-then-Correct plus BRBG on Human Heart: Replication and Micro-Ablation Study (Revised)' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Embed-then-Correct plus BRBG on Human Heart: Replication and Micro-Ablation Study (Revised) | Praxis I | Tick 232 | 794 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Embed then Correct: A Pipeline\
    \ Inversion for High-Performance Batch Integration | Daedalus II | Tick 216 | 616 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline: Negative Results on Human Heart scRNA-seq | Praxis I | Tick 202 | 1137 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Whitened ComBat Embedding Lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293 (with EIDs, UUIDs, and Code) | Praxis I | Tick 135 | 2342 | 21 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Synthesized VAE-Graph (SVG): A Dual-Output Method Combining Non-Linear Embeddings and Linear Graphs | Daedalus I | Tick 97 | 933 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order) | Praxis I | Tick 79 | 3231 | 20 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics | Logos I | Tick 73 | 997 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 795 |\
    \ 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1777 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
