tick: 236
role: model
parts:
- text: "Implementation plan and guardrails\n\nA) Local, distance-capped cross-batch edge replacement (with unsupervised label proxy)\n\n- Rationale update: Graph_conn likely evaluates label-wise connectivity; global stitches won’t help if added edges bridge different labels. A label-free proxy is an unsupervised clustering on the embedding (e.g., Leiden on X_emb), then constrain replacements to stay within the same unsupervised cluster. This biases replacements toward same-label connections without using labels.\n\n- Pipeline integration (after BRBG graph is built):\n  1) Unsupervised clusters:\n     - Run neighbors on X_emb with n_neighbors=15 (already available) and Leiden (resolution ~0.5; robust default). Save cluster labels cl[i].\n  2) Per-node local scale and candidate pools:\n     - For each node i, compute σ_i = median of distances to its current k_total graph neighbors (robust).\n     - For each batch b ≠ batch(i), reuse the balanced-kNN per-batch ranking (cand(i,b), dists) already\
    \ computed during graph build.\n  3) Eligible edges to replace:\n     - For each j ∈ N(i,b) (current cross-batch neighbors), mark as eligible if d(i,j) > τ·σ_i (τ ∈ {1.3, 1.2}, try 1.3 first).\n     - Replacement candidates j′ scanned from cand(i,b) in order with filters:\n       - Distance cap: d(i,j′) ≤ τ·σ_i and d(i,j′) ≤ τ·σ_j′ (two-sided cap).\n       - Cluster-consistency: cl[j′] == cl[i] (unsupervised).\n       - Not already connected to i and preserves per-batch quota (replace 1-for-1).\n     - At most r replacements per (i,b), start with r = 1 (replace only the single farthest cross-batch edge).\n  4) Symmetry and conflicts:\n     - Collect proposed replacements R. Apply only those that do not violate degree/quota on either endpoint after symmetrization.\n     - If two proposals would cause degree overflow on a target, keep the one with larger distance gain Δd = d_old − d_new, drop the rest.\n  5) Apply replacements and rebuild CSR matrices; assert invariants:\n     - deg(i)\
    \ == k_total; per-batch quotas preserved for each i; no duplicates/self-loops; two-sided cap holds.\n\n- Diagnostics to log:\n  - Fraction of edges replaced; per-node max cross-batch distance before/after; proportion of replacements satisfying cluster-consistency.\n  - Label-free proxies: components in subgraphs induced by each unsupervised cluster (expect fewer components if successful).\n  - Metric deltas target: Graph_conn +≥0.003; ARI/NMI within −0.001; Cell_cycle ≥ baseline; cLISI/iLISI within ±0.003.\n\n- Risks and mitigations:\n  - Over-restriction (no valid j′): keep original edge (no harm).\n  - Cluster mismatch: if cl is too coarse/fine, replacements may be rare. Mitigate by a mild resolution sweep (0.4–0.6) only if needed.\n  - Budget cap: r=1 ensures minimal rewiring per batch per node.\n\nB) GCCA-lite shared space (fallback if A neutral/negative)\n\n- Goal: reduce cross-batch misalignment at a structural (axis) level so that same-label, cross-batch neighbors become locally\
    \ closer, improving label-wise connectivity without smoothing away cluster structure.\n\n- Label-free MAXVAR/GCCA proxy:\n  1) For each batch b:\n     - From normalized/log1p HVGs, compute PCA_r (r=50) → Z_b (n_b × r), center columns to zero mean.\n     - Whiten per batch: Z_b_w = Z_b / std(Z_b, axis=0, ddof=1) (avoid zero-divides with floor 1e-8).\n  2) Stack all batches row-wise with equal weights: Z_stack = concat_b Z_b_w.\n  3) SVD/PCA on Z_stack → take top d=60 shared components V_d (r × d), project each batch: Y_b = Z_b_w @ V_d.\n  4) Light ComBat in shared space: run ComBat(key='batch') on Y = concat_b Y_b to remove residual batch mean/var shifts (EtC in shared space).\n  5) Use Y_combat as X_emb. Leave BRBG graph unchanged (residualized PC50 on original HVGs, balanced kNN k=48).\n  - Safety: If runtime/memory tight, compute batch-wise covariances and do an incremental PCA (but r,d are small, feasible).\n  - Diagnostics: Compare per-PC batch predictability R² in shared space vs\
    \ baseline EtC; expect reductions on misaligned axes; check Graph_conn and Cell_cycle vs baseline.\n\n- Success targets: Graph_conn +≥0.003; ARI/NMI stable (±0.001); Cell_cycle ≥ baseline; otherwise back off (reduce d to 56 or adjust whitening floor).\n\nPlan of action (minimal runs)\n\n- Try A with τ=1.3 first (cluster constraint on), r=1; if neutral/negative, try τ=1.2.\n- If A fails, implement B (GCCA-lite shared space) with d=60; if neutral, one follow-up at d=56.\n- Keep within 2 concurrent runs; log EIDs/UUIDs and deltas metric-by-metric. Close lines cleanly if neutral/negative."
