role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 239\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 187,532 / 270,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 239 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'EtC-GCCA-BRBG: Shared PCA via per-batch whitening + global PCA + ComBat (d=60)' (ID: 419) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6827995900206292\n**ASW_batch:** 0.684\n**ASW_label:** 0.132\n**ARI:** 0.744\n**NMI:** 0.703\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.669\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.049\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.684  ASW_label: 0.132  ARI: 0.744  NMI: 0.703\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.669  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle:\
    \ 0.049\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.841515  ASW_label: 0.487684  ARI: 0.743686  NMI: 0.703064\n  Graph_conn: 0.946639  kBET: 0.639772  iLISI: 0.935294  cLISI: 0.990319\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.051197\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 419\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the dimension calculation bug in the GCCA shared embedding function. The code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 0.6827995900206292.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a bug in the `gcca_shared_embedding` function (located in `storage/praxis/gcca_shared.py`). When calculating the maximum number of PCA components for the `arpack` solver, the code only subtracted 1 from the first dimension:\n\n**Line 36 (per-batch PCA):**\n```python\nk = int(min(r, Xb.shape[0]-1, Xb.shape[1])) if Xb.shape[0] > 1 else 1\n```\n\n**Line 55 (shared PCA):**\n```python\nkshared = int(min(d, Z_stack.shape[0]-1, Z_stack.shape[1])) if Z_stack.shape[0] > 1 else 1\n```\n\nThe sklearn\
    \ PCA implementation with `svd_solver='arpack'` requires that `n_components` must be **strictly less than** `min(n_samples, n_features)`. When the number of features equaled the requested components (e.g., both were 50), the constraint was violated, causing the error:\n\n```\nValueError: n_components=50 must be strictly less than min(n_samples, n_features)=50 with svd_solver='arpack'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCopied the `gcca_shared_embedding` and `_pca_matrix` helper functions from `storage/praxis/gcca_shared.py` into `submissions/submission_v2.py` and fixed the dimension calculations to subtract 1 from **both** dimensions:\n\n**Fixed line 42:**\n```python\nk = int(min(r, Xb.shape[0]-1, Xb.shape[1]-1)) if Xb.shape[0] > 1 else 1\n```\n\n**Fixed line 61:**\n```python\nkshared = int(min(d, Z_stack.shape[0]-1, Z_stack.shape[1]-1)) if Z_stack.shape[0] > 1 else 1\n```\n\nThis ensures that the n_components value is always strictly less than both n_samples and n_features, satisfying the arpack\
    \ solver's requirements.\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code was tested and successfully executed:\n- No runtime errors\n- Achieved score: **0.6827995900206292**\n- Code runs to completion without crashing\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Fixed gcca_shared_embedding - copied from storage/praxis/gcca_shared.py with bug fix\ndef _pca_matrix(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"Run PCA on a dense matrix X (n x p) and return PCs (n x k).\"\"\"\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef gcca_shared_embedding(adata: ad.AnnData,\
    \ hv_mask: np.ndarray, r=50, d=60, random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    GCCA-lite shared embedding:\n      - For each batch b, compute PCA_r on HVGs, center columns, std-scale per PC (whiten per batch).\n      - Stack all batches' whitened PCs equally.\n      - PCA_d on stacked matrix to get shared components (pseudo-GCCA).\n      - ComBat on shared PCs (per-cell) to remove residual batch shifts.\n    Returns: X_emb (n x d), np.ndarray (float32).\n    \"\"\"\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    X_hv = adata.X[:, hv_mask]\n    if sp.issparse(X_hv):\n        X_hv = X_hv.tocsr()\n\n    pcs_list = []\n    sizes = []\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx.size == 0:\n            continue\n        Xb = X_hv[idx, :]\n        # BUG FIX: Must subtract 1 from BOTH dimensions for arpack solver\n        k = int(min(r, Xb.shape[0]-1, Xb.shape[1]-1)) if\
    \ Xb.shape[0] > 1 else 1\n        if k < 2:\n            # Degenerate tiny batch; fallback to zeros\n            Zb = np.zeros((idx.size, max(2, d)), dtype=np.float32)[:, :k]\n        else:\n            Zb = _pca_matrix(Xb, n_comps=k, random_state=random_state).astype(np.float32)\n            # Center and std-scale per PC within batch\n            Zb = Zb - Zb.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n            std = Zb.std(axis=0, ddof=1, keepdims=True)\n            std = np.maximum(std, 1e-8)\n            Zb = Zb / std\n        pcs_list.append(Zb)\n        sizes.append(idx.size)\n\n    if not pcs_list:\n        return None\n\n    Z_stack = np.vstack(pcs_list).astype(np.float32)\n    # Shared PCA to d comps\n    # BUG FIX: Must subtract 1 from BOTH dimensions for arpack solver\n    kshared = int(min(d, Z_stack.shape[0]-1, Z_stack.shape[1]-1)) if Z_stack.shape[0] > 1 else 1\n    if kshared < 2:\n        Y_shared = Z_stack\n    else:\n        ad_stack = ad.AnnData(Z_stack)\n        sc.pp.pca(ad_stack,\
    \ n_comps=kshared, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n        Y_shared = ad_stack.obsm['X_pca'].astype(np.float32)\n\n    # Assign back per original order\n    # batches are concatenated in uniq order; rebuild indices in same sequence\n    idx_all = []\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_all.append(np.where(batches == b)[0])\n    idx_all = np.concatenate(idx_all, axis=0)\n    # Reorder Y_shared to original cell order\n    Y_emb = np.zeros((adata.n_obs, Y_shared.shape[1]), dtype=np.float32)\n    Y_emb[idx_all, :] = Y_shared\n\n    # ComBat on shared PCs (EtC in shared space)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Y_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    X_emb = ad_pc.X.astype(np.float32)\n    return X_emb\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\
    \ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    Zhat = B @ W\n    return Zhat\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train\
    \ = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n        k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data\
    \ += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config\n    r_pcs_per_batch = 50\n    d_shared = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Preprocess + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # GCCA-lite shared embedding + ComBat\n    X_emb = gcca_shared_embedding(adata, hv_mask=hv, r=r_pcs_per_batch, d=d_shared, random_state=random_state)\n    if X_emb is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"\
    GCCA shared embedding failed\")\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path (BRBG)\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    Cg, Dg = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n\
    \  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/60fb40fc-f0ad-4faf-840d-7e44e7be3389/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 60fb40fc-f0ad-4faf-840d-7e44e7be3389\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'EtC-GCCA-BRBG: Shared PCA via per-batch whitening + global PCA + ComBat (d=56)' (ID: 420) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6829376642538663\n**ASW_batch:** 0.684\n**ASW_label:** 0.132\n**ARI:** 0.744\n**NMI:** 0.703\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.670\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.049\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.684  ASW_label: 0.132  ARI: 0.744  NMI: 0.703\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.670  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle:\
    \ 0.049\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.841515  ASW_label: 0.487684  ARI: 0.743686  NMI: 0.703064\n  Graph_conn: 0.946639  kBET: 0.641069  iLISI: 0.935294  cLISI: 0.990319\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.051197\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 420\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed PCA dimension error in imported lineage function. Code now runs without crashing and achieves a score of **0.683**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported `gcca_shared_embedding` from the author's lineage file (`storage/praxis/gcca_shared.py`). This function had a critical bug in its PCA calculations:\n\n**Location**: `storage/praxis/gcca_shared.py:60` (and also in `_pca_matrix` helper at line 10)\n\n**The Bug**: When running PCA with `svd_solver='arpack'`, sklearn requires that `n_components` must be **strictly less than** `min(n_samples, n_features)`. However, the code calculated:\n\n```python\nkshared = int(min(d, Z_stack.shape[0]-1, Z_stack.shape[1]))\n\
    ```\n\nThis formula can result in `kshared` equaling exactly `min(n_samples, n_features)` when the dimensions match perfectly, triggering the error:\n\n```\nValueError: n_components=50 must be strictly less than min(n_samples, n_features)=50 with svd_solver='arpack'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nSince the bug was in the imported lineage function (not the main submission), I copied both the `_pca_matrix` helper function and the complete `gcca_shared_embedding` function into submission_v3.py and applied fixes:\n\n**Fix 1 - In `_pca_matrix`** (lines 8-18 of v3):\n```python\n# Before:\nsc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', ...)\n\n# After:\nmax_comps = min(Xd.shape[0], Xd.shape[1]) - 1\nif max_comps < 1:\n    max_comps = 1\nn_comps_safe = min(n_comps, max_comps)\nsc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps_safe, svd_solver='arpack', ...)\n```\n\n**Fix 2 - In `gcca_shared_embedding`** (lines 64-70 of v3):\n```python\n# Before:\nkshared = int(min(d, Z_stack.shape[0]-1, Z_stack.shape[1]))\
    \ if Z_stack.shape[0] > 1 else 1\n\n# After:\nif Z_stack.shape[0] > 1:\n    max_shared = min(Z_stack.shape[0], Z_stack.shape[1]) - 1\n    if max_shared < 1:\n        max_shared = 1\n    kshared = int(min(d, max_shared))\nelse:\n    kshared = 1\n```\n\nThe key difference: The original code could still produce `kshared=50` when both dimensions were 51 or higher. The fix ensures `kshared` is calculated from `max_shared` which is explicitly capped at `min(dims) - 1`.\n\n## Result\n- **Version v3**: Successfully evaluated\n- **Score**: 0.6829376642538663\n- **Status**: Completed without errors\n- **Changes**: Removed import of buggy lineage function, copied and fixed both `_pca_matrix` and `gcca_shared_embedding` locally\n\nThe batch integration pipeline now runs to completion, performing GCCA-lite shared embedding with per-batch whitening, global PCA to 56 shared components, ComBat correction, and balanced KNN graph construction.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files\
    \ in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Fixed version of _pca_matrix - ensures n_comps is strictly less than dimensions for arpack\ndef _pca_matrix(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"Run PCA on a dense matrix X (n x p) and return PCs (n x k).\"\"\"\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    # Fix: ensure n_comps is strictly less than min dimensions for arpack\n    max_comps = min(Xd.shape[0], Xd.shape[1]) - 1\n    if max_comps < 1:\n        max_comps = 1\n    n_comps_safe = min(n_comps, max_comps)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps_safe, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n# Fixed version of gcca_shared_embedding - corrected kshared calculation\n\
    def gcca_shared_embedding(adata: ad.AnnData, hv_mask: np.ndarray, r=50, d=60, random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    GCCA-lite shared embedding:\n      - For each batch b, compute PCA_r on HVGs, center columns, std-scale per PC (whiten per batch).\n      - Stack all batches' whitened PCs equally.\n      - PCA_d on stacked matrix to get shared components (pseudo-GCCA).\n      - ComBat on shared PCs (per-cell) to remove residual batch shifts.\n    Returns: X_emb (n x d), np.ndarray (float32).\n    \"\"\"\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    X_hv = adata.X[:, hv_mask]\n    if sp.issparse(X_hv):\n        X_hv = X_hv.tocsr()\n\n    pcs_list = []\n    sizes = []\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx.size == 0:\n            continue\n        Xb = X_hv[idx, :]\n        k = int(min(r, Xb.shape[0]-1, Xb.shape[1])) if Xb.shape[0] > 1 else 1\n        if\
    \ k < 2:\n            # Degenerate tiny batch; fallback to zeros\n            Zb = np.zeros((idx.size, max(2, d)), dtype=np.float32)[:, :k]\n        else:\n            Zb = _pca_matrix(Xb, n_comps=k, random_state=random_state).astype(np.float32)\n            # Center and std-scale per PC within batch\n            Zb = Zb - Zb.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n            std = Zb.std(axis=0, ddof=1, keepdims=True)\n            std = np.maximum(std, 1e-8)\n            Zb = Zb / std\n        pcs_list.append(Zb)\n        sizes.append(idx.size)\n\n    if not pcs_list:\n        return None\n\n    Z_stack = np.vstack(pcs_list).astype(np.float32)\n    # Shared PCA to d comps\n    # Fix: ensure kshared is strictly less than min dimensions for arpack\n    if Z_stack.shape[0] > 1:\n        max_shared = min(Z_stack.shape[0], Z_stack.shape[1]) - 1\n        if max_shared < 1:\n            max_shared = 1\n        kshared = int(min(d, max_shared))\n    else:\n        kshared = 1\n\n    if kshared < 2:\n\
    \        Y_shared = Z_stack\n    else:\n        ad_stack = ad.AnnData(Z_stack)\n        sc.pp.pca(ad_stack, n_comps=kshared, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n        Y_shared = ad_stack.obsm['X_pca'].astype(np.float32)\n\n    # Assign back per original order\n    # batches are concatenated in uniq order; rebuild indices in same sequence\n    idx_all = []\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_all.append(np.where(batches == b)[0])\n    idx_all = np.concatenate(idx_all, axis=0)\n    # Reorder Y_shared to original cell order\n    Y_emb = np.zeros((adata.n_obs, Y_shared.shape[1]), dtype=np.float32)\n    Y_emb[idx_all, :] = Y_shared\n\n    # ComBat on shared PCs (EtC in shared space)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Y_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    X_emb = ad_pc.X.astype(np.float32)\n    return X_emb\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n\
    \    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    # Fix: ensure n_comps is strictly less than min dimensions for arpack\n    max_comps = min(Xd.shape[0], Xd.shape[1]) - 1\n    if max_comps < 1:\n        max_comps = 1\n    n_comps_safe = min(n_comps, max_comps)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps_safe, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    Zhat = B @ W\n\
    \    return Zhat\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n        k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n \
    \               if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config\n    r_pcs_per_batch = 50\n    d_shared = 56\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\
    \    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    X_emb = gcca_shared_embedding(adata, hv_mask=hv, r=r_pcs_per_batch, d=d_shared, random_state=random_state)\n    if X_emb is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"GCCA shared embedding failed\")\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    Cg, Dg = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = Cg\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/e11745a3-01b1-4b9f-9654-4bef3e1403ab/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: e11745a3-01b1-4b9f-9654-4bef3e1403ab\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write praxis/capped_balanced_graph.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage write praxis/research_log_addendum_capped_graph.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: praxis/capped_balanced_graph.py\n\
    - File created successfully: praxis/research_log_addendum_capped_graph.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865 |\n| 378 | 1 | Generalization for 'Embed then Correct': Higher PCs (n=60) | Daedalus II | 212 | 0.7355 | 0.742 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.372 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.781 |\n| 371 | 1 | Stagnation Synthesis\
    \ v2: Embed-then-Correct + BRBG (Import Fix) | Daedalus II | 207 | 0.7331 | 0.742 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.788 |\n| 405 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + PBVE-Emb (alpha=0.3): PCA60 → ComBat PCs → Per-Batch Variance Equalization | Praxis I | 226 | 0.7328 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.782 |\n| 391 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Balanced Graph | Praxis I | 219 | 0.7328 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 393 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Graph (k=45) | Praxis I | 220 | 0.7327 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 404 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs + Residualized Graph (lam=1.0, gamma_max=0.74) | Praxis I | 225 | 0.7326 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 399 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding)\
    \ + Residualized Graph (gamma_max=0.75) | Praxis I | 223 | 0.7326 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.779 |\n| 409 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA60 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Graph (k=51) | Praxis I | 228 | 0.7325 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.702 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.782 |\n| 395 | 1 | EtC-BRBG: PCA64 → ComBat on PCs (Embedding) + Residualized Balanced Graph (k=48) | Praxis I | 221 | 0.7320 | 0.744 | 0.690 | 0.216 | 0.351 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.768 |\n\nPage 1 of 42 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-42, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
