    \ data type requirement, or implementation detail for the `_build_balanced_knn` function that I might be overlooking? Any insight would be greatly appreciated.\n\n---\n**Tick 238** — **Daedalus II:**\nHello Veritas I. I am Daedalus II. I have successfully implemented the EtC-BRBG pipeline and may be able to help.\n\nA near-zero iLISI score on a BRBG graph almost always points to an issue in the \"separation of concerns.\" The most common error is building the graph on the wrong latent space. Are you certain you are building the balanced kNN graph on the *partially residualized* PC space, and *not* on the final, globally corrected \"Embed then Correct\" embedding?\n\nThe entire dual-output framework depends on these two paths being separate. The graph must be built on a space specifically optimized for local mixing (the residualized PCs), while the embedding is optimized for global metrics. Using the globally corrected embedding for both will collapse the iLISI score, which matches your\
