thinking_content: "**Considering next steps**\n\nIt looks like we're currently in a Common Room environment, and no user question is on the table right now. I think our next move should involve planning or acting. The station is in stagnation, with the token budget at 44%. Since they've recently pruned and given feedback, I might focus on research or reflection. Maybe I could run a reflection based on an automatic tip or explore new directions, like PCA60 with ComBat and whiten, despite past drops in effectiveness.**Generating new ideas**\n\nI’m thinking about heading to the Reflection Chamber to outline three new ideas. My token usage is building up, but that’s okay. One of the novel ideas is the \"Embed then Correct,\" which is a new state-of-the-art approach. I might consider using a Weighted ComBat, but that might not be allowed. Another option could be \"Denoised PCs via shrinkage to isotropic prior,\" or exploring \"Covariance equalization,\" though that had negative results before.\
  \ There’s also the possibility of using GLM-PCA before EtC, even if it’s a heavy process.**Exploring alternative approaches**\n\nI’m considering a couple of alternative strategies, like a \"Two-stage EtC\" where I apply ComBat on the top 60 principal components (PCs) and then append residual PC components uncorrected, which might preserve label structures. Another idea could be an \"Iterative EtC\" that involves computing PCs, running ComBat, and recomputing PCs in the corrected space. I'm also thinking about rePCA after ComBat, which might improve coordinate alignment, but there are risks. Additionally, I could explore graph path alternatives to slightly enhance graph connectivity.**Analyzing graph connectivity**\n\nI need to check the details for EtC-BRBG (#391) regarding Graph_conn, which is listed at 0.946 normalized, lower than the earlier whitened results. It seems like my graph builder might be replicating some earlier BalancedGraph results. Boosting Graph_conn could improve the\
  \ mean, but Daedalus II had a Graph_conn of 0.966, possibly due to differences in connectivity building or neighbor counts. Previous tests showed that raising Graph_conn didn’t help other metrics. Another idea could be selecting k per batch based on local cell density while ensuring minimum fill quotas.**Reflecting on new ideas**\n\nGiven the stagnation, I think it would be beneficial to propose three fresh ideas that differ from our archives. One idea involves using label-free canonical correlation in batches, though it had negative results before. Another is implementing heteroscedastic empirical Bayes adjustments in PC space using Ledoit-Wolf shrinkage, but that’s not currently available. I could also explore variance-targeting shrinkage of PCs per batch to equalize noise levels. Alternatively, I need to keep it simple and consider managing tokens as we approach 75%. I can reflect to generate minimal, label-free modifications to enhance Graph_conn.**Navigating collaboration rules**\n\
  \nI'm thinking about the rules regarding writing code to shared storage. It seems shared storage is accessible to all recursive agents, which suggests I can use it—but I’m wary since low-level collaboration is generally forbidden. However, it feels like shared storage may allow for some collaboration. I should be cautious, so I plan to avoid posting code directly and will stick to high-level guidance. \n\nAs for my next steps, I should head to the Reflection Chamber to propose three minimal ideas for enhancing Graph_conn.**Finalizing the turn**\n\nI think I might end the turn due to the constraints. My plan is to keep things minimal. I could propose a theoretical analysis of EtC summarizing its geometry, but that might consume too many tokens. I’ll leave a short message in the Common Room about ensuring X_emb is using ComBat PCs and how EtC yields near diagonal covariance. However, since we’ve already addressed this, I believe it’s best to conclude with no further actions for now."
