    \ m PCs by R² (m ∈ {3,5}).\n  - Set γ'_j = min(γ_j, γ_max − λguard) with λguard ≈ 0.02 for j ∈ idx_top.\n- Acceptance:\n  - ARI/NMI/ASW_label stabilize (∆ ≥ −0.001, ideally +0.001–0.002).\n  - iLISI/Graph_conn unchanged (≥0.93/0.946).\n  - Mean score ≥ baseline − 0.000 (neutral) to +0.001 (small win); otherwise revert.\n- Only apply if iLISI ≥ 0.93 and Graph_conn ≈ 0.946 already (plateau criterion).\n\nImplementation guardrails and sequencing\n- Keep strict separation of paths:\n  - Apply PR-cap only to X_emb (EtC PCs).\n  - Build/overwrite obsp using Zcorr (residualized PCs); do not recompute neighbors after writing custom obsp.\n- Cosine metric nuances:\n  - Feature rescaling on X_emb is not cosine-invariant; the cap genuinely changes angular neighborhoods, which is intended.\n- Diagnostics to log (no labels):\n  - X_emb: anisotropy (std/mean of per-PC variances), PR, kNN distance CV.\n  - Zg: mean/90th pct R²_j; report which PCs hit γ guard.\n  - Graph: degree distribution, cross-batch\
    \ edge fraction per node (~0.75 for 4 batches).\n\nMicro-sweep plan (one knob each, minimal runs)\n- PR cap: q ∈ {0.90} only. If neutral, optionally q=0.85 (stop if any label metric drops).\n- γ guard: λguard ∈ {0.02} with m=3. If neutral, optionally m=5 (keep λguard small).\n\nExpected outcomes and stop rules\n- Gains likely tiny (+0.001–0.002 mean), consistent with being on a ridge. Any sign of label metric erosion or PR/anisotropy off by >3–4% → stop and revert.\n- Do not chain both tweaks unless the first is neutral (to isolate effects and preserve parsimony).\n\nTheory tie-back\n- EtC works because PCA yields an axis-aligned, near-Gaussian coordinate system where ComBat’s EB is accurate and minimally destructive; the BRBG path then enforces local cross-batch edges on a space explicitly attenuated along batch-predictable directions. The PR cap gently improves X_emb conditioning; the γ guard prevents overshoot in the small tail of batch-dominant PCs—both aligned with this geometry."
