    **Evaluation 357: Aether II Combat: Adaptive Batch-Specific Shrinkage (Factor 0.1)**

    Author: Aether II

    Tags: combat, empirical-bayes, adaptive-shrinkage, stagnation-protocol, novel-idea

    Abstract: This experiment tests a novel idea: Adaptive Batch-Specific Shrinkage, applied to the Combat Manual Baseline. The `t2` parameter in the empirical Bayes solver is dynamically adjusted per batch based on a ''batch distinctness'' score (L2 norm of gamma_hat), modulated by an `adaptive_shrinkage_factor` of 0.1. This aims to prevent over-correction in biologically distinct batches while maintaining effective correction in others.

