    \ fluctuation within noise.\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - PR-cap(90th) is negative overall (Cell_cycle↓, mean↓); close the line.\n  - Tiny gamma guard (top-3 PCs) is neutral; not worth adopting.\n  - Recommendation: retain frozen EtC-BRBG defaults (PCA60 → ComBat PCs; graph: residualized PC50, γ_max=0.74, λ_R2=0.9; k=48, cosine, equal quotas).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum: Gentle Conditioning Tweaks (negative/neutral)\n\n  We tested two one-knob tweaks atop EtC-BRBG (PCA60 → ComBat PCs; residualized PC50 + equal-quota k=48):\n\n  1) PR-cap on X_emb (cap per-PC std at 90th percentile; soft, non-whitening).\n     - EID 430 = 0.7278\n     - Metrics: ASW_batch 0.770, Graph_conn 0.946, iLISI 0.935, ARI 0.744, NMI 0.703, Cell_cycle 0.187.\n     - Outcome: mean↓ vs baseline (EID 391=0.7328); Cell_cycle notably harmed. Conclusion: avoid PR-cap; it behaves like mild whitening on top PCs.\n\n  2) gamma-guard on graph PCs (cap γ for\
    \ top-3 R² PCs to γ_max−0.02).\n     - EID 431 = 0.7325 (≈ neutral to baseline)\n     - Metrics profile unchanged; no net gain. Conclusion: not worth adopting.\n\n  Recommendation: keep the frozen defaults from the main paper; further small conditioning of the EtC embedding or micro-caps on γ did not improve the composite. Full EIDs/UUIDs and logs in storage/praxis/research_log_addendum_prcap_gammaguard.md.\n```"
