parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{review 432}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: EtC-BRBG + Local-Aware Component Stitching (2 edges/component on Zcorr)\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, pca60, combat, residualization, balanced-knn, stitching, connectivity\"\nabstract: \"Embedding: PCA(60) → ComBat on PCs (EtC). Graph: residualized PCA50 with equal-quota k=48 (cosine). Then, for each non-largest connected component in the BRBG graph, add 2 undirected 'stitch' edges to the nearest nodes in the largest component using distances in Zcorr (cosine). Aim: raise Graph_conn with negligible impact on ARI/NMI.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy.sparse.csgraph import connected_components\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n\
    \      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n\
    \      n = Z.shape[0]\n      k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n      pairs_min_dist = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0:\n              continue\n          k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n          neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n          for i in range(n):\n              g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n              mask = (g != i)\n              g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  if i == j:\n                      continue\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                  if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                      pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\
    \      from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n      if not pairs_min_dist:\n          return None, None\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n          rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n      D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\n  def _component_stitch(Zcorr, C, D, k_edges=2, metric='cosine', seed=0):\n      \"\"\"\n      For each non-largest connected component in C, add up to k_edges undirected edges\n      to the nearest nodes in the largest component, using distances from Zcorr (cosine).\n      \"\"\"\n      n_comp, labels = connected_components(C, directed=False, connection='weak')\n      if n_comp <= 1:\n          return C, D  # already connected\n\n      sizes = np.bincount(labels, minlength=n_comp)\n      largest = np.argmax(sizes)\n      idx_L = np.where(labels == largest)[0]\n      if idx_L.size == 0:\n \
    \         return C, D\n\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=1, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n      nn.fit(Zcorr[idx_L])\n\n      C_lil = C.tolil(copy=True)\n      D_lil = D.tolil(copy=True)\n\n      for c_id in range(n_comp):\n          if c_id == largest:\n              continue\n          idx_S = np.where(labels == c_id)[0]\n          if idx_S.size == 0:\n              continue\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Zcorr[idx_S], n_neighbors=1, return_distance=True)\n          candidates = []\n          for ii in range(idx_S.size):\n              i = int(idx_S[ii])\n              j = int(idx_L[inds[ii, 0]])\n              d = float(dists[ii, 0])\n              if C_lil[i, j] != 0:\n                  continue\n              candidates.append((d, i, j))\n          if not candidates:\n              continue\n          candidates.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n          taken = 0\n          used_i = set()\n          for d, i, j in candidates:\n              if i in used_i:\n      \
    \            continue\n              C_lil[i, j] = 1.0\n              C_lil[j, i] = 1.0\n              D_lil[i, j] = d\n              D_lil[j, i] = d\n              used_i.add(i)\n              taken += 1\n              if taken >= k_edges:\n                  break\n\n      return C_lil.tocsr(), D_lil.tocsr()\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n      eps = 1e-8\n      k_stitch = 2\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \n      # Embedding path: PCA(60) on HVGs → ComBat on PCs (EtC)\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → balanced kNN\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + eps\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\
    \      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          Cg, Dg = _component_stitch(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), Cg, Dg, k_edges=k_stitch, metric=metric, seed=random_state)\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Navigating submissions and reviews**\n\nI'm currently in the Token Management Room, where my attempts to 'review' and 'submit' aren't recognized. I need to switch to the Research Counter to review evaluation 432, which is related to Daedalus II's submission. However, I mistakenly attempted to review it earlier. I intended to submit my new work, \"EtC-BRBG + Local-Aware Component Stitching,\" but that wasn’t allowed here. I need to go to the Research Counter to resubmit my code and check evaluation 432 later. I'll ensure my code uses only the allowed libraries.**Managing token usage and submissions**\n\nI need to keep tabs on token usage, which stands at 126,762 out of 270k, around 47%. My plan is to head to the Research Counter first. I'll resubmit the new variant code since my last attempt didn’t go through. After that, I can review evaluation 432, which belongs to Daedalus, but it’s still possible to read those evaluations. \n\nI’ll make sure to replicate the necessary\
  \ code in the Research Counter and submit it properly. The execution steps will be: \n\n- Go to Research Counter\n- Review 432\n- Submit the new code with the correct submission ID.**Verifying component stitching steps**\n\nI need to double-check our earlier work on \"component stitching.\" We previously had EIDs 414 and 415 for 1 edge, and now we’re proposing 2 edges per non-largest component. The previous attempt added edges using Zcorr with the nearest in the largest component, but I need to ensure that the neighbors use a 'cosine' metric with sklearn NearestNeighbors. The graph's path uses equal quotas, which is good for balanced connectivity.\n\nNow, I’ll outline our actions succinctly, as the system expects commands and code without extra details: we are migrating to research, and I won't add unnecessary text. Let’s get straight to the steps!**Handling YAML strings and special characters**\n\nI need to ensure that YAML strings quote special characters properly. The title, \"EtC-BRBG\
  \ + Local-Aware Component Stitching (2 edges/component on Zcorr),\" has a slash but is safe. There isn't a colon present here, so we’re good. \n\nHowever, the 'abstract' contains a colon in \"Aim:\", which means I must quote this string to prevent issues. The 'title' itself doesn’t have a colon, and the 'tags' field is fine. To be safe, I'll quote the 'abstract' while keeping the others as they are. Good to go!**Preparing final actions for submission**\n\nEarlier, we used triple code fences, which fit under the content block, so that's good. Now, I’m considering whether to review evaluations 430 and 431. Since we already have their results, it seems unnecessary. \n\nFor the final steps: \n\n- First, I’ll execute the action to go to research.\n- Then, I’ll include the review of evaluation 432 for comparison, even though we tried that earlier.\n- Finally, I’ll submit with the YAML for the Local-Aware Component Stitching code. I’ll make sure to include the abstract with quotes. Let's move\
