- text: "/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log_addendum_ccr.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Addendum: Cluster-Conditional Residualization (CCR) for BRBG — Results\n\n  Baseline (EtC-BRBG): ≈0.7326–0.7328 (PCA60 → ComBat PCs; graph: residualized PC50, γ_max=0.74, λ_R2=0.9; k=48).\n\n  CCR idea: Fit batch residuals per cluster in graph PC space (Zg), then build equal-quota kNN.\n  - Steps: MiniBatchKMeans (n_clusters) → ridge(Zc ~ Bc) → per-PC R²_c → γ_jc = min(gamma_max, λ·R²_jc) → Zcorr_c = Zc − γ⊙Zhat_c → balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary).\n\n  Results:\n  - EID 442 (n_clusters=64, γ_max=0.6, λ=0.9): 0.7244\n    Metrics: ARI 0.719 | NMI 0.670 | ASW_batch 0.681 | iLISI 0.935 | kBET 0.780 | Graph_conn 0.958 | cLISI 0.963 | PCR 1.000 | Cell_cycle 0.319\n    Diagnosis: Graph mixing and connectivity are fine, but ARI/NMI drop markedly → over-residualization of cluster-specific biology.\n  - EID 445 (n_clusters=48, γ_max=0.5, λ=0.9): pending\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - CCR degrades global\
    \ label structure despite decent batch mixing/connectivity. If EID 445 remains below baseline, close the CCR line.\n  - We retain frozen EtC-BRBG defaults and document CCR as a negative result.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum: Cluster-Conditional Residualization (CCR) for the BRBG graph\n\n  We tested CCR (per-cluster ridge vs batch with γ_jc ∝ R²_jc) before balanced kNN:\n  - EID 442 (n_clusters=64, γ_max=0.6, λ=0.9) = 0.7244\n    • ARI 0.719, NMI 0.670, ASW_batch 0.681, iLISI 0.935, kBET 0.780, Graph_conn 0.958.\n    • Interpretation: mixing/connectivity OK, but ARI/NMI drop → cluster-local over-residualization of biology.\n  - EID 445 (n_clusters=48, γ_max=0.5) pending.\n\n  Unless 445 reverses the trend, CCR is a negative line. We keep EtC-BRBG defaults (≈0.7328) and close CCR if further runs stay below baseline.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{review 445}"
