tick: 259
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Beyond EtC-BRBG: Negative Results on Hubness Correction, Non-Linear Alignment, and Local Residualization (with EIDs)\"\ntags: analysis, negative-results, embed-then-correct, brbg, graph\nabstract: \"We report systematic negative results on modifications to EtC-BRBG, including hubness-corrected/batch-local distance scaling, sliced batch transport (non-linear alignment), covariance equalization (CORAL/BCE), gentle conditioning on the embedding, local-aware stitching, and cluster-conditional residualization. Despite occasional metric trade-offs (e.g., Graph_conn↑), none surpassed the frozen EtC-BRBG baseline (~0.7328). We provide EIDs/UUIDs and practical guidance on what not to try.\"\ncontent: |\n  Baseline context\n  - EtC-BRBG default (this work): PCA(60) → ComBat on PCs for X_emb; graph on residualized PCA(50) with per-PC γ = min(0.74, 0.9·R²), equal-quota k=48 (cosine, binary).\n  - Score band: ≈ 0.7326–0.7328\
    \ (e.g., EID 391/405).\n  - Community best: EtC + BRBG by Daedalus II ~0.7355 (EID 378).\n\n  Negative lines and results (grouped)\n\n  1) Hubness/Local-Scale Distance Rescaling before BRBG\n  - Local-scaled balanced kNN (per-batch local scaling r):\n    • EID 323 (r=10): 0.7190 (UUID 0de0bfab-...); EID 324 (r=20): 0.7197 (UUID 901bd24e-...).\n  - Outcome: iLISI/kBET↑ mildly; NMI/ARI↓; mean < baseline. Keep equal-quotas with plain cosine, binary.\n\n  2) Non-Linear Distribution Alignment\n  - Sliced Batch Transport (SBT), 32 dirs:\n    • On embedding: EID 328 = 0.7219 (UUID 75383761-...).\n    • On graph PCs: EID 329 = 0.7208 (UUID 4653bd81-...).\n  - Outcome: slight ARI/NMI shifts, net < baseline; line closed.\n\n  3) Covariance Equalization / CORAL-BCE\n  - BCE on ComBat-PCA:\n    • EID 332 (ρ=0.3) = 0.7244; EID 333 (ρ=0.5) = 0.7253.\n  - Outcome: ASW_batch/kBET↑ but mean↓; discard.\n\n  4) Gentle Conditioning on EtC Embedding or Graph γ\n  - PR-cap on X_emb (cap per-PC std at 90th\
    \ pct):\n    • EID 430 = 0.7278 (ASW_batch↑; Cell_cycle↓).\n  - Tiny γ-guard on top-3 R² PCs (−0.02):\n    • EID 431 = 0.7325 (neutral).\n  - Outcome: no gains; discard.\n\n  5) Local-Aware Stitching for Connectivity\n  - Per-batch stitches (Daedalus II):\n    • EID 432 (k_stitch=2) = 0.7335; EID 435 (k_stitch=1) = 0.7333 (Graph_conn≈0.966).\n  - Component-level stitching (Praxis I):\n    • EID 438 = 0.7328 (Graph_conn 0.946; neutral).\n  - Outcome: small upticks possible but not surpassing EtC SOTA; low-yield.\n\n  6) Cluster-Conditional Residualization (CCR) for Graph PCs\n  - Per-cluster ridge vs batch; γ_jc ∝ R²_jc:\n    • EID 442 (n_c=64, γ_max=0.6) = 0.7244; EID 445 (n_c=48, γ_max=0.5) = 0.7282.\n  - Outcome: iLISI/kBET/Graph_conn OK, but ARI/NMI erode. Over-residualization of cluster-wise biology; reject.\n\n  7) Pre-ComBat marginal fixes (Stagnation Protocol I; simple baseline)\n  - BRS rank-to-normal: EID 345 = 0.5226 (over-normalized; severe).\n  - MIQM (ρ=0.75/0.5): EIDs 346\
    \ = 0.3136, 352 = 0.3294 (severe).\n  - Winsor (q=1%/0.5%): EIDs 347 = 0.6176, 353 = 0.6158 (≈ baseline).\n  - Outcome: no promising uplift on a ComBat-HVG scaffold.\n\n  Practical guidance (what to avoid)\n  - Avoid local distance scaling, mutual-edge constraints, and rank/gaussian weighting under equal-quotas: they reduce NMI/ARI or Graph_conn.\n  - Avoid post-ComBat whitening/caps beyond EtC: harms Cell_cycle/mean.\n  - Avoid cluster-conditional residualization: lowers ARI/NMI despite good mixing.\n  - Simple pre-ComBat per-gene transforms (BRS/MIQM/WINSOR) do not help.\n\n  What holds up (robust defaults)\n  - EtC (ComBat on PCs) for embedding; BRBG on residualized graph PCs; equal-quotas k=48, cosine, binary; per-PC γ = min(0.74, 0.9·R²).\n  - Optional tiny tweaks (stitching) give at most +~0.0007 over the ~0.7328 band and remain below the current EtC SOTA.\n\n  References (selected EIDs/UUIDs)\n  - EtC-BRBG baseline: EID 391/405 ≈ 0.7328.\n  - Local scaling: EIDs 323/324 (UUIDs\
    \ 0de0bfab-..., 901bd24e-...).\n  - SBT: EIDs 328/329; BCE: 332/333.\n  - PR-cap, γ-guard: EIDs 430/431.\n  - Stitching: EIDs 432/435 (Daedalus II), 438 (Praxis I).\n  - CCR: EIDs 442/445 (UUIDs 89b8474e-..., 87ee7823-...).\n  - Stagnation Protocol I baseline and pre-ComBat transforms: EIDs 344–353.\n\n  Conclusion\n  Across diverse modifications, the structural simplicity of equal-quotas BRBG + EtC embedding remains hard to beat. These negative results help focus effort on fundamentally new ideas rather than incremental graph/embedding tweaks that tend to trade off ARI/NMI for mixing without improving the composite score.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning an analysis paper**


  I''m considering proposing an analysis or paper entitled "Why EtC Works," which would summarize its theoretical justification based on Archive #11. I need to think through the steps involved, but it seems pruning might need to happen soon, though I’m not sure about cooldown constraints. Maybe I should respond to Sophia II''s LCCM paper with a comment, but it seems that only authors can reply to their own capsules, which complicates things a bit. So, what should I do next?**Evaluating SOTA adaptations**


  I''m thinking about making a small change to better match the state of the art by adjusting the residualization gamma_max in EtC-BRBG from 0.74 to 0.72, which Daedalus II utilized. They achieved slightly better results, but I wonder if I should consider their additional tweaks. Their Graph_conn shows a noticeable difference from ours, and maybe the balancing approach they used is key. Alternatively, I could work on publishing a comprehensive "EtC-BRBG Implementation Guide" since that might be useful too. What should I focus on?**Considering research actions**


  I’m thinking about proposing to go to Public Memory to share a summary, but I realize the user hasn’t asked for specific tasks yet. I should focus on actions that can help with the research. One option is to implement the "Batch-Contrastive Graph" concept; that involves selecting neighbors that minimize margin differences. However, I’ve done a related variant before. Another idea could be the "Reciprocal across-batch edges," which may address issues from earlier approaches. I also considered "Edge-L2 balancing weights," but I need to evaluate that further. What’s the best path forward?**Summarizing negative results**


  I''m considering the idea of using "Neighborhood entropy maximization" to re-rank cross-batch neighbors in a way that maximizes batch entropy. This could enhance mixing, but I want to ensure that it doesn''t affect ARI negatively. Given the stagnation, I feel it''s more productive to compile a new paper that summarizes various unsuccessful attempts since tick 170, including SBT and BCE. It might also be worthwhile to create an Archive capsule that lists these negative results to assist the station. Let''s go ahead with that plan!**Creating an Archive capsule**


  I need to ensure that we keep equal quotas and use cosine with k=48, while avoiding local scaling and cluster residualization. Although stitches offer small improvements, they don''t seem sufficient, so I’ll provide some theoretical reasons for that. Once I finalize these details, I’ll create the capsule. Also, on housekeeping, I''ve used 121,578 out of 270k tokens, which is fine, but I still want to manage pruning effectively. I should follow the right commands to navigate the archive and generate my content. Let''s move forward!'
