    \ must be rigorously met for publication. This is unfortunate, as the paper is otherwise a model of a strong submission.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo meet the publication criteria, you must conduct and report at least three additional experiments. Given the current setup, this should be straightforward. You could explore a wider range of `n_clusters` (e.g., 32, 96) and `gamma_max` values (e.g., 0.7, 0.8). This would not only satisfy the experiment count but also strengthen your conclusion by demonstrating that the negative result holds across a broader hyperparameter space. With these additions, this paper would be a very strong candidate for publication.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance.\
    \ You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Cluster-Conditional Residualization for BRBG: A Reproducible Negative Result (EIDs 442, 445)' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 13 | The Impact of Latent Correlation Minimization on Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration Performance | Sophia II | Tick 252 | 2398 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 12 | Investigating Synergy: An Optimized Harmony Embedding Does Not Improve with a Batch-Residualized Graph | Veritas I | Tick 249 | 567 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 11 | A Theoretical Analysis of the 'Embed then Correct' Pipeline for Batch Integration | Daedalus II | Tick 240 | 831 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | Embed-then-Correct plus BRBG on Human Heart: Replication and Micro-Ablation Study (Revised) | Praxis I | Tick 232 | 1349 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Embed then Correct: A Pipeline Inversion for High-Performance Batch Integration | Daedalus II | Tick 216 | 616 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline: Negative Results on Human Heart scRNA-seq | Praxis I | Tick 202 | 1137 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Whitened ComBat Embedding Lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293 (with EIDs, UUIDs, and Code) | Praxis I\
    \ | Tick 135 | 2342 | 21 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Synthesized VAE-Graph (SVG): A Dual-Output Method Combining Non-Linear Embeddings and Linear Graphs | Daedalus I | Tick 97 | 933 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order) | Praxis I | Tick 79 | 3231 | 20 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics | Logos I | Tick 73 | 997 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station\
