tick: 261
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC-BRBG-CCR: n_clusters=64, gamma_max=0.7 (k=48)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, clustering, balanced-knn, brbg\"\nabstract: \"CCR ablation 1: Keep clusters at 64 but increase gamma_max to 0.7 to test robustness of negative results. Embed: PCA(60) → ComBat on PCs. Graph: PCA(50) → cluster-conditional residualization vs batch → equal-quota kNN (k=48, cosine).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.graph_ccr import build_ccr_graph\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd\
    \ = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      n_clusters = 64\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.7\n      lam_r2 = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding path: PCA(60) → ComBat on PC scores (EtC)\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb,\
    \ use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: PCA(50) → CCR → balanced kNN\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n\n      Zcorr, Cg, Dg = build_ccr_graph(Zg, batches, n_clusters=n_clusters, l2=l2,\n                                      gamma_max=gamma_max, lam_r2=lam_r2,\n                                      k_total=k_total, metric=metric, random_state=random_state)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC-BRBG-CCR:\
    \ n_clusters=64, gamma_max=0.8 (k=48)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, clustering, balanced-knn, brbg\"\nabstract: \"CCR ablation 2: Keep clusters at 64 but increase gamma_max to 0.8. Embed: PCA(60) → ComBat on PCs. Graph: PCA(50) → cluster-conditional residualization vs batch → equal-quota kNN (k=48, cosine).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.graph_ccr import build_ccr_graph\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n\
    \      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      n_clusters = 64\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.8\n      lam_r2 = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding path: PCA(60) → ComBat on PC scores (EtC)\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n\
    \      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: PCA(50) → CCR → balanced kNN\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n\n      Zcorr, Cg, Dg = build_ccr_graph(Zg, batches, n_clusters=n_clusters, l2=l2,\n                                      gamma_max=gamma_max, lam_r2=lam_r2,\n                                      k_total=k_total, metric=metric, random_state=random_state)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiments**\n\nI’m thinking about how we need to respond from the Archive Room regarding the reviewer feedback. They asked for more experiments, specifically three more around CCR parameters, namely n_clusters and gamma_max. We have room in our token budget, so that’s good! I’ll outline plans for four experiments, considering the reviewer’s suggestions. \n\nWe should ensure reproducibility and include EIDs and results before revising the paper. The aim is to meet the five-experiment threshold.**Planning additional experiments**\n\nI need to ensure we have five experiments for the proposed method. We already have two, so I'll add three more to meet that requirement. The recommended values include both gamma 0.7 and 0.8, so I’m thinking of choosing experiments like (64, 0.7), (64, 0.8), and (32, 0.5). This combination covers the necessary parameters. Plus, if we can run four, we should add (96, 0.5) as well. However, I need to keep in mind that we can only run\
  \ two evaluations at a time.**Coordinating experiment submissions**\n\nI can submit two experiments this tick and wait for the results before proceeding with the next ones. The process allows for multi-turn submissions, which is fine. I’ll head to the Research Counter from the Archive Room to submit two CCR variants. \n\nThe first variant will be n_clusters=64, gamma_max=0.7, and the second will be n_clusters=64, gamma_max=0.8. After these results, I’ll submit the remaining two with parameters of n_clusters=32, gamma_max=0.5, and n_clusters=96, gamma_max=0.5. Meanwhile, I can also start preparing the revised paper content structure for updates!**Implementing actions**\n\nI'm ready to implement the necessary actions. First, I'll execute the action to go to the Research Counter. \n\nNext, I’ll submit the two experiments for gamma values of 0.7 and 0.8, using the same submission code as before but with the adjusted parameters. \n\nI also think it might be a good idea to add a research log\
  \ entry for tracking purposes. I'll make sure to keep the code content minimal to stay within the token budget while crafting the necessary code blocks. Let's get these actions done!"
