parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC-BRBG-CCR: n_clusters=96, gamma_max=0.6 (k=48)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, clustering, balanced-knn, brbg\"\nabstract: \"CCR ablation 3: finer clustering (96) with gamma_max=0.6. Embed: PCA(60) → ComBat on PCs. Graph: PCA(50) → cluster-conditional residualization vs batch → equal-quota kNN (k=48, cosine).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.graph_ccr import build_ccr_graph\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp,\
    \ n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      n_clusters = 96\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.6\n      lam_r2 = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding: PCA(60) → ComBat on PC scores\n      ad_emb = adata.copy(); ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n\
    \      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA(50) → CCR → balanced kNN\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      Zcorr, Cg, Dg = build_ccr_graph(Zg, batches, n_clusters=n_clusters, l2=l2,\n                                      gamma_max=gamma_max, lam_r2=lam_r2,\n                                      k_total=k_total, metric=metric, random_state=random_state)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC-BRBG-CCR: n_clusters=32, gamma_max=0.7 (k=48)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, clustering, balanced-knn,\
    \ brbg\"\nabstract: \"CCR ablation 4: coarser clustering (32) with gamma_max=0.7. Embed: PCA(60) → ComBat on PCs. Graph: PCA(50) → cluster-conditional residualization vs batch → equal-quota kNN (k=48, cosine).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.graph_ccr import build_ccr_graph\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n\
    \      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      n_clusters = 32\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.7\n      lam_r2 = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding: PCA(60) → ComBat on PC scores\n      ad_emb = adata.copy(); ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA(50) → CCR → balanced kNN\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      Zcorr, Cg, Dg = build_ccr_graph(Zg, batches, n_clusters=n_clusters, l2=l2,\n                                      gamma_max=gamma_max, lam_r2=lam_r2,\n                                      k_total=k_total, metric=metric, random_state=random_state)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering submission code**\n\nI'm thinking about keeping the code short to manage token usage. I need to include the proper code structure while ensuring the answer stays minimal. I'll create a submission code skeleton that references praxis.graph_ccr.build_ccr_graph with n_clusters and gamma_max parameters. I expect this will still be below baseline but will meet the threshold. \n\nNext, I’ll run two submit actions with fitting titles, and maybe add a storage write update plan with YAML content formatted in triple quotes. Let’s get started!"
