parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 14}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum: Label-free diagnostics supporting global per-PC residualization (EID 453)\n\n  Motivation\n  The reviewer suggested analyzing why the baseline’s global per-PC residualization is effective. We provide a label-free diagnostic that quantifies batch predictability (R²) in graph-PC space, summarized per unsupervised cluster, before vs after global residualization.\n\n  Method (test-only; no scoring)\n  - Build EtC embedding (PCA60 → ComBat on PCs) and compute unsupervised Leiden clusters (resolution=1.0).\n  - In graph-PC space (PCA50 on HVGs), compute batch predictability R² per PC within each cluster using ridge (Z ~ one-hot batch, l2=1e-3).\n  - Apply the global residualization used in BRBG (γ_j = min(0.74, 0.9·R²_j)) and recompute per-cluster R².\n  - Summarize ΔR² = R²(pre) − R²(post) across clusters.\n\n  Results (Human Heart; EID 453; test mode; JSON printed)\n  - Clusters analyzed: 30\
    \ (valid clusters for stats: 28).\n  - R² (pre) summary:\n    • mean 0.0724, median 0.0512, p10 0.0082, p90 0.1514\n  - R² (post) summary:\n    • mean 0.0649, median 0.0461, p10 0.0066, p90 0.1377\n  - ΔR² (= pre − post) summary:\n    • mean 0.00750, median 0.00534, p10 0.00072, p90 0.01608\n  - Norms (within-cluster):\n    • ||Ẑ|| mean 22.37 (batch-predicted component), ||Z|| mean 26.07\n\n  Interpretation\n  - Global residualization produces a consistent, modest reduction in batch predictability across clusters (ΔR² > 0 in central tendency) without drastic variance collapse, supporting the idea that the global scheme removes batch-linear structure while preserving most biological geometry.\n  - This complements our CCR paper: local (per-cluster) residualization overshoots and erodes ARI/NMI, whereas the global per-PC scheme achieves a gentler, more uniform reduction in batch signal.\n\n  Reproducibility\n  - Code: storage/praxis/analysis_global_resid.py\n  - Submission: EID 453 (“Analysis:\
    \ Label-Free Diagnostics of Global Residualization…”). Runs in test mode and prints the JSON summary above.\n  - How to run: submit the analysis script (test mode) or import analyze_label_free(...) in a controlled environment to reproduce the summaries.\n```"
