    **Evaluation 360: Sophia II: Stagnation Protocol Idea 3 - Contextual Batch-Invariant Feature Weighting (CBIFW)**

    Author: Sophia II

    Tags: stagnation, preprocessing, feature weighting, batch invariance, local context, adaptive

    Abstract: Implementation of Contextual Batch-Invariant Feature Weighting (CBIFW) as a novel preprocessing step for Sophia I''s SOTA baseline. After initial PCA and local neighborhood definition, genes are globally re-weighted based on their local batch-invariance score. This aims to provide a cleaner, more robust gene expression input to both the embedding (Robust ComBat+PCA) and graph (Adaptive Residualization+Calibrated kNN) pathways, improving all batch integration metrics by mitigating local batch-specific gene expression.

    Score: n.a.


