tick: 272
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I. Location: Token Management Room. Recap: I consolidated EtC-BRBG at ~0.7326–0.7328; CCR (cluster-conditional residualization) consistently underperformed (Archive #14). Gentle gamma_max=0.72 was neutral; component stitching neutral; local-scaling, SBT, BCE/whitening tweaks, and various graph augmentations were neutral-to-negative. Recent archives: Veritas I reported no synergy between Harmony and BRBG (#12); Sophia II found latent correlation minimization harms local mixing (#13). SOTA for EtC remains ~0.7355 (Daedalus II), replicated ~0.7347–0.7353.\n\nReflection: We are at a robust plateau: embedding-side linear ComBat in PCA space plus balanced-quotas graph from residualized PCs is strong; most extra conditioning either reintroduces magnitude bias (hurting iLISI/kBET) or shaves biology (ARI/NMI). My takeaway: breakthroughs will likely come from (a) rethinking neighborhood construction without sacrificing quotas, or (b) a new embedding objective that explicitly\
    \ balances cross-batch alignment and intra-batch geometry with a label-free stop criterion. Recent negatives in SBT/BCE/LCCM suggest that naive post-hoc alignment of latent correlations hurts fine local structure. I will (1) read the two new archives fully to harvest formal arguments/diagnostics, then (2) do a short reflection to propose three fresh, minimal-parameter ideas that are genuinely distinct from prior lines, and only then consider targeted experiments.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{read 12,13}\n\n/execute_action{goto reflect}\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  Based on full readings of #12 (Harmony+BRBG synergy: negative) and #13 (LCCM: negative), propose three distinct, minimal-parameter ideas that are not variants we've already tried (no SBT/BCE/gamma tweaks/CCR/stitching/local scaling/whitening/PBVE).\n  Constraints: simple, dataset-agnostic, label-free w.r.t biology (batch labels allowed), and compatible with EtC-BRBG separation\
    \ of concerns.\n  Draft ideas to vet:\n  1) Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG): After equal-quotas balanced kNN on Zcorr, perform block-wise Sinkhorn scaling to equalize cross-batch mass per node (soft reweighting) but then binarize at a fixed per-node threshold to preserve degree and avoid magnitude bias. Goal: tame over-represented cross-batch links without changing quotas or distances. One knob: iteration cap or epsilon; plan to default to a single pass + binarize.\n  2) Dual-Temperature Neighbors (DTN): Build two balanced graphs on Zcorr with cosine at (a) normal scale and (b) slightly “sharpened” scale via cosine^τ (τ∈{0.9,1.1}); fuse by union with degree cap to preserve k_total. Hypothesis: captures both coarse and fine local alignments without weights. One knob: τ; default 1.1. Binarized union keeps structure dominant.\n  3) Batch-Mean Centered PCA for Graph PCs (BM-PCA): Before PCA(50) for graph PCs, center each batch by its gene-wise mean in the normalized/log1p HVG matrix\
    \ (not ComBat; just centering), then PCA → residualization → balanced graph. Rationale: remove per-gene mean batch shifts upstream of PCA to improve downstream adaptive residualization’s effectiveness without affecting X_emb. Knobs: none beyond standard PCA dims.\n  For each: anticipate metric movements (iLISI/kBET/Graph_conn vs ARI/NMI/cLISI), risks, and go/no-go criteria. Also outline tiny ablation (at most one scalar) and rollback rules.\ntick: 5\n```"
