tick: 272
role: user
parts:
- text: 'Based on full readings of #12 (Harmony+BRBG synergy: negative) and #13 (LCCM: negative), propose three distinct, minimal-parameter ideas that are not variants we''ve already tried (no SBT/BCE/gamma tweaks/CCR/stitching/local scaling/whitening/PBVE).

    Constraints: simple, dataset-agnostic, label-free w.r.t biology (batch labels allowed), and compatible with EtC-BRBG separation of concerns.

    Draft ideas to vet:

    1) Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG): After equal-quotas balanced kNN on Zcorr, perform block-wise Sinkhorn scaling to equalize cross-batch mass per node (soft reweighting) but then binarize at a fixed per-node threshold to preserve degree and avoid magnitude bias. Goal: tame over-represented cross-batch links without changing quotas or distances. One knob: iteration cap or epsilon; plan to default to a single pass + binarize.

    2) Dual-Temperature Neighbors (DTN): Build two balanced graphs on Zcorr with cosine at (a) normal scale and (b) slightly “sharpened” scale via cosine^τ (τ∈{0.9,1.1}); fuse by union with degree cap to preserve k_total. Hypothesis: captures both coarse and fine local alignments without weights. One knob: τ; default 1.1. Binarized union keeps structure dominant.

    3) Batch-Mean Centered PCA for Graph PCs (BM-PCA): Before PCA(50) for graph PCs, center each batch by its gene-wise mean in the normalized/log1p HVG matrix (not ComBat; just centering), then PCA → residualization → balanced graph. Rationale: remove per-gene mean batch shifts upstream of PCA to improve downstream adaptive residualization’s effectiveness without affecting X_emb. Knobs: none beyond standard PCA dims.

    For each: anticipate metric movements (iLISI/kBET/Graph_conn vs ARI/NMI/cLISI), risks, and go/no-go criteria. Also outline tiny ablation (at most one scalar) and rollback rules.



    **Reflection Tick 1 / 5**'
