role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I. Location: Reflection Chamber. Recap: EtC-BRBG is robust at ~0.7326–0.7328; many conditioning and graph tweaks were neutral/negative. New archives #12 and #13 reinforce that naïve latent post-processing harms local mixing or shows no synergy. I’m refining three minimal, label-free ideas compatible with EtC-BRBG.\n\nIdea 1 — Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG)\n- Mechanism:\n  - Start from the standard equal-quotas balanced kNN on Zcorr (rows balanced).\n  - For each batch b, lightly column-balance the adjacency block A_b so targets in batch b share inbound degree more evenly (reduce hubs).\n  - Then reselect per-row top k_per_batch edges by scaled scores and binarize; union across batches; symmetrize; distances remain original.\n- Expected metric effects:\n  - iLISI/kBET: up or ≈ (hubness↓, more even cross-batch distribution).\n  - Graph_conn: ≈ (degree preserved).\n  - ARI/NMI/cLISI: ≈ (still nearest edges; no weights at evaluation).\n- Risk/mitigation:\n  -\
    \ Over-balancing can drop genuinely closest targets → ARI/NMI↓. Use a single light column step; never force columns above a percentile cap.\n- One knob + defaults:\n  - Column target dampening α ∈ {1.0 (default), 0.8}. Single pass; no row reweight beyond per-row top-k rebinarization.\n- Diagnostics (label-free):\n  - In-degree CV per batch block (expect ↓), per-node cross-batch fraction (≈ stable), degree ~k_total.\n\nIdea 2 — Dual-Temperature Neighbors (DTN)\n- Mechanism:\n  - Build G0 with standard cosine; build Gτ with “sharpened” angular ordering via (1−cos)^τ (τ>1 makes closer neighbors rank even higher).\n  - Node-wise union of edges; if degree exceeds k_total, keep k_total smallest original cosine distances; binarize.\n- Expected metric effects:\n  - iLISI/kBET: mild ↑ (captures complementary neighbors).\n  - Graph_conn: ≈; ARI/NMI: ≈ (truncate by nearest distances).\n- Risk/mitigation:\n  - If union admits too many mid-distance edges, truncation might drop a few very close ones;\
    \ keep τ close to 1 and use original distances for truncation.\n- One knob + defaults:\n  - τ ∈ {1.05, 1.1}; default 1.1.\n- Diagnostics:\n  - Overlap between G0 and Gτ (Jaccard per node), degree distribution, iLISI versus baseline.\n\nIdea 3 — Batch-Mean Centered PCA for Graph PCs (BM-PCA)\n- Mechanism:\n  - Before PCA(50) on HVGs for graph path only, subtract per-batch gene means from normalized/log1p X (HVGs).\n  - Then PCA → adaptive residualization (γ_max=0.74, λ_R2=0.9) → balanced kNN.\n  - Embedding (EtC) unchanged; separation of concerns intact.\n- Expected metric effects:\n  - ASW_batch/iLISI/kBET: ↑ or ≈ (location shifts removed upstream).\n  - ARI/NMI: ≈ (affine centering preserves within-batch ranks); Graph_conn: ≈.\n- Risk/mitigation:\n  - If true biology appears as mean shifts, slight ARI/NMI ↓; introduce gentle blend λ_c ∈ {1.0, 0.8} (default 1.0).\n- Diagnostics:\n  - Per-gene across-batch mean variance ↓; PC-wise batch R² before/after; PR and anisotropy stable.\n\nExecution\
    \ plan and guardrails\n- Order (cheapest to test, least invasive first): DTN (τ=1.1) → BBSG (α=1.0) → BM-PCA (λ_c=1.0). Keep EtC embedding fixed; only modify graph pipeline on Zcorr or pre-PCA input.\n- Acceptance (vs EtC-BRBG baseline):\n  - Mean ≥ +0.002, ARI/NMI drop ≤ 0.003, Graph_conn ≥ 0.94, iLISI not worse.\n- Rollback:\n  - If any idea fails by ≥ −0.005 mean or hurts ARI/NMI beyond thresholds, stop its ablation (no second setting).\n- If one passes, confirm at k=45 (ridge check) and document with full EIDs/UUIDs."
