tick: 272
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I. Location: Reflection Chamber. Recap: EtC-BRBG baseline is robust (~0.7326–0.7328). Many graph/embedding tweaks (local scaling, SBT, BCE/whitening variants, stitching, CCR, γ tweaks) were neutral or negative. Archives #12 (Harmony+BRBG: no synergy) and #13 (LCCM: decorrelation hurts local mixing) argue against heavy post-hoc latent manipulation. I’m finalizing three minimal, label-free ideas that respect EtC-BRBG’s separation of concerns: BBSG, DTN, and BM-PCA.\n\nFeasibility, pseudocode, complexity, pitfalls, and validation\n\n1) Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG)\n- Feasibility: Works entirely on the already-built equal-quotas graph blocks; single pass; keeps edge count and quotas; no labels beyond batch.\n- Pseudocode (per batch block A_b ∈ {0,1} with rows = all queries, cols = nodes in b):\n  - c = colsum(A_b); nR, nC = A_b.shape\n  - t_base = k_per_batch * nR / nC\n  - t = α * t_base + (1−α) * median(c)  # α ∈ {1.0 default, 0.8}\n  - s_j = min(cap, t /\
    \ max(c_j, 1))  # cap ≈ 2.0 to avoid extreme corrections\n  - For each row i: score_j = s_j if A_b[i,j]==1 else 0; keep top k_per_batch by score_j; set those to 1, others 0.\n  - Union across batches; symmetrize; connectivities = binary; distances = original cosine distances for kept edges (no weight carry-over).\n- Complexity: O(E) to compute c; row-wise top-k on ≤k_per_batch entries per batch block is O(nR * k_per_batch log k_per_batch), trivial at k_per_batch≈12 (for 4 batches, k_total=48).\n- Pitfalls:\n  - If s_j over-penalizes genuine nearest hubs, ARI/NMI could dip; α=1.0+cap=2.0 with one pass minimizes this risk.\n  - Do not reweight edges in obsp; re-binarize only.\n- Diagnostics:\n  - In-degree CV within each A_b before/after (expect ↓).\n  - Degree per node ~ k_total (± overlaps), cross-batch fraction ~ (B−1)/B.\n- Expected metrics: iLISI/kBET ↑ or ≈; Graph_conn ≈; ARI/NMI ≈. Go/no-go: mean ≥ +0.002, ARI/NMI drop ≤ 0.003, Graph_conn ≥ 0.94, iLISI not worse.\n\n2) Dual-Temperature\
    \ Neighbors (DTN)\n- Feasibility: Reuses balanced-kNN builder twice with a monotone angular transform; union and cap back to k_total; preserves binary structure and quotas.\n- Pseudocode:\n  - Build G0 on Zcorr with cosine distance d0 = 1−cos.\n  - Build Gτ with dτ = (1−cos)^τ (τ ∈ {1.05, 1.1}, default 1.1); same quotas per batch.\n  - For each node i: E = neighbors from G0 ∪ Gτ; if |E| > k_total, select k_total edges with smallest original d0 (protect standard nearest).\n  - Symmetrize; connectivities = binary; distances = d0 of selected edges (or min if edge from both).\n- Complexity: ~2× nearest-neighbor queries per batch; still manageable at 20k cells × 2k genes (PC50).\n- Pitfalls:\n  - If union admits too many mid-distance edges, truncation could eject a few very close ones; using d0 to cap mitigates this.\n- Diagnostics:\n  - Per-node Jaccard(G0,Gτ), fraction of novel edges kept; degree check; iLISI/kBET vs baseline.\n- Expected metrics: iLISI/kBET ↑ (slight), Graph_conn ≈, ARI/NMI\
    \ ≈. Same go/no-go thresholds.\n\n3) Batch-Mean Centered PCA for Graph PCs (BM-PCA)\n- Feasibility: Operates on normalized/log1p HVGs just before PCA for the graph path; very simple affine centering; no ComBat, so separation intact. Memory is the main consideration (dense HVG block).\n- Pseudocode:\n  - X = log1p(normalize_total(counts)); restrict to HVGs.\n  - For each batch b: μ_b = mean(X[b, :], axis=0); X[b, :] ← λ_c * (X[b, :] − μ_b) + (1−λ_c) * X[b, :]  # λ_c ∈ {1.0 default, 0.8}\n  - PCA(50) on X → Zg; adaptive residualization (γ_max=0.74, λ_R2=0.9) → Zcorr; build equal-quotas balanced kNN (k_total=48, cosine), write connectivities (binary) and distances (cosine).\n- Complexity: O(n_cells × n_HVG) to center; PCA50 cost unchanged; overall OK at 20k×2k (ensure float32).\n- Pitfalls:\n  - If true biology manifests as mean shifts, ARI/NMI can dip; λ_c=1.0 first; back off to 0.8 only if mild positive signs appear.\n- Diagnostics:\n  - Across-batch per-gene mean variance ↓; PC batch\
    \ R² ↓ without PR collapse; iLISI/kBET ≥ baseline.\n- Expected metrics: ASW_batch/iLISI/kBET ↑ or ≈; Graph_conn ≈; ARI/NMI ≈. Same go/no-go.\n\nGeneral execution and logging plan\n- Keep embedding fixed (EtC: PCA60 on HVGs → ComBat PCs → neighbors(15) for keys).\n- Graph path: always from Zcorr (or BM-PCA→Zg→Zcorr), equal quotas, k_total=48, cosine, binary. Overwrite obsp after any sc.pp.neighbors call (never call afterward).\n- Instrumentation (stdout):\n  - Config (idea + scalar α/τ/λ_c).\n  - k_total, k_per_batch; degree stats (median/5–95%); cross-batch fraction.\n  - BBSG: pre/post in-degree CV by batch block; fraction of edges changed.\n  - DTN: Jaccard per node between G0 and Gτ; fraction of union trimmed to k_total.\n  - BM-PCA: Δ var_across_batch(means), PC batch R² pre/post; PR and per-PC variance spread.\n- Acceptance/rollback:\n  - Accept idea if mean ≥ +0.002 with ARI/NMI stable (≤ 0.003 drop), iLISI not worse, Graph_conn ≥ 0.94.\n  - If first setting fails by ≥ −0.005 or\
    \ harms ARI/NMI beyond thresholds, stop that idea (no second setting).\n  - If passes, confirm robustness with a single k=45 run (ridge check).\n- Risk control:\n  - Never introduce weighted connectivities; always binarize to avoid magnitude bias (a recurring failure mode).\n  - Preserve quotas strictly; no proportional quotas or mutual-only variants (historically harmful).\n  - Keep changes localized (neighbor selection or pre-PCA centering), leaving adaptive residualization as primary variance control.\n\nIf none pass thresholds:\n- Document negatives (EIDs/UUIDs, diagnostics) and publish a brief note on “Structure-first micro-adjustments show no gain over EtC-BRBG,” helping others avoid these rabbit holes.\n- Otherwise, if one clears, integrate into the frozen EtC-BRBG baseline as an optional “+” variant and verify against EtC SOTA (~0.7355) to assess headroom."
