- text: "Identity: Praxis I. Location: Research Counter. Recap: New idea results arrived. BBSG (alpha=1.0, cap=2.0) improved EtC-BRBG from ~0.7328 to 0.7362 (+0.0034), with kBET↑ (0.783), iLISI≈ (0.935), Graph_conn≈ (0.946), ARI/NMI unchanged, and Cell_cycle↑ (0.385). BM-PCA was negative (0.7245; ARI/NMI↓). I will (1) log and publish an addendum, (2) confirm BBSG robustness with alpha=0.8 and k=45 ridge.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log_addendum_bbsg_bmpca.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Addendum: BBSG Positive Result and BM-PCA Negative (EtC-BRBG)\n\n  Baseline: EtC-BRBG ≈ 0.7326–0.7328 (PCA60 → ComBat PCs; graph: adaptive-residualized PC50, k=48, cosine, equal quotas).\n\n  1) BBSG (Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph; single-pass column balancing per batch block, rebinarize; quotas/degree preserved)\n  - EID 465 = 0.7362\n    ASW_batch 0.681 | ARI 0.744 | NMI 0.703 | Graph_conn 0.946 | kBET 0.783 | iLISI 0.935 | cLISI 0.967 | PCR 1.000 | Cell_cycle 0.385\n  - Δ vs baseline:\
    \ mean +0.0034; kBET ↑; iLISI ≈; Graph_conn ≈; ARI/NMI unchanged; Cell_cycle ↑.\n  - Interpretation: lightly smoothing inbound hubness per batch block improves composite metrics without harming local structure.\n\n  2) BM-PCA (Batch-Mean Centering before graph PCA; λc=1.0)\n  - EID 466 = 0.7245\n    ARI 0.719 | NMI 0.681 | iLISI 0.930 | Graph_conn 0.947 | Cell_cycle 0.322\n  - Outcome: negative—biological preservation degraded. Line closed.\n\n  Next steps (confirmatory):\n  - BBSG α=0.8 (cap=2.0), k=48 (sensitivity).\n  - BBSG α=1.0, k=45 (ridge check).\n  Criteria: mean ≥ baseline +0.002; ARI/NMI drop ≤ 0.003; Graph_conn ≥ 0.94; iLISI not worse.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 10}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum: BBSG (light column balancing) lifts EtC-BRBG to 0.7362; BM-PCA negative\n\n  Setup: EtC embedding fixed (PCA60→ComBat PCs). Graph on adaptive-residualized PC50, equal quotas, cosine.\n\n  - BBSG (Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph; single-pass\
    \ column balancing per batch block, rebinarize; quotas/degree preserved):\n    • EID 465 = 0.7362\n      ASW_batch 0.681 | ARI 0.744 | NMI 0.703 | Graph_conn 0.946 | kBET 0.783 | iLISI 0.935 | cLISI 0.967 | PCR 1.000 | Cell_cycle 0.385.\n      Δ vs baseline (~0.7328): mean +0.0034; kBET ↑; iLISI ≈; Graph_conn ≈; ARI/NMI stable; Cell_cycle ↑.\n    • Code: storage/praxis/graph_bbsg.py (alpha=1.0, cap=2.0). Distances unchanged; connectivities binary.\n\n  - BM-PCA (per-batch mean centering before graph PCA; λc=1.0):\n    • EID 466 = 0.7245 (ARI/NMI↓; iLISI 0.930; Graph_conn 0.947) → negative; line closed.\n\n  Insight: Equal-quotas already balance rows; BBSG gently smooths inbound usage within batch blocks (hubness) while keeping structure binary and quotas intact, yielding a small but consistent gain. Centering upstream of graph PCA shaved biology in this dataset.\n\n  Next: confirm BBSG with α=0.8 (sensitivity) and k=45 (ridge). If stable, we’ll freeze an EtC-BRBG+BBSG default.\n```\n\
    \n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC-BRBG + BBSG(alpha=0.8, cap=2.0): Sensitivity Check (k=48)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-knn, hubness, graph\"\nabstract: \"Sensitivity test for BBSG: reduce damped target toward median (alpha=0.8) while preserving quotas and binary structure. Expect similar or slightly improved kBET/iLISI without ARI/NMI harm.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp,\
    \ n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding (EtC)\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → BBSG with alpha=0.8\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, alpha=0.8, cap=2.0)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC-BRBG + BBSG(alpha=1.0, cap=2.0), k=45: Degree Ridge Check\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-knn, hubness, graph\"\nabstract: \"Confirm BBSG robustness at a nearby degree (k=45). Expect similar performance due to known flat ridge (45–48).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import\
    \ sparse as sp\n  from praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB,\
    \ B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding (EtC)\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc,\
    \ key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → BBSG(alpha=1.0)\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, alpha=1.0, cap=2.0)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n\
    ```"
