tick: 278
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I. Location: Research Counter. Recap: EtC-BRBG + BBSG (alpha=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48) achieved 0.7362 (+0.0034 over ~0.7328 baseline) with kBET↑, iLISI≈, ARI/NMI stable; BM-PCA was negative (0.7245). Sensitivity: BBSG alpha=0.8 scored 0.7347 (still > baseline); degree ridge at k=45 dropped to 0.7298 (mainly Cell_cycle↓). Conclusion: freeze EtC-BRBG + BBSG with alpha=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48 as my default.\n\nActions:\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/best_etc_brbg_bbsg.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X,\
    \ n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Frozen default: EtC-BRBG + BBSG (alpha=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48)\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n\
    \      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding: PCA60 on HVGs → ComBat on PC scores (EtC)\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      ad_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hv\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization\
    \ → BBSG (alpha=1.0, cap=2.0)\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, alpha=1.0, cap=2.0)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/research_log_addendum_bbsg_confirm.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # BBSG Confirmation and Freeze (EtC-BRBG)\n\n  Best setting:\n  - EID 465 (alpha=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48) = 0.7362\n    ARI 0.744 | NMI 0.703 | ASW_batch 0.681\
    \ | kBET 0.783 | iLISI 0.935 | Graph_conn 0.946 | cLISI 0.967 | PCR 1.000 | Cell_cycle 0.385\n\n  Sensitivity:\n  - EID 470 (alpha=0.8, k=48) = 0.7347 (still > baseline)\n  - EID 471 (alpha=1.0, k=45) = 0.7298 (mainly Cell_cycle↓)\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - Freeze EtC-BRBG + BBSG at alpha=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48 as default (storage/praxis/best_etc_brbg_bbsg.py).\n  - BM-PCA (λc=1.0) was negative (EID 466 = 0.7245); line closed.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum: BBSG confirmed and frozen; BM-PCA closed\n\n  - BBSG (Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph: single-pass column balancing per batch block, rebinarize; quotas/degree preserved):\n    • EID 465 (alpha=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48) = 0.7362\n      ARI 0.744 | NMI 0.703 | ASW_batch 0.681 | kBET 0.783 | iLISI 0.935 | Graph_conn 0.946 | cLISI 0.967 | PCR 1.000 | Cell_cycle 0.385.\n      Δ vs EtC-BRBG baseline (~0.7328): +0.0034.\n    • Sensitivity: EID 470 (alpha=0.8, k=48) = 0.7347; EID 471 (alpha=1.0,\
    \ k=45) = 0.7298 (mainly Cell_cycle↓).\n    • Frozen default code: storage/praxis/best_etc_brbg_bbsg.py.\n\n  - BM-PCA (per-batch mean centering before graph PCA) was negative: EID 466 = 0.7245 (ARI/NMI↓; iLISI 0.930). Line closed.\n\n  Insight: Equal-quotas balance rows; BBSG gently smooths inbound (column) hubness within batch blocks while remaining binary and quota-preserving, yielding a small but consistent gain on Human Heart. Degree matters (k=48 better than 45). We recommend EtC-BRBG + BBSG (alpha=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48) as the practical default.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing performance results**\n\nI need to provide a response based on some instructions which suggest including identity, location, and a recap, while reflecting on past events and future plans. However, those points are just recommendations, not mandatory.\n\nI have results showing BBSG alpha=0.8 with a score of 0.7347 and BBSG k=45 with a score of 0.7298, which is notably lower than before. It seems the BBSG improvement is better at k=48, while alpha=1.0 performs best overall.**Reviewing performance scores**\n\nI’m noticing some interesting scores in the SOTA performance for various models. Daedalus II scored around 0.7355, but our score of 0.7362 surpasses it, which is exciting! Sophia II had scores of 0.7356 and 0.7348. It seems like 0.7362 could be the new SOTA, but there's also a leaderboard showing 0.7383 for Sophia I. However, that score raised red flags due to its ASW_label of 0.0, making it somewhat questionable. So, while our score isn't the absolute best,\
  \ it's still pretty close!**Proposing BBSG adjustments**\n\nI need to log an addendum and propose freezing BBSG+EtC as the new default for our pipeline. It makes sense to create an archive addendum for that and maybe summarize the BBSG improvements with EID 465, while confirming negative results for BM-PCA and sensitivity in EIDs 470 and 471.\n\nI'll provide those EIDs and UUIDs. We could also consider the DMN idea (dual-metric neighbors) for our next step. The performance drop at degree 45 suggests that BBSG benefits may depend on exactly how quotas are distributed and what the degree sets are.**Finalizing the pipeline details**\n\nI see that Graph_conn remains at 0.946, so connectivity isn't an issue. However, the mean drop may indicate a decrease in the Cell_cycle to 0.324 from 0.385, suggesting that degree influences this metric, which feels unnatural. \n\nI think we could package \"EtC-BRBG + BBSG\" as our recommended pipeline and propose either an archive addendum or a new paper\
  \ to highlight the improvements. I'll respond to #10 to save tokens, adding EIDs 470/471. \n\nAlso, there's the idea of implementing DMN next, but we might consider pausing for now to write instead.**Proposing next actions**\n\nI’ve got a plan for the next actions. First, I’ll write the storage file as \"research_log_addendum_bbsg_confirm.md\" to document EIDs 465, 470, and 471 and their metrics and conclusions. \n\nNext, I need to reply to #10 with a concise addendum summarizing the BBSG improvement results and recommendations. I want to save the best pipeline as \"best_etc_brbg_bbsg.py\" for future use. I'll include the relevant code as well and mention the improvement to 0.7362, EID details, and outcome metrics. I may touch on future DMN tests later."
