tick: 279
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I. Location: Archive Room. Recap: EtC-BRBG + BBSG (alpha=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48) achieved 0.7362 (+0.0034 over ~0.7328 baseline), with kBET up, iLISI stable, ARI/NMI unchanged; BM-PCA was negative. Sensitivity checks: alpha=0.8 scored 0.7347 (> baseline), k=45 dropped to 0.7298 (mainly Cell_cycle). I froze the default at EtC-BRBG + BBSG (alpha=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48). I will publish a focused archive capsule documenting the method and results.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BBSG: Column-Balanced Quota Graph Improves EtC-BRBG to 0.7362 on Human Heart\"\ntags: protocol, graph, balanced-knn, embed-then-correct\nabstract: \"We introduce Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG), a single-pass, per-batch column-balancing of inbound usage on top of the equal-quotas balanced kNN graph, followed by rebinarization. BBSG preserves quotas, degree, and original distances, reducing hubness while keeping structure-first principles. On the EtC-BRBG pipeline, BBSG improves the\
    \ mean score to 0.7362 (+0.0034 over baseline), with kBET up, iLISI stable, and ARI/NMI unchanged. Sensitivity shows alpha=0.8 remains > baseline; k=45 degrades (degree matters). We provide EIDs, code paths, and a frozen default.\"\ncontent: |\n  1) Context\n  EtC-BRBG (Embed-then-Correct + Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph) is a strong baseline on Human Heart:\n  - Embedding: PCA(60) on HVGs → ComBat on PC scores (EtC).\n  - Graph: PCA(50) on HVGs → adaptive residualization (γ_max=0.74, λ_R2=0.9) → equal-quotas balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary).\n  Baseline mean ≈ 0.7326–0.7328 on our runs.\n\n  2) Method: Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG)\n  Motivation: Equal quotas enforce per-row balance (each node selects k_per_batch per batch) but can leave inbound imbalance (column hubs) within batch blocks. We smooth inbound usage lightly while preserving quotas/degree and avoiding weight bias.\n  Algorithm (single pass per batch block):\n    - Start from the standard equal-quotas graph\
    \ on Zcorr (adaptive residualized PCs).\n    - For each batch b, take the adjacency block A_b (rows: all queries; cols: targets in batch b).\n    - Compute column sums c_j and a damped target inbound t = α·(k_per_batch·n_rows/n_cols_b) + (1−α)·median(c).\n    - Column scale s_j = min(cap, t / max(c_j, 1)).\n    - For each row, reselect the top k_per_batch candidates by (s_j desc, distance asc); set those edges to 1, others 0.\n    - Union across batches; symmetrize; store original cosine distances; connectivities remain binary.\n  Defaults: α=1.0, cap=2.0; k_total=48.\n\n  3) Results (Human Heart, ~20k cells × 2k HVGs)\n  - EID 465 (α=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48): mean 0.7362\n    ASW_batch 0.681 | ASW_label 0.218 | ARI 0.744 | NMI 0.703 |\n    Graph_conn 0.946 | kBET 0.783 | iLISI 0.935 | cLISI 0.967 |\n    PCR 1.000 | Cell_cycle 0.385\n    Δ vs EtC-BRBG baseline (~0.7328): +0.0034; kBET↑; iLISI≈; ARI/NMI unchanged.\n  - Sensitivity:\n    • EID 470 (α=0.8, k=48): 0.7347 (still > baseline).\n\
    \    • EID 471 (α=1.0, k=45): 0.7298 (mainly Cell_cycle↓) → degree matters; keep k=48.\n\n  4) Negative Control\n  - BM-PCA (per-batch mean centering before graph PCA; λ_c=1.0) was negative:\n    • EID 466 = 0.7245 (ARI/NMI↓; iLISI 0.930; Graph_conn 0.947). Line closed.\n\n  5) Code Paths and Frozen Default\n  - BBSG builder: storage/praxis/graph_bbsg.py\n  - Frozen default pipeline: storage/praxis/best_etc_brbg_bbsg.py\n    Config: PCA60→ComBat PCs (embedding); graph PCA50→adaptive residualization; BBSG α=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48; cosine; binary.\n\n  6) Why BBSG Works\n  Equal-quotas balance rows but can create column hubs within batch blocks. A single light column-balancing step reduces hubness without introducing weights at evaluation or breaking quotas, maintaining structure-first (binary) graphs and preserving local geometry. The gain manifests primarily as kBET↑ while iLISI and ARI/NMI remain stable.\n\n  7) Practical Recommendation\n  For EtC-BRBG on Human Heart: adopt EtC-BRBG + BBSG\
    \ (α=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48). Avoid lowering degree to 45 (Cell_cycle↓). Future work may probe automatic α selection or per-batch block diagnostics; however, current defaults are robust and simple.\n\n  8) Reproducibility\n  - EID 465 (primary), EID 470 (α=0.8), EID 471 (k=45), EID 466 (BM-PCA negative).\n  - Full scripts and configurations available in the storage paths above; evaluations include UUID logs.\n```"
