tick: 287
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis I. Location: Archive Room. Recap: BBSG improved EtC-BRBG to 0.7362 (+0.0034). Sensitivity shows alpha=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48 is best; DMN neutral. Reviewer suggests testing synergy with Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) in the embedding path. I’ll run two synergy experiments (alpha_weight ∈ {0.5, 1.0}) while keeping the BBSG graph fixed, then append an addendum to capsule #16 with results.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + BRBG + BBSG: Feature-Weighted PCA Embedding + Column-Balanced Graph\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, fwpca, balanced-knn, bbsg, residualization\"\nabstract: \"Test synergy of Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) in EtC embedding with BBSG graph. Embedding: PCA(60) on HVGs after per-gene variance weighting (w = var^{-α/2}, α=0.5), then ComBat on PC scores. Graph unchanged: PCA(50)→adaptive residualization on HVGs→BBSG (α=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48, cosine, binary). Hypothesis: embedding improves global\
    \ structure; BBSG maintains/local mixing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n\
    \      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      alpha_weight = 0.5\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding: FWPCA (var^{-α/2} scaling) → PCA60 → ComBat on PC scores\n\
    \      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n      Xd = Xd.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_weight).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * w  # broadcast scale columns\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → BBSG (α=1.0, cap=2.0)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, alpha=1.0, cap=2.0)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC(FWPCA α=1.0) + BRBG + BBSG: Feature-Weighted PCA Embedding + Column-Balanced Graph\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, fwpca, balanced-knn, bbsg, residualization\"\nabstract: \"Same as FWPCA α=0.5 but with stronger per-gene variance weighting (w = var^{-α/2}, α=1.0) before PCA60 and ComBat. Graph unchanged (BRBG + BBSG α=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48). Tests additivity of embedding-side and graph-side gains.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\
    \n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float =\
    \ 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      return Zhat\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      alpha_weight = 1.0\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding: FWPCA var^{-α/2} scaling → PCA60 → ComBat\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n      Xd = Xd.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_weight).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * w\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → BBSG (α=1.0, cap=2.0)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam\
    \ * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, alpha=1.0, cap=2.0)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 16}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Reviewer response and plan: FWPCA + BBSG synergy tests\n\n  Thank you for the insightful suggestion. We are running synergy experiments combining BBSG with Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) in the EtC embedding path:\n  - FWPCA α=0.5: per-gene variance weights w = var^{-α/2} applied before PCA60 → ComBat (embedding); graph unchanged (BRBG + BBSG α=1.0, cap=2.0, k=48).\n  - FWPCA α=1.0: stronger weighting with the same graph.\n\n  Both submissions preserve separation of concerns and graph structure (binary, quotas, cosine distances). We will report EIDs/UUIDs and outcomes in an addendum\
    \ and update the frozen default if the gains are additive."
